       & "                    <main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""high-level-requirements--adacovex""><a class="
       & """header"" href=""#high-level-requirements--adacovex"">High-Level Requirements "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adacovex</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""requirement-index""><a class=""header"" href=""#requirement-index"">Requi"
       & "rement Index</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-ARCH: Architecture and build system</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-SCAN: Ada source scanning</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-PROOF: SPARK / GNATprove proof analysis</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-TEST: Test result parsing</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-COMPLIANCE: DO-178C compliance assessment (all DAL levels A-E)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-DAL-A to E: Per-level DAL criteria (see below)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-DAL-A: DAL-A criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced, no orphans, tests pass, Gold SPARK</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-DAL-B: DAL-B criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced, no orphans, tests pass, Silver SPARK</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-DAL-C: DAL-C criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced, no orphans, tests pass, Bronze SPARK</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-DAL-D: DAL-D criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced, tests pass</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-DAL-E: DAL-E criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-RENDER-ANSI: ANSI terminal rendering</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-RENDER-SVG: SVG badge generation</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-RENDER-MD: Markdown report generation</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-RENDER-HTML: HTML dashboard and JSON API</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-SERVER: HTTP server</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-ANSI: Terminal colour support</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-TZ: Timezone resolution and local-time formatting</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-CLI: CLI argument parsing</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-COMPLEXITY: Cyclomatic complexity and LOC gating</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-METRICS: Docstring coverage metrics</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-DIFF: Differential assessment ("
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "compare-base / "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "coverage-delta)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-MANIFEST: Alire manifest and dependency-graph parsing</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-PROVE: GNATprove subcommand</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-SBOM: Proof-aware SBOM generation</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>HLR-IR: IR type profiles, host/target config, and foreign type-name lowe"
       & "ring</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""requirements""><a class=""header"" href=""#requirements"">Requirements</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-ARCH: The tool shall build with <code>alr build</code> and support Ma"
       & "kefile targets for build, prove, fmt, lint, api-docs, changelog, and clean.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-SCAN: The tool shall recursively scan Ada source files. It shall extr"
       & "act subprogram declarations, docstring annotations, and HLR traceability tag"
       & "s.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-PROOF: The tool shall parse GNATprove summary output. It shall catego"
       & "rise verification conditions (flow, run-time, assertions, contracts, termina"
       & "tion).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-TEST: The tool shall parse AUnit test results (Markdown or stdout). I"
       & "t shall report total passed / failed test counts.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-COMPLIANCE: The tool shall assess DO-178C compliance for any DAL leve"
       & "l A through E. The compliance package defines and implements the assessment "
       & "criteria per level. The criteria appear in HLR-DAL-A through HLR-DAL-E.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-DAL-A: DAL-A assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage. All HLRs fou"
       & "nd in source must be traced. The assessment shall find no orphan tags. All t"
       & "ests must pass. The SPARK Gold level is the minimum requirement. All run-tim"
       & "e checks, assertions, functional contracts, and termination must be proved.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-DAL-B: DAL-B assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage. The assessme"
       & "nt shall find no orphan tags. All tests must pass. The SPARK Silver level is"
       & " the minimum requirement. All run-time checks and assertions must be proved."
       & " The code must be AoRTE-free.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-DAL-C: DAL-C assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage. The assessme"
       & "nt shall find no orphan tags. All tests must pass. The SPARK Bronze level is"
       & " the minimum requirement. Flow analysis must pass.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-DAL-D: DAL-D assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage. All tests mu"
       & "st pass. There is no SPARK proof requirement.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-DAL-E: DAL-E assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage only. There i"
       & "s no test or proof requirement.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-RENDER-ANSI: The tool shall render a colour-annotated summary report "
       & "to standard output. It shall use ANSI escape codes.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-RENDER-SVG: The tool shall generate Shields.io-style SVG badges. The "
       & "badges show SPARK level, test status, and DO-178C compliance status.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-RENDER-MD: The tool shall generate Markdown verification reports (VER"
       & "IFICATION.md). It shall generate traceability matrices (TRACE.md).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-RENDER-HTML: The tool shall generate a self-contained HTML dashboard "
       & "page. It shall generate a JSON metrics API.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-SERVER: The tool shall serve the dashboard, API, and badge endpoints."
       & " It shall use a built-in HTTP/1.1 server on a configurable port.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-ANSI: The tool shall colour its terminal output, and shall suppress c"
       & "olour inside CI or when NO_COLOR is set.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-TZ: The tool shall resolve a display timezone from the operating syst"
       & "em or from a user timezone override, and format the current date and time in"
       & " that zone.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-CLI: The tool shall accept CLI arguments in "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "key=value and "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "key value forms. It shall use sensible defaults. It shall print usage help o"
       & "n "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "help.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-COMPLEXITY: The tool shall compute per-file and per-subprogram cyclom"
       & "atic complexity for Ada source files. The tool shall enforce configurable LO"
       & "C and complexity gates. The gates cover maximum file LOC, maximum file perce"
       & "ntage of the codebase, maximum function complexity, and maximum file complex"
       & "ity.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-METRICS: The tool shall compute docstring coverage as a percentage of"
       & " documented subprograms over total subprograms.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-DIFF: The tool shall support differential assessment via <code>--comp"
       & "are-base</code>. The tool shall compare the target at a git base ref against"
       & " its current working tree. The tool shall report deltas in docstring coverag"
       & "e, HLR traceability, SPARK proof level, test results, and DAL status. The to"
       & "ol shall also support a lightweight docstring-coverage gate via <code>--cove"
       & "rage-delta</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-MANIFEST: The tool shall resolve the project dependency graph from Al"
       & "ire manifest files (alire.toml / alire-dev.toml). It shall resolve the alire"
       & ".lock solved-crate list and GNAT project (.gpr) with clauses. It shall dedup"
       & "licate results across sources.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-SBOM: The tool shall generate proof-aware software bills of materials"
       & ". It shall use CycloneDX 1.5 and SPDX 2.3 JSON. It shall extend every compon"
       & "ent with the adacovex:proof_level and adacovex:dal_target properties.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-PROVE: The tool shall provide a <code>prove</code> subcommand that ru"
       & "ns GNATprove against the root .gpr file of the target project. gnatprove is "
       & "not a declared dependency of the tool. When the alire.toml / alire-dev.toml "
       & "of the target project declares a gnatprove dependency, gnatprove is resolved"
       & " through Alire (<code>alr exec</code>). The tool then requires only <code>al"
       & "r</code> on PATH. Otherwise it falls back to a gnatprove on PATH, a cached ~"
       & "/.adacovex/toolchain/bin gnatprove, and finally a platform toolchain downloa"
       & "d. It transfers control to the standard assessment pipeline.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HLR-IR: The tool shall define bounded target machine-integer types. The t"
       & "ypes are IR_Int8 through IR_Int64 and IR_UInt8 through IR_UInt64. The tool s"
       & "hall define a host/target word-size configuration. The tool shall lower fore"
       & "ign type names (int32_t, size_t, usize, and more) onto these types. The tool"
       & " shall synthesise bounded Ada declarations. GNATprove can prove these declar"
       & "ations free of integer overflow.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
