       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><a href=""https://github.com/skanaar/nomnoml"">nomnoml</a> is bundled under"
       & " <code>resources/nomnoml.js</code> (71 KB, MIT). It is inlined into the dash"
       & "board page shell. It renders the dependency hierarchy as a UML-style diagram"
       & ". The diagram appears in the alternative view of the <strong>Dependencies</s"
       & "trong> tab (Tree / Diagram toggle).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The MIT licence text is preserved in the bundle header comment.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><a href=""https://github.com/cytoscape/graphre"">graphre</a> is bundled und"
       & "er <code>resources/graphre.js</code> (38 KB, MIT). It is inlined before nomn"
       & "oml. It provides the <code>graphre.graphlib</code> and Dagre layout that the"
       & " UMD wrapper (<code>global.graphre</code>) of nomnoml requires. Without it, "
       & "<code>nomnoml.draw</code> throws <code>graphlib is undefined</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The MIT licence text is preserved in the bundle header comment.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><a href=""https://github.com/nextapps-de/flexsearch"">FlexSearch</a> is bun"
       & "dled under <code>resources/flexsearch.js</code> (16 KB, Apache-2.0). It is i"
       & "nlined into the dashboard page shell. It provides the global search box (pac"
       & "kages, HLRs, dependencies). The search box uses an in-memory forward-tokeniz"
       & "ed index.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The index loads from <code>/__GRAPH_JSON__</code> at page load. The Apach"
       & "e-2.0 licence text is preserved in the bundle header comment.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><a href=""https://github.com/petersolopov/yace"">yace</a> is a tiny, zero-d"
       & "ependency code editor component (under 2 KB) by Peter Solopov. adacovex vend"
       & "ors its <code>code()</code> tokenizer highlighter (<code>src/highlighters/co"
