       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Ada source-file scanner."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Walks a project directory tree, reads every .ads file, extracts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram declarations, HLR tags, and docstring annotations."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "HLR-SCAN: Source scanning</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Supported docstring annotations (placed immediately before a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram declaration, no intervening blank lines):"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@param Name  Description.       "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Document a formal parameter"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@return Description.            "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Document a function return value"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@field Description.             "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Document a record component"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "@formal Name  Description.      "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Document a generic formal</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Standard tag aliases are accepted (<code>@parameter</code> == <code>@para"
       & "m</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>@returns</code> == <code>@return</code>), and the summary tags <code>@"
       & "brief</code> / <code>@summary</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "mark a subprogram as documented.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Conventions (following Ada_CRDT style):"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Prefix:  "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "   (two dashes + two spaces)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Summary: Capitalized sentence ending with a period."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Alignment: Two spaces between tag name and description text."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Placement: Summary lines first, then tag lines, then declaration.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Other standard comment styles are also recognised as docstrings:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "  one-line summary (single space, <code>-- </code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "  one-line summary (two spaces, <code>--  </code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "  one-line summary (tab separator)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "A bare <code>--</code> or <code>---</code> divider is not a docstring.  Docs"
       & "trings can"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "appear before or after the declaration.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Google style (Doxygen-free Python convention):"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "  Args:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "      X (int):  First operand."
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "  Returns:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "      The sum."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "An "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Args:"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " header opens a parameter block: deeper-indented comment lines"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inside it count as parameter entries.  "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Returns:"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " marks a documented"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "return value.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Sphinx style (reStructuredText field lists):"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "  :param X:  First operand."
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "  :returns: The sum."
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & ":param"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
