       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-110""><a class=""header"" href=""#adaco"
       & "vex-110"">adacovex 1.1.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-07-30</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.0.0 -&gt; 1.1.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-generic-keyword-bounds-not-matching-single-line-declarations""><a "
       & "class=""header"" href=""#h1-generic-keyword-bounds-not-matching-single-line-dec"
       & "larations"">H1: Generic keyword bounds not matching single-line declarations<"
       & "/a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Is_Subprogram_Decl</code> in <code>adacovex-parsers-source.adb</cod"
       & "e> had off-by-one bounds:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>""genericprocedure""</code> (16 chars) was compared against a 15-char sl"
       & "ice, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>""genericfunction""</code> (15 chars) against a 14-char slice. Since Ada"
       & " string"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "equality requires matching lengths, both branches never fired, meaning"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>generic procedure Reset;</code> on a single line was invisible to the "
       & "scanner.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> Single-line generic subprograms were silently ex"
       & "cluded from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "coverage tracking, docstring requirements, and subprogram counts.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Bounds corrected to <code>&gt;= 16</code> and <code"
       & ">&gt;= 15</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-determine_spark_level-returning-gold-for-missing-proof-data""><a c"
       & "lass=""header"" href=""#h2-determine_spark_level-returning-gold-for-missing-pro"
       & "of-data"">H2: <code>Determine_SPARK_Level</code> returning Gold for missing p"
       & "roof data</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When no GNATprove output exists (all fields zero), <code>0 &gt;= 0</code>"
       & " returned Gold"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "instead of Stone, causing DAL-C assessment to pass incorrectly for projects"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with no proof data at all.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> False-positive compliance pass for unproven proj"
       & "ects.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> <code>Parse_Prove_Out</code> now sets <code>Success"
       & " := Summary.Total_VCs &gt; 0</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "matching the existing guard in <code>Parse_Prove_JSON</code>. <code>Determin"
       & "e_SPARK_Level</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "remains a pure function.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h3-i2s-dropping-most-significant-digit-for-10-digit-numbers""><a clas"
       & "s=""header"" href=""#h3-i2s-dropping-most-significant-digit-for-10-digit-number"
       & "s"">H3: <code>I2S</code> dropping most significant digit for 10-digit numbers"
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>while R &gt; 0 and Pos &gt; 1</code> in <code>adacovex-renderers-sv"
       & "g.adb</code> exited when"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Pos = 1</code> even if <code>R</code> still held a digit. Numbers &gt;"
       & "= 1,000,000,000 (the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "upper half of <code>Natural</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s domain) would lose their leading digit.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> Incorrect SVG badge width or test-count output f"
       & "or very large"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "values (practically unlikely but technically incorrect).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Removed <code>and Pos &gt; 1</code> condition; loop"
       & " now exits when <code>R = 0</code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Return slice adjusted from <code>Buf (Pos + 1 .. 10)</code> to <code>Buf (Po"
       & "s .. 10)</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h4-unsynchronized-running-flag-across-server-tasks""><a class=""header"
       & """ href=""#h4-unsynchronized-running-flag-across-server-tasks"">H4: Unsynchroni"
       & "zed <code>Running</code> flag across server tasks</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>Running</code> field in <code>Server_State</code> was read/writ"
       & "ten by 5 tasks (1 main</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>4 workers) without synchronization. On weakly-ordered architectures,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "writes may never become visible to other tasks.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> If a worker hit 100 consecutive socket errors an"
       & "d set"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Running := False</code>, other workers and the main loop could hang in"
       & "definitely.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Extracted <code>Running</code> from the <code>Serve"
       & "r_State</code> record to a local"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Boolean with Atomic</code> variable in <code>Start</code>, ensuring pr"
       & "oper visibility"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "across tasks.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h5-read_request_line-buffer-overread-on-long-request-lines""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#h5-read_request_line-buffer-overread-on-long-request-lines"""
       & ">H5: <code>Read_Request_Line</code> buffer overread on long request lines</a"
       & "></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When 4096 bytes filled the buffer without a CRLF terminator, the last"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "two received bytes were silently discarded. The returned string could"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contain trailing undefined buffer content.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> Malformed path extraction for request URIs &gt;="
       & " 4094 bytes.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Added <code>or else Last &gt;= Buffer'Length</code>"
       & " guard, returning <code>""""</code> on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "buffer-full without CRLF to signal a malformed request.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h6-start_search--end_search-unprotected-against-exceptions""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#h6-start_search--end_search-unprotected-against-exceptions"""
       & ">H6: <code>Start_Search</code> / <code>End_Search</code> unprotected against"
       & " exceptions</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Ada.Directories.Search_Type</code> handles could leak if <code>Get_"
       & "Next_Entry</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "raised (e.g., on corrupted directory entries).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> OS resource leak (directory handle) during sourc"
       & "e traversal.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Wrapped <code>Start_Search</code> .. <code>End_Sear"
       & "ch</code> in a <code>begin exception when others =&gt; End_Search (Search); "
       & "raise; end;</code> block.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h7-naturalimage-leading-spaces-in-user-facing-output""><a class=""head"
       & "er"" href=""#h7-naturalimage-leading-spaces-in-user-facing-output"">H7: <code>N"
       & "atural'Image</code> leading spaces in user-facing output</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Natural'Image</code> and <code>Integer'Image</code> in Ada prepend "
       & "a space for non-negative"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "values, producing ugly output like <code>""  found  19 packages""</code> and <"
       & "code>&lt;td&gt; 19&lt;/td&gt;</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> Cosmetic "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " extra whitespace in terminal reports and HTML dashboard.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Added local <code>Img(Natural)</code> helper that s"
       & "trips the leading space."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Applied to <code>adacovex_main.adb</code> (terminal output) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex-renderers-html.adb</code> (dashboard HTML).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h8-hlr--false-match-inside-larger-words""><a class=""header"" href=""#h8"
       & "-hlr--false-match-inside-larger-words"">H8: <code>HLR-</code> false match ins"
       & "ide larger words</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Has_HLR_Tag</code> matched "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "HLR-"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " anywhere in a comment, including inside"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "larger words like <code>SUBHLR-SCAN</code>, producing false HLR tag detectio"
       & "ns.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> False positive HLR traceability, potentially mas"
       & "king missing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "requirements.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Added word-boundary check: skip <code>H</code> if p"
       & "receded by an uppercase"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "letter.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h9-removed-dead-code-parse_test_stdout""><a class=""header"" href=""#h9-"
       & "removed-dead-code-parse_test_stdout"">H9: Removed dead code <code>Parse_Test_"
       & "Stdout</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The stub procedure <code>Parse_Test_Stdout</code> in <code>adacovex-parse"
       & "rs-tests</code> was"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "never called and served no purpose.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Impact:</strong> Dead code surface area.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Removed the specification and implementation.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h10-closef-not-inside-exception-protection-after-read-loop""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#h10-closef-not-inside-exception-protection-after-read-loop"""
       & ">H10: <code>Close(F)</code> not inside exception protection after read loop<"
       & "/a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>In <code>Scan_Ads_File</code>, <code>Flush_Pending</code> and <code>Close"
       & "(F)</code> were outside the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exception-protected block. If <code>Flush_Pending</code> somehow raised, the"
       & " file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "handle would leak.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Fix:</strong> Moved <code>Flush_Pending</code> and <code>Close(F)"
       & "</code> inside the <code>begin ... exception ... end</code> block that prote"
       & "cts the read loop.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>152/152 native tests passing; counts unchanged from 1.0.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Self-assessment: <strong>Platinum</strong> (28/28 VCs proved, AoRTE-free)"
       & "."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada_CRDT (strict): <strong>Platinum</strong> (273 VCs, 5 justified overflow "
       & "checks).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. The tags in <code>docs/HLR.md</code> continue to cover the f"
       & "ixed packages:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>HLR-SCAN</code>, <code>HLR-PROOF</code>, <code>HLR-TEST</code>, <code>"
       & "HLR-COMPLIANCE</code>, <code>HLR-DAL-A..E</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>HLR-RENDER-ANSI</code> / <code>HLR-RENDER-SVG</code> / <code>HLR-RENDE"
       & "R-MD</code> / <code>HLR-RENDER-HTML</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>HLR-SERVER</code>, <code>HLR-CLI</code>, <code>HLR-METRICS</code>, <co"
       & "de>HLR-ARCH</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
