       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1100""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1100"">adacovex 1.10.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-15</em>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Version bumped 1.9.0 -&gt; 1.10.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-multi-standard-compliance-abstraction-iso-26262--iec-62304""><a cl"
       & "ass=""header"" href=""#c1-multi-standard-compliance-abstraction-iso-26262--iec-"
       & "62304"">C1: Multi-standard compliance abstraction (ISO 26262 / IEC 62304)</a>"
       & "</h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>One assessment can now satisfy DO-178C, ISO 26262, and IEC 62304 at the s"
       & "ame"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time. A new <code>docs/standards.md</code> page maps the three standards"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & " integrity levels"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(DAL A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "E, ASIL A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "D/QM, and safety classes A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "C) onto a shared rigor tier"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with the same four evidence checks adacovex already computes: HLR"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "traceability, no orphan tags, passing tests, and a minimum SPARK level.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Implemented via a <code>Compliance_Standard</code> type (<code>DO_178C</c"
       & "ode>, <code>ISO_26262</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>IEC_62304</code>) with <code>To_String</code> / <code>To_Standard</cod"
       & "e> conversions, a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Standard_Level_Name</code> level re-labelling function, and a <code>--"
       & "standard=NAME</code> CLI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "flag (default <code>do178c</code>) that reuses <code>--dal=LEVEL</code> as t"
       & "he shared rigor tier. A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "new <code>Assess_Standard</code> procedure runs the same evidence checks as "
       & "<code>Assess_DAL</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and records the standard, so the ANSI report and SVG badge print "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "ASIL B"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Class A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " instead of "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "DAL-C"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-metric-sync-tooling-for-test-counts-and-spark-level""><a class=""he"
       & "ader"" href=""#c2-metric-sync-tooling-for-test-counts-and-spark-level"">C2: Met"
       & "ric-sync tooling for test counts and SPARK level</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Hardcoded test counts and SPARK-level gates now have a script to keep the"
       & "m in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "sync, matching the existing proof-status script for VC counts. A new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/update-test-count.py</code> parses <code>docs/test_result.md</co"
       & "de>, rewrites the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "anchored test-count phrases across AGENTS.md, README.md, Makefile, the CI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "workflows, and <code>agents-tree.map</code>, then regenerates the AGENTS.md "
       & "source tree."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/update-proof-status.py</code> additionally rewrites the <code>--"
       & "require-spark</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>require-spark</code> CI gates in the Makefile, workflows, and docs.</p"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-source-scanner-recognises-oop-modifiers-and-word-boundaries""><a c"
       & "lass=""header"" href=""#c3-source-scanner-recognises-oop-modifiers-and-word-bou"
       & "ndaries"">C3: Source scanner recognises OOP modifiers and word boundaries</a>"
       & "</h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The scanner"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>Is_Subprogram_Decl</code> now understands <code>overriding</code> an"
       & "d"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>not overriding</code> subprogram declarations in addition to plain, ge"
       & "neric, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "function forms, and tab-indented declarations are handled.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-root-contributingmd""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4-root-contributin"
       & "gmd"">C4: Root CONTRIBUTING.md</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The contribution guide moved to a root-level <code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code>"
       & " so GitHub"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "renders its contributing link; the changelog format and unit-test catalogue "
       & "live"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "there.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-adacovex-status-subcommand""><a class=""header"" href=""#c5-adacovex-"
       & "status-subcommand"">C5: <code>adacovex status</code> subcommand</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new <code>adacovex status</code> subcommand reports the toolchain + pla"
       & "tform state"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "without running an assessment and without downloading or deploying anything:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "whether Alire (<code>alr</code>) is installed, whether gnatprove is dependen"
       & "cy-managed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(target manifest pin) or detectable (global pin, on <code>$PATH</code>, or c"
       & "ached in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>~/.adacovex/toolchain</code>), the host logical-CPU count and CI statu"
       & "s, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resulting default GNATprove parallelism. It also prints the release-note tha"
       & "t"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the CI binary is Linux x86-64 only.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-platform-support-documentation""><a class=""header"" href=""#c6-platf"
       & "orm-support-documentation"">C6: Platform-support documentation</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new <code>docs/platforms.md</code> page documents the supported platfor"
       & "ms (Linux as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "primary, macOS/FreeBSD/Windows from source), the CPU core-count detection"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "order (<code>/proc/cpuinfo</code>, <code>sysctl</code>, <code>nproc</code>, "
       & "<code>NUMBER_OF_PROCESSORS</code>, PowerShell),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CI detection, prove parallelism resolution, and the Linux-only release binar"
       & "y.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-dedicated-per-standard-level-flags-and---standardall""><a class=""h"
       & "eader"" href=""#c7-dedicated-per-standard-level-flags-and---standardall"">C7: D"
       & "edicated per-standard level flags and <code>--standard=all</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The shared <code>--dal=LEVEL</code> tier is complemented by dedicated lev"
       & "el flags that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spell each standard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s integrity level in its own naming: <code>--asil=LEVEL</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>A|B|C|D|QM</code>, ISO 26262) and <code>--class=LEVEL</code> (<code>A"
       & "|B|C</code>, IEC 62304). Each sets"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "both the compliance standard and the shared tier, so <code>--asil=B</code> i"
       & "s the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unambiguous spelling of "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "assess at ASIL B"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " (tier C) and <code>--class=A</code> of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "assess at safety Class A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ". <code>--standard=all</code> runs one assessment at the shared"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tier and emits badges for every standard (<code>do178c.svg</code>, <code>iso"
       & "26262.svg</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>iec62304.svg</code>) plus a per-standard breakdown in the ANSI report,"
       & " HTML"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard, JSON API, and Markdown report, without re-scanning or re-proving."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The CLI parser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s argument loop was extracted into a testable <code>Parse_Args</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entry point (a plain argument vector, no <code>Ada.Command_Line</code> acces"
       & "s) so the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "last-write-wins precedence across <code>--dal</code> / <code>--asil</code> /"
       & " <code>--class</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--standard</code> is covered by unit tests.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-standard-aware-sbom-and-renderers""><a class=""header"" href=""#c8-st"
       & "andard-aware-sbom-and-renderers"">C8: Standard-aware SBOM and renderers</a></"
       & "h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The proof-aware SBOM now records the assessment standard and its native l"
       & "evel"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "label alongside the shared tier: the root component carries"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex:standard</code> (<code>DO-178C</code> / <code>ISO 26262</code"
       & "> / <code>IEC 62304</code>) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex:level</code> (<code>DAL-C</code> / <code>ASIL B</code> / <cod"
       & "e>Class A</code>), in addition to the existing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex:proof_level</code> and <code>adacovex:dal_target</code> prope"
       & "rties (CycloneDX"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "properties, SPDX <code>attributionTexts</code>, and the Markdown table). The"
       & " HTML"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard, JSON API, and Markdown <code>VERIFICATION.md</code> now print the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standard-specific level label and the <code>--standard=all</code> per-standa"
       & "rd"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "breakdown; the ANSI report and SVG badges already did.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-per-standard-reference-pages""><a class=""header"" href=""#c9-per-sta"
       & "ndard-reference-pages"">C9: Per-standard reference pages</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Each standard now has a dedicated reference page mirroring the existing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "DO-178C one: <code>docs/api-docs/adacovex-asil-levels.md</code> (ISO 26262 A"
       & "SIL A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "D/QM"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "level definitions, criteria, and tier mapping) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/api-docs/adacovex-class-levels.md</code> (IEC 62304 safety classe"
       & "s A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "C)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Both are linked from the README documentation table, the CLI reference, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/standards.md</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c10-sbom-emits-every-standard-under---standardall""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#c10-sbom-emits-every-standard-under---standardall"">C10: SBOM emits e"
       & "very standard under <code>--standard=all</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The proof-aware SBOM is now fully standard-aware end to end. A single"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standard writes <code>adacovex:standard</code> / <code>adacovex:level</code>"
       & " for just that standard"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>--asil=B</code> -&gt; <code>ISO 26262</code> / <code>ASIL B</code>; <"
       & "code>--class=A</code> -&gt; <code>IEC 62304</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Class A</code>). Under <code>--standard=all</code> the same two proper"
       & "ties carry the joined"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "values for every standard "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>adacovex:standard = DO-178C, ISO 26262, IEC 62304</code> and <code>ad"
       & "acovex:level = DAL-C / ASIL B / Class A</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " across"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CycloneDX, SPDX <code>attributionTexts</code>, and the Markdown table, while"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex:dal_target</code> keeps the shared tier. Two new helpers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>All_Standards_Property</code>, <code>All_Levels_Property</code>) driv"
       & "e the joined output,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>Standard_Level_Name</code> now posts its tight 1..8 length bound.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c11-ci-feature-parity-with-the-multi-standard-set""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#c11-ci-feature-parity-with-the-multi-standard-set"">C11: CI feature p"
       & "arity with the multi-standard set</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The composite action gained <code>standard</code> / <code>asil</code> / <"
       & "code>class</code> inputs (threaded"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through to the assessment as <code>--standard</code> / <code>--asil</code> /"
       & " <code>--class</code>, with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--dal</code> still the shared tier) and now parses the compliance stat"
       & "us from the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standard-specific label (<code>DAL-X</code>, <code>ASIL X</code>, <code>QM</"
       & "code>, or <code>Class X</code>) instead of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "only <code>DAL-X</code>. <code>ci.yml</code> now runs three jobs: an <code>-"
       & "-standard=all</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "self-assessment, the native test suite and a push-only <code>make coverage-g"
       & "ate</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release-tag docstring gate. <code>pr-check.yml</code> and <code>release.yml<"
       & "/code> also pass"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>standard: all</code>, so PRs gate coverage across standards and releas"
       & "es emit all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "three compliance badges.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-scanner-false-positives-on-identifier-prefixes""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#h1-scanner-false-positives-on-identifier-prefixes"">H1: Scanner false"
       & " positives on identifier prefixes</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Is_Subprogram_Decl</code> matched <code>procedure</code> / <code>fu"
       & "nction</code> as a bare prefix, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "line such as <code>functionality : Integer := 0;</code> was counted as a sub"
       & "program"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration. Keyword matching now requires a word boundary, so identifiers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that merely begin with a keyword no longer inflate subprogram and docstring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "counts.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-subprogram-names-merged-with-return""><a class=""header"" href=""#h2-"
       & "subprogram-names-merged-with-return"">H2: Subprogram names merged with <code>"
       & "return</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The name extractor stripped all blanks, so a parameterless function like"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>function Value return Integer;</code> recorded the name <code>Valueret"
       & "urn</code>. Name"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "extraction now works on the raw line and stops at the keyword boundary,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "producing <code>Value</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>501 tests (was 395). The types category gained 23 checks for the dedicate"
       & "d"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "level parsers (<code>To_ASIL</code>, <code>Is_Valid_ASIL</code>, <code>To_Cl"
       & "ass</code>, <code>Is_Valid_Class</code>) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Standard_Slug</code>; the CLI-config category gained 31 checks (the <c"
       & "ode>Standard_All</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "default plus 30 flag-precedence checks driven through the new <code>Parse_Ar"
       & "gs</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entry point); the SVG category gained six checks for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standard-parameterized <code>Render_Compliance_Badge</code>; the SBOM catego"
       & "ry gained 29"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks (18 for the single-standard standard/level properties plus 11 for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "all-standards joined properties); and a new HTML/Markdown renderer category"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(17 checks) covers standard-aware dashboard, JSON, and Markdown output."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Total categories: 10 (was 9).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 401/401 VCs proved across 44 analysed units (was 343 at 1.9.0)."
       & " The compliance-standard layer (<code>Compliance_Standard</code>, <code>To_S"
       & "tandard</code>, <code>Standard_Level_Name</code>, <code>Standard_Slug</code>"
       & ", <code>To_ASIL</code>, <code>To_Class</code>) and the SBOM <code>Level_Prop"
       & "erty</code> / <code>All_Standards_Property</code> helpers added 58 SPARK VCs"
       & ", all discharged. The <code>prove</code> subcommand"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default proof budget was raised from <code>--steps=5000</code> to <code>--"
       & "steps=10000</code> because 5000 sat on the solver"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s non-determinism boundary for the enlarged unit; an explicit <code>--steps="
       & "...</code> still overrides it. Changed scanner files remain non-SPARK (`Adac"
       & "ovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Parsers. Source`).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. Source scanning remains covered by the existing <code>-- HLR"
       & "-SCAN</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tag in <code>src/parsers/adacovex-parsers-source.ads</code>; the new standar"
       & "d-aware"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "assessment and renderers reuse the existing <code>HLR-COMPLIANCE</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>HLR-DAL-A..E</code> / <code>HLR-SBOM</code> / <code>HLR-RENDER-*</code"
       & "> tags.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
