       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1110""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1110"">adacovex 1.11.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-17</em>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Version bumped 1.10.0 -&gt; 1.11.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1---version-flag-with-the-version-source-tied-to-the-installation-m"
       & "ethod""><a class=""header"" href=""#c1---version-flag-with-the-version-source-ti"
       & "ed-to-the-installation-method"">C1: <code>--version</code> flag with the vers"
       & "ion source tied to the installation method</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex --version</code> prints the bundled version (<code>adacove"
       & "x vX. Y. Z</code>) and exits. The version"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s source depends on how the binary was installed: a new <code>tools/gen-vers"
       & "ion.py</code> (pure stdlib, <code>argparse</code>/<code>pathlib</code>, type"
       & "d) resolves it from the first available of <code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code> (re"
       & "lease builds "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the release workflow and <code>make release VERSION=x.y.z</code> set it fro"
       & "m the `vX.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Y. Z<code>tag, and the action's build step regenerates the version file f"
       & "rom it, so the shipped binary always reports exactly the tag it was built fr"
       & "om),</code>alire/alire-dev.toml<code>(source checkouts), or</code>alire.toml"
       & "<code>(dependency-managed installs: when covex is built as an Alire crate th"
       & "e binary is compiled from the published crate source, whose</code>alire.toml"
       & "<code>-- the toml associated with the covex binary for dependency management"
       & " -- carries the release-manifest version;</code>alire-dev.toml<code>may not "
       & "exist in that tree). The script regenerates</code>src/adacovex_version_info."
       & "ads<code>on every</code>make build<code>(byte-identical when nothing changed"
       & "), and</code>Adacovex. Version<code>in</code>src/adacovex.ads<code>re-export"
       & "s the generated constant, so</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "version<code>, the man page, the SBOM tool version, and the result-cache nam"
       & "espace can never drift. </code>make bump-version<code>no longer hand-edits</"
       & "code>src/adacovex.ads`.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-man-subcommand-with-a-versioned-man-page""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c2-man-subcommand-with-a-versioned-man-page"">C2: <code>man</code> subcomma"
       & "nd with a versioned man page</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex man</code> installs the man page into the <strong>local ma"
       & "n database</strong> (Linux/WSL, no root): the default root is <code>$XDG_DAT"
       & "A_HOME/man</code> or <code>~/.local/share/man</code>, <code>--dir=PATH</code"
       & "> overrides it, and the index is refreshed with <code>mandb</code> when pres"
       & "ent. The page is generated by a new <code>Adacovex. Renderers. Man</code> pa"
       & "ckage and embeds the binary version (in the `.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>TH<code>header and a</code>VERSION<code>section).</code>adacovex man "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "check<code>parses the installed page and exits</code>0<code>when it matches "
       & "the binary,</code>1<code>when a newer version is available or none is instal"
       & "led, so a shell prompt hook can run</code>adacovex man "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "check<code>and auto-install the man page when the machine detects a newer ve"
       & "rsion.</code>make man<code>builds and installs. CLI hygiene: a bare</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "check<code>/</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "dir<code>without the</code>man` subcommand is now a loud error instead of be"
       & "ing silently ignored.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-multi-vcs-differential-modes-mercurial-subversion-fossil-jj""><a c"
       & "lass=""header"" href=""#c3-multi-vcs-differential-modes-mercurial-subversion-fo"
       & "ssil-jj"">C3: Multi-VCS differential modes (Mercurial, Subversion, Fossil, jj"
       & ")</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--compare-base</code> and <code>--coverage-delta</code> no longer r"
       & "equire git. A new <code>Adacovex. VCS</code> package detects the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s VCS by marker file (<code>.git</code> / <code>.jj</code> / <code>.hg</code"
       & "> / <code>.svn</code> / <code>.fslckout</code> / <code>_FOSSIL_</code>, with"
       & " a command-tool probe fallback) and snapshots a base revision without touchi"
       & "ng the working tree: git <code>worktree add --detach</code>, hg <code>archiv"
       & "e -r</code>, svn <code>info --show-item url</code> + <code>export -r</code>,"
       & " fossil <code>open</code> on a copied repo DB, and jj via <code>jj git expor"
       & "t</code> into its internal git store followed by a git worktree against <cod"
       & "e>.jj/repo/store/git</code> (jj commits are git commits). All snapshot comma"
       & "nds run through <code>sh -c</code>, so the feature works on Linux and WSL.</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For VCS whose snapshot UX is poor "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Subversion (no local history, network-dependent checkouts) and Fossil (nich"
       & "e tooling) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adacovex prints a note recommending the developers convert the repository t"
       & "o git (or a git-compatible VCS); git and jj (colocated jj+git resolves as gi"
       & "t) give the best experience.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-adacovex-status-reports-vcs-availability""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c4-adacovex-status-reports-vcs-availability"">C4: <code>adacovex status</co"
       & "de> reports VCS availability</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex status</code> now has a <code>vcs:</code> section listing "
       & "which VCS command-line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tools are available on PATH for the differential modes "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " git, mercurial"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>hg</code>), subversion (<code>svn</code>), fossil, jj, and the man-pa"
       & "ge tool (<code>mandb</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "plus the VCS detected for the target repository. When the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s VCS tool is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "missing from PATH, status prints a note that <code>--compare-base</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--coverage-delta</code> will need it. The exit code remains prove-tool"
       & "chain-driven;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the VCS report is informational.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-markdown-summaries-on-every-ci-run-with-loud-threshold-failures"">"
       & "<a class=""header"" href=""#c5-markdown-summaries-on-every-ci-run-with-loud-thr"
       & "eshold-failures"">C5: Markdown summaries on every CI run, with loud threshold"
       & " failures</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every CI run now leaves a Markdown summary at the bottom of the job page."
       & " The composite action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s assessment step writes an <code>## adacovex assessment</code> table (targe"
       & "t, bundled version, compliance label, SPARK level, tests, coverage) with a P"
       & "ASSED/FAILED verdict, and a new <code>if: always()</code> <strong>Write run "
       & "summary</strong> step appends a run-overview table on success and failure. T"
       & "he <code>ci.yml</code>, <code>pr-check.yml</code>, and <code>release.yml</co"
       & "de> workflows each gained a <code>summary</code> job (<code>if: always()</co"
       & "de>, <code>needs:</code> all other jobs) that aggregates every job result in"
       & "to one table. Threshold failures fail loudly at every layer: unmet <code>--r"
       & "equire-*</code> gates exit non-zero, are re-surfaced as GitHub <code>::error"
       & "::</code> annotations, are listed in the FAILED summary, and the workflow <c"
       & "ode>summary</code> job exits <code>1</code> when any of its dependencies fai"
       & "led.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s build step also verifies the downloaded/built binary with <code>--version<"
       & "/code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-man-db-mandb-detection-in-man-and-status""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c6-man-db-mandb-detection-in-man-and-status"">C6: man-db (mandb) detection "
       & "in <code>man</code> and <code>status</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex man</code> now tells the user when man-db is missing inste"
       & "ad of silently"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "skipping the database refresh: <code>Update_Database</code> returns whether "
       & "mandb was"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "found and exited 0, and a missing/failed mandb prints a warning that the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "page is still installed and readable via <code>man -l</code>. <code>adacovex"
       & " status</code> gained a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "note in the <code>vcs:</code> section explaining that <code>adacovex man</co"
       & "de> cannot refresh the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "man database when mandb is absent from PATH, so users know up front.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-make-check-quality-gate--single-source-crate-description""><a clas"
       & "s=""header"" href=""#c7-make-check-quality-gate--single-source-crate-descriptio"
       & "n"">C7: <code>make check</code> quality gate + single-source crate descriptio"
       & "n</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new <code>make check</code> target runs the full quality gate in one co"
       & "mmand "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " build,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "native tests, SPARK proof, SVG badges, API docs, SBOM, ASCII, changelog"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "format, and description sync "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and the obsolete <code>dev-setup</code> / <code>prod-setup</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stubs were removed. The crate description now has a single source of truth:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire/description.txt</code> + <code>alire/long-description.txt</code>"
       & ", propagated to every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest (<code>alire.toml</code>, release manifests, index entries) by a ne"
       & "w"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/update-description.py</code> (<code>make description</code>, <co"
       & "de>CHECK=1</code> to verify),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "wired into <code>make bump-version</code> / <code>make release</code> so a n"
       & "ew release always ships"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the current description. The <code>release</code> output (and the GitHub rel"
       & "ease body)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now links every changelog from the last release tag up to the released"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version. Build/dev prerequisites now list <strong>Python 3</strong> for the "
       & "pure-stdlib"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/*.py</code> scripts.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-result-caching-extended-to-hlrllr-parses-the-sbom-graph-and-diffs"
       & """><a class=""header"" href=""#c8-result-caching-extended-to-hlrllr-parses-the-s"
       & "bom-graph-and-diffs"">C8: Result caching extended to HLR/LLR parses, the SBOM"
       & " graph, and diffs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The on-disk result cache now also covers the DO-178C HLR.md/LLR.md parses"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>hlr:</code>/<code>llr:</code> keys, served into the DAL assessment), "
       & "the resolved SBOM"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dependency graph (<code>graph:</code> key over the manifests, lockfile, ever"
       & "y .gpr file,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the <code>.adacovex/patches/</code> dir), and the <code>--compare-base</"
       & "code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--coverage-delta</code> source scans (via <code>Scan_Project_Cached</c"
       & "ode>), so unchanged"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inputs are not re-parsed across runs.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-sbom-subcommand-is-standard-aware-and-defaults-to-all-standards"">"
       & "<a class=""header"" href=""#c9-sbom-subcommand-is-standard-aware-and-defaults-t"
       & "o-all-standards"">C9: <code>sbom</code> subcommand is standard-aware and defa"
       & "ults to all standards</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>sbom</code> subcommand accepts the standard flags (<code>--stan"
       & "dard</code>, <code>--dal</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--asil</code>, <code>--class</code>) and <strong>defaults to all stand"
       & "ards</strong>: without an explicit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standard flag the SBOM carries the joined DO-178C / ISO 26262 / IEC 62304"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "properties at the shared DAL tier; <code>--standard=iso26262</code> / <code>"
       & "--asil=B</code> narrows"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "it to ISO 26262 at ASIL B, <code>--class=A</code> to IEC 62304 at Class A. T"
       & "he usage,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "man page, README, and CLI reference document the new form.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c10---serve-dashboard-is-standard-aware-with-lightdark-themes""><a cl"
       & "ass=""header"" href=""#c10---serve-dashboard-is-standard-aware-with-lightdark-t"
       & "hemes"">C10: <code>--serve</code> dashboard is standard-aware with light/dark"
       & " themes</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The served dashboard (<code>--serve</code>) is standard-aware like the <c"
       & "ode>sbom</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subcommand: without an explicit <code>--standard</code> / <code>--asil</code"
       & "> / <code>--class</code> it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "renders every standard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s compliance level (DAL-C, ASIL B, Class A) at the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shared tier, and an explicit standard flag narrows it to that single"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standard. The dashboard page also supports <strong>light and dark themes</st"
       & "rong>: colors"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are driven by CSS custom properties, the initial theme follows the browser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>prefers-color-scheme</code>, and a header button toggles between light"
       & " and dark"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(persisted in <code>localStorage</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>616 tests (was 501), across 12 categories (was 10). The CLI-config catego"
       & "ry"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "covers <code>--version</code>, the <code>man</code> subcommand and its <code"
       & ">--check</code> / <code>--dir</code> flags,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the standard-awareness defaults for the <code>sbom</code> subcommand and"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--serve</code> dashboard (all standards by default, narrowed by <code>"
       & "--standard</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--asil</code> / <code>--class</code>); the HTML/Markdown renderers cat"
       & "egory covers the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standard-aware dashboard with the light/dark theme toggle,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>prefers-color-scheme</code>, and the JSON output; the DAL compliance c"
       & "ategory"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(16) gained the cached-HLR parse round-trip; the SBOM generator category"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(118) gained the dependency-graph cache round-trip; the Man page renderer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "category covers page structure, the embedded version, an install/read-back"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "round-trip, and the <code>Update_Database</code> man-db contract; the VCS su"
       & "pport"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "category (29) covers marker-file detection for every VCS, display and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tool-binary names, and the UX-conversion recommendations.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 401/401 VCs proved (unchanged from 1.10.0), 0 unproved, 0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "justified: the <code>--serve</code> standard-awareness and light/dark themin"
       & "g work"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "touched the config defaults and the HTML renderer only and added no proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "obligations. Proven with <code>make prove</code> under gnatprove 16.1.0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>--steps=10000</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. The VCS abstraction reuses the existing <code>-- HLR-DIFF</c"
       & "ode> tag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>src/core/adacovex-vcs.ads</code>, <code>src/core/adacovex-diff.ads</c"
