       & "/h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>tools/update-proof-status.py</code> and <code>tools/update-test-cou"
       & "nt.py</code> previously"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rewrote a hardcoded list of docs, which let stale metrics live in any file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "not on the list (e.g. the <code>601/601</code> test count in <code>alire/lon"
       & "g-description.txt</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "re-propagated to every manifest by the next <code>make description</code>). "
       & "Both tools"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now share <code>tools/live_files.py</code>, which derives the file set from "
       & "the tree:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every text file is scanned except generated outputs (docs/api-docs,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "docs/badges, docs/test_result.md, sbom.json, the generated Ada specs),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "historical records (past-release changelogs and past proof ledgers keep"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "their release-time numbers), and the tools themselves. Both also gained a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--check</code> mode that fails when any live file carries a stale metr"
       & "ic, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/update-doc-links.py</code> gained the same. The stale pre-1.12.0"
       & " VC counts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "in CONTRIBUTING.md and the crate-description proved/total phrasing are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "covered by new anchored patterns, as are the JSON API sample fields"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>""total_vcs""</code> / <code>""proved_vcs""</code> / <code>""tests_passed"""
       & "</code> / <code>""tests_failed""</code> in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "README and CLI reference) and the Makefile help"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Platinum, N VCs"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " comma"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "form "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so every number in the docs is anchored to generated artifacts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</code> and <code>docs/test_result.md</cod"
       & "e>) rather than a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hand-written claim.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-make-check-gate-ordering--tree-wide-count-sync-checks""><a class="""
       & "header"" href=""#c4-make-check-gate-ordering--tree-wide-count-sync-checks"">C4:"
       & " <code>make check</code> gate ordering + tree-wide count-sync checks</a></h3"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>make check</code> now runs cheap static gates first (ascii, spark-o"
       & "ff, changelog,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version source, doc links) so a formatting or sync problem fails before the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "expensive build + SPARK proof, then build / test / prove / doc / sbom, then"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the count-sync checks (<code>test-count --check</code>, <code>proof-status -"
       & "-check</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>description --check</code>) so a stale metric anywhere in the tree fai"
       & "ls the gate"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "loudly instead of silently drifting into the next release. The README"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Makefile-targets section, <code>make help</code>, and the AGENTS.md table we"
       & "re updated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "accordingly.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-readme-slimmed-433-lines-was-508""><a class=""header"" href=""#c5-rea"
       & "dme-slimmed-433-lines-was-508"">C5: README slimmed (433 lines, was 508)</a></"
       & "h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Detail duplicated from the docs was trimmed and pointed at its canonical"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "page: the VCS snapshot table (now one line, pointing at cli-reference"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s VCS"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section), the compliance-artifacts-identical paragraph (pointing at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standards.md), the full Makefile-targets table (pointing at AGENTS.md), the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "install/bundle instructions (condensed with the attestation + Linux-x86-64"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "notes kept), and the trust section (tightened). The JSON API section, flag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table, and examples remain in the README.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-aillm-usage-documented-on-a-dedicated-page""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c6-aillm-usage-documented-on-a-dedicated-page"">C6: AI/LLM usage document"
       & "ed on a dedicated page</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Ken Thompson <em>Reflections on Trusting Trust</em> reference, the AI"
       & " assistance"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "disclosure, and the "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "why should I trust your code"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " argument moved out of the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "README into <code>docs/llm-usage.md</code>, which also documents how LLM age"
       & "nts are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "expected to work on the tree under <code>AGENTS.md</code> (match conventions"
       & ", zero"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "library dependency, SPARK discipline, <code>make check</code> as the contrac"
       & "t,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "regenerate generated files rather than hand-editing them) and how every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "number in the docs is anchored to generated artifacts via the tree-wide sync"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tools rather than a written claim. The README now links to the page.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-unknown-flags-with-no-suggestion-print-the-full-usage""><a class="""
       & "header"" href=""#c7-unknown-flags-with-no-suggestion-print-the-full-usage"">C7:"
       & " unknown flags with no suggestion print the full usage</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>An unknown flag that has no close-enough known flag (edit distance &gt; 2"
       & ")"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now prints the full usage text to stdout after the one-line error, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "completely unrecognized token lands the user on the flag list instead of a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bare error. Near-miss typos still get just the "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "did you mean"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " hint (no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "usage dump). A new <code>Unknown_No_Suggest</code> config flag drives the be"
       & "haviour;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "config tests cover all three cases (no-match flag, near-miss flag, no-match"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bare word).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-adacovex-action-works-when-referenced-via-uses-""><a class=""header"
       & """ href=""#c8-adacovex-action-works-when-referenced-via-uses-"">C8: adacovex ac"
       & "tion works when referenced via <code>uses: ./</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s build/download steps read <code>github.action_repository</code>, which is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>empty</strong> when the action is referenced by a local path (<code>"
       & "uses: ./</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "consumer branch then tried to clone <code>https://github.com/.git</code> and"
       & " failed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with exit 128, breaking adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own <code>consumer-run-tests</code> CI job. Both"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "steps now fall back to <code>github.repository</code> (the workflow"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own repo, which"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "IS adacovex for the self-test), and the build step falls back to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>github.sha</code> for the ref so the scratch clone checks out the exac"
       & "t commit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "under test.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-installation-methods-on-a-dedicated-page""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c9-installation-methods-on-a-dedicated-page"">C9: installation methods on a"
       & " dedicated page</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>docs/installation.md</code> now covers the three install routes (Al"
       & "ire manifest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dependency, <code>alr install</code>, release bundle / source build), the pe"
       & "r-method"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version source, and keeping the man page in sync. The README"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s install"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section shrank to a two-line summary pointing at it, the giant CLI flag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table was dropped (the brief subcommand code block remains, with the full"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table in docs/cli-reference.md), the JSON API section was condensed to the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "endpoint + a curl example, and the README"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s documentation table now links"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the dashboard/JSON-API section directly. The README also now calls out that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--serve</code> serves a <strong>viewable HTML dashboard</strong> at <c"
       & "ode>/</code> (not just an API).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c10-llm-usage-page-expanded""><a class=""header"" href=""#c10-llm-usage-"
       & "page-expanded"">C10: LLM-usage page expanded</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The page gained a "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Working in a fork or branch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " section (the <code>make check</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "workflow as arbiter), a "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "served dashboard as a trust surface"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " section, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "an "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "honest limits"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " section (presence vs accuracy, SPARK-proof bar,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "changelog validator) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all anchored to the same gates and artifacts as the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rest of the docs.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c11-generated-file-generators-skip-rewriting-when-unchanged""><a clas"
       & "s=""header"" href=""#c11-generated-file-generators-skip-rewriting-when-unchange"
       & "d"">C11: generated-file generators skip rewriting when unchanged</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>tools/gen-version.py</code> and <code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code>"
       & " now compare the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generated output against the committed file and skip the write (printing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "up to date"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ") when byte-identical, so <code>make build</code> no longer touches"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "two generated files on every run "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>git status</code> stays quiet and the build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "output is shorter.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>659 tests (was 501), across 12 categories. The CLI-config category (124 c"
       & "hecks, up from 112) adds: <code>man --force</code> parsing (with and without"
       & " the prove-options guard), unknown-flag rejection with exit code 1, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "did you mean"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " suggestions for near-miss flags (single/multi character edits, missing dash"
       & "es), and the <code>Unknown_No_Suggest</code> contract (set for a no-match un"
       & "known flag and bare word, unset for a near-miss flag that produces a suggest"
       & "ion); the HTML/Markdown renderers category (34 checks) covers the dashboard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s theme dropdown (all three options, the <code>data-initial-theme</code> CLI"
       & "-theme marker, the Save settings button, <code>saveTheme</code> persistence,"
       & " the <code>? theme=</code> query param, the embed hint, the bundled template"
       & " shell, <code>data-theme</code> override, <code>prefers-color-scheme</code>,"
       & " and <code>localStorage</code>, plus no leftover <code>__CARDS__</code>/<cod"
       & "e>__THEME__</code> placeholders) on top of the standard-aware dashboard and "
       & "JSON output; the DAL compliance category (16) gained the cached-HLR parse ro"
       & "und-trip; the SBOM generator category (118) gained the dependency-graph cach"
       & "e round-trip; the Man page renderer category (18 checks) covers page structu"
       & "re, the embedded version, an install/read-back round-trip, the <code>Update_"
       & "Database</code> man-db contract, and a SYNOPSIS regression check (single quo"
       & "ted <code>. B</code> lines, no `.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>RI` concatenation); the VCS support category (29 checks) covers marker-fi"
       & "le detection for every VCS, display and tool-binary names, and the UX-conver"
       & "sion recommendations.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 408/408 VCs proved across 45 analysed units (up from 44): the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--theme</code> additions (the <code>Dashboard_Theme</code> type and it"
       & "s <code>To_String</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>To_Theme</code> / <code>Is_Valid_Theme</code> conversions in <code>Ada"
       & "covex.Types</code>) reuse the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "already-proved uppercase/parse patterns and add 7 VCs, all proved; the new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bundled dashboard template package (<code>Adacovex.Dashboard_Template</code>"
       & ", a String"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "constant generated from <code>resources/dashboard.html</code>) adds one anal"
       & "ysed unit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with no proof obligations; the CLI config parser (including the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Unknown_No_Suggest</code> field), VCS, and man-page packages are non-S"
       & "PARK I/O"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "code and add no proof obligations. Proven with <code>make prove</code> under"
       & " gnatprove"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "16.1.0 (<code>--steps=10000</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. The <code>man --force</code> and unknown-flag work stays cov"
       & "ered by the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "existing <code>HLR-CLI</code> (<code>src/core/adacovex-config.ads</code>); t"
       & "he doc-sync, generator,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and gate changes are Python/Makefile tooling that adds no traceability, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the installation/LLM-usage pages are documentation. The action and CI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "changes are workflow files that add no traceability.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
