       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1150""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1150"">adacovex 1.15.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-18</em>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Version bumped 1.14.0 -&gt; 1.15.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-docs-cross-linking-audit-and-generator-owned-api-doc-links""><a cl"
       & "ass=""header"" href=""#c1-docs-cross-linking-audit-and-generator-owned-api-doc-"
       & "links"">C1: docs cross-linking audit and generator-owned API-doc links</a></h"
       & "3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The docs were audited for misplaced and missing cross-links. The README"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "compliance bullet now leads with the general standards page instead of the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "DO-178C-only DAL page, and its ISO 26262 / IEC 62304 links point at the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dedicated ASIL / Class level pages; the "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Compliance levels"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " section links"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "all three per-level pages. <code>docs/target-projects.md</code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s HLR-format reference"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now points at the docstring spec"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s HLR-tags section instead of the DAL"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "criteria page, and the plain-text doc references in CONTRIBUTING.md,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "llm-usage.md, installation.md, platforms.md, and standards.md became real"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "links (dashboard.md and sbom.md gained standards links too, and llm-usage.md"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "carried a stale 653/653 test count, now corrected to 666/666).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The six hand-written reference pages (docstring spec, test formats, SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "levels, DAL/ASIL/Class levels) gained reciprocal "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "See also"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " sections. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generated api-docs cross-links live in <code>tools/rst2md.py</code> so they "
       & "survive"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make doc</code> regeneration: <code>GUIDE_PAGES</code> adds a "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Guides"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " section to the API"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "index, and <code>PACKAGE_GUIDES</code> renders a "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "See also"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " line on 13 package pages"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(parsers, compliance, types, prove, cache, diff, vcs, cpus, renderers,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "server) pointing at their reference pages "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " gnatdoc drops markdown link"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "URLs from <code>.ads</code> comments, so the links cannot live in source doc"
       & "strings."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "AGENTS.md"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Documentation block (via <code>tools/doc-links.map</code>) and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "developer-guide now document the pattern.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-badges-sized-per-glyph-instead-of-a-flat-7px-per-character-estima"
       & "te""><a class=""header"" href=""#c2-badges-sized-per-glyph-instead-of-a-flat-7px"
       & "-per-character-estimate"">C2: badges sized per-glyph instead of a flat 7px-pe"
       & "r-character estimate</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every SVG badge sized its label and value segments as <code>chars * 7 + 1"
       & "0</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pixels and centered the text, so the visible side padding was whatever the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "flat estimate left over. Uppercase-heavy text (SPARK, DO-178C, ISO 26262,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "IEC 62304) renders wider than 7px per glyph at the badge font"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s 11px size"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and came out nearly flush against the segment edge, while narrow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "lowercase/digit text (docs, 100%, Platinum) came in well under the estimate"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and carried visibly extra padding.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Badge_SVG</code> now measures each segment as the sum of per-glyph "
       & "advance"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "widths "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a DejaVu Sans metric table at 11px, rounded to the pixel, with a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "7px fallback for unknown characters "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " plus a fixed 20px total padding, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every badge carries the same 10px side padding regardless of its letters:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the Platinum value segment is 66px (46px text + 20) and the DAL-C PASS"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "segment 82px (62 + 20), the docs label 46px (26 + 20) and the 100% value"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "50px (30 + 20). Segments that were flush before (SPARK, ISO 26262,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "IEC 62304) now carry the same generous 10px margin as the rest. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard and server-served badges (<code>/badge/*.svg</code>) use the same "
       & "renderer,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so they pick up the fix automatically; the six <code>docs/badges/*.svg</code"
       & "> files"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are regenerated by <code>make prove</code> / <code>make run-self</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-spark_mode-on-expansion-across-pure-computation-helpers""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#c3-spark_mode-on-expansion-across-pure-computation-helpers"""
       & ">C3: SPARK_Mode On expansion across pure computation helpers</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>GNATprove analysed only a handful of explicitly-annotated subprograms; mo"
       & "st"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pure helpers were plain and so carried no proof obligations. <code>SPARK_Mod"
       & "e =&gt; On</code> (with Pre/Post contracts) was added where the computation "
       & "is pure and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the types are SPARK-clean, expanding the proved surface from 408 to 433"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "VCs with zero unproved:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>renderers-svg</code>: the per-glyph helpers <code>Glyph_Width</cod"
       & "e> / <code>Text_Width</code>, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "palette functions <code>Badge_Text_Color</code> / <code>Spark_Color</code> /"
       & " <code>Spark_Text_Color</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(the latter two were already On), and the integer-to-string <code>I2S</code>"
       & " all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prove; the string-assembly (<code>Badge_SVG</code> and the <code>Render_*</c"
       & "ode> badges) stays"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "plain "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " concat-chain bounds blow the solver budget, matching the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "existing <code>renderers-sbom</code> convention, and the <code>Render_Tests_"
       & "Badge</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Render_Compliance_Badge</code> / <code>Render_DO178C_Badge</code> func"
       & "tions take types"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from the non-SPARK <code>Types.Implementation</code> container package, so t"
       & "hey"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot be analysed.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>compliance-dal</code>: <code>Min_SPARK_For</code> and <code>Need_T"
       & "ests</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the two pure"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "helpers at the heart of the DAL assessment "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " are now On with contracts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pinning their result ranges (<code>Need_Tests</code> &lt;= 3, <code>Min_SPAR"
       & "K_For</code> maps"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every DAL level into <code>Stone</code>..<code>Platinum</code>). <code>Is_DA"
       & "L_Achieved</code> takes a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>DAL_Assessment</code> from <code>Types.Implementation</code> and stays"
       & " plain.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>cpus</code>: <code>Default_Prove_Jobs</code> is On with a Post pin"
       & "ning the CI /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "non-CI branch arithmetic (<code>Natural'Max (1, Cores - 2)</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>parsers-gnatprove</code>: <code>Determine_SPARK_Level</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the exact same rules the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof-status sync tool implements in Python "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " is On with a Post"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pinning its result to <code>Stone</code>..<code>Platinum</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Units that are I/O- or container-heavy (<code>main</code>, <code>server-h"
       & "ttp</code>, <code>cache</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>vcs</code>, <code>parsers-source</code>, <code>parsers-manifest</code>"
       & ") keep their default-off bodies,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "matching the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s existing SPARK discipline: subprograms that touch"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Types.Implementation</code> (the non-formal <code>Ada.Containers</code"
       & "> types SPARK forbids"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "analysing) or do file/process I/O carry no <code>SPARK_Mode</code> aspect ra"
       & "ther than"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "an explicit Off pragma.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-svg-renderer-tests-assert-badge-pixel-geometry""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#c4-svg-renderer-tests-assert-badge-pixel-geometry"">C4: SVG renderer "
       & "tests assert badge pixel geometry</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The SVG tests previously asserted only badge content "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " SVG markup, labels,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and values "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so a regression in the C2 per-glyph sizing (a wrong advance"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "width, a lost padding term, a mis-centered label) could ship a visually"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "broken badge with every test still green. The renderer tests now pin the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "actual pixel geometry of every badge.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex_renderer_svg_tests.adb</code> gained two helpers: <code>Nt"
       & "h_Attr</code> extracts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the numeric value of the Nth <code>attr=""...""</code> occurrence from the gen"
       & "erated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "markup (its leading-space needle keeps <code>x=""</code> from matching inside"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "clip-path corner radius <code>rx=""3""</code>), and <code>Check_Geometry</code"
       & "> asserts the six"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "numbers that fully determine a badge "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " total width, label and value"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "segment widths, the value segment"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s x offset (it must start exactly where"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the label segment ends), and the two centered text positions. All twelve"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "badge renderings now lock their geometry, e.g. SPARK Platinum 121px"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(55 + 66) with text centers at 27/88, Tests 738 Passed 130px (48 + 82),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "docs 100% 96px (46 + 50), DO-178C 149px (67 + 82), ISO 26262 160px"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(76 + 84), and IEC 62304 164px (75 + 89) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the exact values the C2"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "per-glyph table and 20px padding contract produce, and the same geometry"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make run-self</code> emits into <code>docs/badges/*.svg</code> (the re"
       & "generated tests.svg"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shows "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "738 Passed"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " at the same 130px width, since the tabular digits are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "all 7px). The suite grows from 666 to 738 checks (SVG renderer category"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "36 to 108).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-spark_mode-on-expansion-across-the-cli-validation-and-vcs-label-h"
       & "elpers""><a class=""header"" href=""#c5-spark_mode-on-expansion-across-the-cli-v"
       & "alidation-and-vcs-label-helpers"">C5: SPARK_Mode On expansion across the CLI "
       & "validation and VCS label helpers</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Building on C3, <code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> was added to five more p"
       & "ure helpers "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the ones with SPARK-clean types whose contracts are full characterizations"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of the result:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>config</code>: <code>Has_Prefix</code>, <code>Is_Help_Topic</code>"
       & ", and <code>Is_Valid_DAL</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the CLI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "argument parser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s pure validation helpers "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " are On with Postconditions"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that exactly characterize their results (a quantified prefix match for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Has_Prefix</code>, a leading-dash-or-alphabetic scan for <code>Is_Help"
       & "_Topic</code>, a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "single A-E/a-e character test for <code>Is_Valid_DAL</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>vcs</code>: <code>To_String</code> and <code>Tool_Name</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the VCS display/tool-name label"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "helpers used by <code>adacovex status</code> and the differential modes "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " are On"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with Posts pinning their result to the exact six-value repertoire"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>""git""</code>, <code>""mercurial""</code>, <code>""subversion""</code>, <c"
       & "ode>""fossil""</code>, <code>""jj""</code>, <code>""""</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The one C5 helper left plain "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>config.Is_All</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " was finished in C6"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "below. This expansion adds 38 provable checks (433 to 471 VCs) with zero"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unproved; the analysed-unit count stays 45 because the new On subprograms"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "live in units already analysed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-is_all-proved-and-the-server-badge-endpoints-pinned""><a class=""he"
       & "ader"" href=""#c6-is_all-proved-and-the-server-badge-endpoints-pinned"">C6: Is_"
       & "All proved, and the server badge endpoints pinned</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Two additions on top of C5: the <code>config.Is_All</code> proof was fini"
       & "shed, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the <code>/badge/*.svg</code> server surface gained direct geometry coverage"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong><code>config.Is_All</code> is now <code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code"
       & ">.</strong> The C5 attempt to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "characterize it with a quantified Post over the uppercased buffer blew the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prover"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s step budget in every formulation tried (per-character"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "equivalence, a True-implies-length-3 shape). The resolution is structural:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the upper-cased-buffer comparison <code>Up = ""ALL""</code> is exactly equival"
       & "ent to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "three case-insensitive character tests "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>S'Length = 3</code>, the first"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "character in <code>'a' | 'A'</code>, and the next two in <code>'l' | 'L'</co"
       & "de> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "function body and postcondition now state that characterization directly"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(no buffer, no quantifier). The Post fully characterizes the result and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proves cleanly, adding 13 provable checks (471 to 484 VCs) with zero"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unproved; the analysed-unit count stays 45 since <code>config</code> was alr"
       & "eady"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "analysed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Server badge endpoints covered by geometry tests.</strong> The fi"
       & "ve"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/badge/*.svg</code> routes in <code>adacovex-server-http.adb</code> se"
       & "rve"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Render_SPARK_Badge (Proof.Level)</code>, <code>Render_Tests_Badge (Tes"
       & "ts)</code>, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Render_Compliance_Badge (Assess, DO_178C / ISO_26262 / IEC_62304)</cod"
       & "e> for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>spark</code>, <code>tests</code>, <code>do178c</code>, <code>iso26262<"
       & "/code>, and <code>iec62304</code> respectively. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C4 geometry tests already pinned the spark / tests / ISO 26262 / IEC"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "62304 render calls and the <code>Render_DO178C_Badge</code> wrapper, but"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/badge/do178c.svg</code> is served through the standard-parameterized"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Render_Compliance_Badge (Assess, DO_178C)</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a call the suite did not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exercise. The SVG tests now carry a "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Server badge endpoints"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " section that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "names each route and pins its exact server-side render call: every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "endpoint asserts content plus the full six-number geometry, including"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/badge/do178c.svg</code> in both Achieved ("
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "DAL-C PASS"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ", 67/82/149) and Unmet"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "("
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "DAL-C FAIL"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ", 67/76/143) states through the exact server call, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/badge/tests.svg</code> at the self-assessment count (791 Passed, 48/8"
       & "2/130)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the same geometry <code>make run-self</code> emits into <code>docs/badges/t"
       & "ests.svg</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-release-changelog-list-now-newest-first-instead-of-glob-order""><a"
       & " class=""header"" href=""#h1-release-changelog-list-now-newest-first-instead-of"
       & "-glob-order"">H1: release changelog list now newest-first instead of glob ord"
       & "er</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>Create GitHub Release</code> step in <code>.github/workflows/re"
       & "lease.yml</code> iterated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/changelogs/adacovex-*.md</code> with a shell glob, so the release"
       & " body"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>Changelogs</strong> list came out in lexicographic file-name order "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>0.1.0</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>1.0.0</code>, <code>1.1.0</code>, <code>1.10.0</code>..<code>1.14.0</c"
       & "ode>, then <code>1.3.0</code>..<code>1.9.0</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " instead of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "newest-first. The step now collects the in-range versions and pipes them"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through <code>sort -V -r</code>, so the list reads <code>1.14.0</code> down "
       & "to <code>1.10.0</code> (and down"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to <code>0.1.0</code> when no previous release tag is found). The <code>make"
       & " release</code> target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prints the same list in the same order, and <code>docs/ci-cd.md</code> docum"
       & "ents the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "newest-first contract.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-bump-deprecated-node-20-actions-to-node-24-runtimes""><a class=""he"
       & "ader"" href=""#h2-bump-deprecated-node-20-actions-to-node-24-runtimes"">H2: bum"
       & "p deprecated Node-20 actions to Node-24 runtimes</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>GitHub deprecated the Node.js 20 runtime on Actions runners: actions that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "target Node 20 are now forced to run on Node 24, and every such step emits"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a deprecation warning. The composite action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>actions/cache</code> restore/save"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "steps (<code>@v4</code>, Node 20) and <code>actions/upload-artifact</code> s"
       & "teps (<code>@v4</code>, Node 20)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are bumped to <code>@v5</code> and <code>@v7</code> respectively, which run "
       & "on the Node 24"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "runtime (minimum Actions Runner 2.327.1). <code>actions/checkout@v7</code> a"
       & "nd"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>actions/attest@v4</code> already run on Node 24 and are unchanged. All"
       & " action"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inputs and outputs are unchanged, and consumers of the action (e.g."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada_CRDT via <code>bladeacer/adacovex@v1</code>) pick up the fix with the ne"
       & "xt"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>791 tests (was 738), across 12 categories: the C4 geometry tests add 72"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks to the SVG renderer category (36 to 108), and the C6 server badge"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "endpoint tests add 53 more (108 to 161) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the only test changes. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "changelog-listing and action-version fixes (H1/H2) are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release-workflow, Makefile, and composite-action shell/YAML code; the docs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "change is documentation plus <code>tools/rst2md.py</code> Python tooling (co"
       & "vered by"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make doc</code> and <code>make link-check</code>); and the SPARK expan"
       & "sions (C3/C5/C6) add"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "aspects and contracts without changing behaviour. The regenerated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/badges/*.svg</code> geometry is verified by <code>make run-self</"
       & "code>, by the proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run emitting the six badges, and now also directly by the C4/C6 unit tests.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 484/484 VCs proved across 45 analysed units (up from 408 at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "1.14.0): the C3 <code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> expansion added 25 provable"
       & " checks"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(408 to 433) across the renderers-svg helpers, the compliance-dal helpers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>Min_SPARK_For</code>, <code>Need_Tests</code>), <code>cpus.Default_Pr"
       & "ove_Jobs</code>, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>parsers-gnatprove.Determine_SPARK_Level</code>; the C5 expansion added"
       & " 38 more"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(433 to 471) across the config validation helpers (<code>Has_Prefix</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Is_Help_Topic</code>, <code>Is_Valid_DAL</code>) and the VCS label hel"
       & "pers (<code>To_String</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Tool_Name</code>); and the C6 <code>Is_All</code> completion added 13 "
       & "more (471 to 484)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all pure computation with SPARK-clean types. 0 unproved, 0 justified;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the non-SPARK bodies keep gnatprove analysing only the On subprograms,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exactly as before. Proven with <code>make prove</code> under gnatprove 16.1."
       & "0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>--steps=10000</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. The badge geometry tests (C4) and the server badge endpoint "
       & "tests (C6) extend the coverage of the existing <code>HLR-RENDER-SVG</code> t"
       & "ag (<code>src/renderers/adacovex-renderers-svg.ads</code>/<code>.adb</code> "
       & "and <code>src/tests/adacovex_renderer_svg_tests.adb</code>); the C6 endpoint"
       & " tests also pin the badge surface of <code>LLR-SERVER-01</code> (<code>HLR-S"
       & "ERVER</code>), whose routes are served through the same render calls. The SP"
       & "ARK expansions are covered by the existing <code>HLR-COMPLIANCE</code> / <co"
       & "de>HLR-DAL-*</code> tags (<code>compliance-dal</code>), <code>HLR-CPU</code>"
       & " (<code>cpus</code>), <code>HLR-PROOF</code> (<code>parsers-gnatprove</code>"
       & "), <code>HLR-CLI</code> (<code>config</code>, including the completed <code>"
       & "Is_All</code> proof), and <code>HLR-DIFF</code> (<code>vcs</code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the contracts extend the subprograms these tags already trace. The two fixe"
       & "s (H1/H2) live in release-workflow shell code, the <code>make release</code>"
       & " target, the composite action, and docs; the docs change touches documentati"
       & "on and <code>tools/rst2md.py</code> / <code>tools/doc-links.map</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>None of these carry HLR traceability tags.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
