       & "<li><code>Count_Proof_Patches</code> scans <code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/pa"
       & "tches/</code> for <code>.ads</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.adb</code> patch files; a target with no proof patches is proved agai"
       & "nst its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "own tree exactly as before.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Build_Patched_Copy</code> copies the target tree (excluding <code>"
       & ".git</code>, <code>obj</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>.adacovex</code>) into <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/adacovex-proof/</c"
       & "ode> and overwrites each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof-patched source with its merged form "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " package-level aspects"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spliced onto the package declaration line (a <code>package body ... is</code"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration included), and each aspect-carrying subprogram declaration"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "replaced by the patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declaration block. The merge engine (<code>Apply</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "matches on name <strong>and</strong> normalised parameter profile, so an ove"
       & "rloaded"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram patches its exact signature and never a same-named sibling;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the default <code>in</code> mode is equivalent to a bare mode (<code>in out<"
       & "/code> and <code>out</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stay distinct). Spec declarations terminate at their <code>;</code>, body"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarations at their <code>is</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a patched body declaration is replaced"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "without touching the body proper. An unmatched patch reference fails"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "loudly instead of being silently dropped.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>gnatprove runs against the copy"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s root project and the resulting"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>gnatprove.out</code> is copied back to <code>&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatpr"
       & "ove/gnatprove.out</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for the assessment pipeline. The copy lives under the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>obj/</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so it is excluded from scanning, manifest graphs, and the prove input"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hash. The originals are never touched.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Proof-patch contents are folded into the prove result-cache key, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patch edit invalidates the cached proof and forces a re-prove.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The two patch shapes: a <strong>spec patch</strong> (<code>.ads</code>) r"
       & "e-declares the vendored spec with contracts; a <strong>body patch</strong> ("
       & "<code>.adb</code>) opts the vendored body into the proof "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " gnatprove analyses a unit"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s body only when the body itself declares <code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code>, "
       & "so a SPARK-clean vendored body needs both. Where the body is SPARK-clean and"
       & " opted in, gnatprove proves the patched contracts (the documented <code>Vecm"
       & "ath. Clamp</code> worked example proves its <code>Post =&gt; Clamp'Result in"
       & " Lo .. Hi</code> outright "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all of its VCs proved, none unproved); where it is not (e.g. bodies that ca"
       & "ll `Ada.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Text_IO<code>, which is </code>SPARK_Mode Off`), gnatprove skips the I/O "
       & "bodies by design and reports the unit out of proof scope "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a proof patch never drags the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s proof level down.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Ada_CRDT dogfood target proves the mechanism end to end: its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads</code> now declares <code>"
       & "SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code> on the vendored package and pins the <code>Scroll"
       & "_Screen (From, To)</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scroll-region contract, and both <code>make run-ada-crdt</code> and Ada_CRDT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make prove</code> run through the patched copy, preserving the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(576 VCs, Platinum, DAL-C, 0 unproved). The merge engine is covered by the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "new <code>Proof patches</code> test category (C3). The patched-tree design a"
       & "nd the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patch file format are documented in the new <em>Proof patches: SPARK contrac"
       & "ts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "over vendored dependencies</em> section of <code>docs/architecture.md</code>"
       & " and in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "AGENTS.md"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s patch-directory section.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-server-routes-made-testable""><a class=""header"" href=""#c2-server-r"
       & "outes-made-testable"">C2: server routes made testable</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Adacovex.Server.HTTP</code> now exposes the request-path mapping as"
       & " a pure,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK-analysed function: <code>Route_Kind</code> and <code>Route (Path)</cod"
       & "e> return the route"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "kind (<code>Root</code>, <code>Badge_Spark</code>, <code>Badge_Tests</code>,"
       & " <code>Badge_DO178C</code>, <code>Badge_ISO26262</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Badge_IEC62304</code>, <code>API_Metrics</code>, or <code>Not_Found</c"
       & "ode>) and <code>Handle_Request</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "case-dispatches on the result instead of matching path strings inline. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "route mapping carries a full characterization postcondition, so the server"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "badge surface is provable rather than only exercised.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The new <code>Server routing</code> test category (C3"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s sibling, 24 tests) pins the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exact mapping for every route the server actually serves "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " dashboard,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "all five <code>/badge/*.svg</code> endpoints, <code>/api/metrics</code>, and"
       & " unknown paths "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the dispatch table cannot drift from the routes <code>Handle_Request</code> "
       & "serves.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-proof-patch-merge-engine-tests""><a class=""header"" href=""#c3-proof"
       & "-patch-merge-engine-tests"">C3: proof-patch merge engine tests</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>New <code>Proof patches</code> test category (35 tests) covering the merg"
       & "e engine in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Adacovex.Prove_Patch.Apply</code>: package-aspect splicing onto the pa"
       & "ckage"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration line (specs and <code>package body</code> declarations), subprog"
       & "ram"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration replacement (spec <code>;</code> and body <code>is</code> termin"
       & "ators), profile-aware"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "matching that distinguishes overloads (the exact <code>Scroll_Screen</code> "
       & "no-arg vs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "two-arg case from the vt100 dogfood) and treats the default <code>in</code> "
       & "mode as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bare (<code>in out</code> stays distinct), unmatched-patch rejection, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patch-content hashing for the prove cache key.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-documentation--a-dedicated-proving-guide-hlrllr-links-and-full-cl"
       & "i-coverage""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4-documentation--a-dedicated-proving-g"
       & "uide-hlrllr-links-and-full-cli-coverage"">C4: documentation "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a dedicated proving guide, HLR/LLR links, and full CLI coverage</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Proving moved from scattered design notes to a dedicated user-facing page"
       & ": new <code>docs/proving.md</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <em>Proving and writing SPARK proofs</em> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " covers how <code>adacovex prove</code> works (gnatprove resolution, the fal"
       & "l-through assessment, the result cache), what a proof contains (the VC categ"
       & "ories and the Stone.. Platinum model), how to write SPARK contracts (the bod"
       & "y-must-opt-in rule, why <code>Ada. Text_IO</code> bodies are skipped), and t"
       & "he full proof-patch section: <strong>why</strong> patches exist for vendored"
       & " deps (strict mode counts vendored code, bodies must opt in, sources are imm"
       & "utable), <strong>how</strong> to write the <code>.ads</code> spec patch and "
       & "<code>.adb</code> body patch, the matching rules, a worked <code>Vecmath. Cl"
       & "amp</code> example that proves its contract, and a pitfalls section.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The page is linked from the README documentation table, AGENTS.md"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Documentation block, the CLI reference, target-projects, and architecture."
       & "</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The CLI reference gained the missing first-class surfaces: a full <strong"
       & "><code>prove</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subcommand</strong> section (its eight options, the fall-through to the asse"
       & "ssment"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pipeline, gnatprove resolution, the patched-copy proof tree, and the cache /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--force</code> semantics), the <strong><code>--no-sbom</code> / <code>"
       & "--sbom-format</code></strong> flags for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "automatic SBOM every assessment writes, and <strong><code>man --force</code>"
       & "</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/sbom.md</code> now documents the Markdown (<code>md</code>) SBOM "
       & "format alongside"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CycloneDX and SPDX. The internal traceability documents <code>docs/HLR.md</c"
       & "ode> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/LLR.md</code> are now linked from the README and AGENTS.md docume"
       & "ntation"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "lists.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>850 tests (was 791), across 14 categories: the C2 <code>Server routing</c"
       & "ode> category"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adds 24 tests (new category) and the C3 <code>Proof patches</code> category "
       & "adds 35"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(new category) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the only test changes; the SVG renderer category stays at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "161. All other changes (C1/C2) add aspects and contracts without changing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "behaviour. The regenerated <code>docs/badges/*.svg</code> geometry is unchan"
       & "ged and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make run-ada-crdt</code> dogfood regression still passes. Counts synce"
       & "d with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make test-count</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 487/487 VCs proved across 48 analysed units (up from 484 at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "1.15.0): the C2 <code>Route</code> mapping in <code>server-http</code> (newl"
       & "y <code>SPARK_Mode =&gt; On</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with its path-to-route postcondition) and the newly analysed units"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>prove_patch</code>, <code>server_tests</code>, <code>prove_patch_test"
       & "s</code>) added 3 provable checks"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(484 to 487) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " 230 run-time checks, 78 assertions, 52 functional contracts,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "45 data-dependency checks, 4 initialization checks, and 78 termination"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks, all proved. 0 unproved, 0 justified; the I/O- and container-heavy"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>prove_patch</code> bodies stay default-off, so gnatprove analyses only"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK-clean helpers, exactly as before. Proven with <code>make prove</code> "
       & "under"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove 16.1.0 (<code>--steps=10000</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. The proof-patch machinery extends the existing <code>HLR-PRO"
       & "VE</code> tag (<code>src/core/adacovex-prove_patch.ads</code>/<code>.adb</co"
       & "de> alongside <code>adacovex-prove</code>), covered by the C3 merge-engine t"
       & "ests and the Ada_CRDT dogfood regression (<code>make run-ada-crdt</code>), a"
       & "nd documented in the new <code>docs/proving.md</code> guide, <code>docs/arch"
       & "itecture.md</code>, and AGENTS.md. The C4 documentation changes are document"
       & "ation-only (new <code>proving.md</code> page, README/AGENTS.md link tables, "
       & "CLI-reference and sbom.md coverage) and carry no HLR tags. The C2 route mapp"
       & "ing extends <code>HLR-SERVER</code> / <code>LLR-SERVER-01</code>: <code>Rout"
       & "e</code> is the single pure mapping behind every <code>/</code>, <code>/badg"
       & "e/*.svg</code>, and <code>/api/metrics</code> route that <code>Handle_Reques"
       & "t</code> serves, pinned by the C2 <code>Server routing</code> tests and prov"
       & "ed by its postcondition.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>None of the changes introduce new high-level requirements; the two new te"
       & "st categories extend the coverage of the existing <code>HLR-PROVE</code> and"
       & " <code>HLR-SERVER</code> tags.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
