       & Character'Val(147)
       & " proved vs unproved VCs;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Test results</strong> bar chart "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " per-category pass counts;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Proof check-types</strong> bar chart "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " proved checks per check kind;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Docstring coverage</strong> bar chart "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " documented vs undocumented"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprograms per unit.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Charts.css is vendored as <code>resources/charts.min.css</code> and <stro"
       & "ng>inlined into the self-contained dashboard template</strong> (<code>resour"
       & "ces/dashboard.html</code>), so the dashboard keeps its zero-dependency, sing"
       & "le-file, offline-serving property "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no CDN, no network. The chart cards are generated by the new <code>Renderer"
       & "s. HTML. Render_Charts</code> and injected through the template"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>__CHARTS__</code> placeholder.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Charts update live with the metrics (the JSON API below feeds the same da"
       & "ta the dashboard shows). See <a href=""../usage/dashboard.html#metrics-charts"
       & """>docs/dashboard.md</a> and <a href=""../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.html"">docs/THIRD"
       & "_PARTY_NOTICES.md</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-dependency-graph--rest-api--json-metrics-export""><a class=""header"
       & """ href=""#c2-dependency-graph--rest-api--json-metrics-export"">C2: dependency "
       & "graph "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " REST API + JSON metrics export</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dependency graph the SBOM builds is no longer locked inside <code>sbo"
       & "m.json</code>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>GET /api/deps</code></strong> on the <code>--serve</code> "
       & "dashboard returns the full dependency"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "graph as JSON (name, version, scope, parent, purl, kind), matching the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "existing <code>/api/metrics</code> endpoint style.  The server state now car"
       & "ries the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolved graph, populated once in serve mode.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>--emit-metrics=PATH</code></strong> writes a combined mach"
       & "ine-readable export after"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the assessment:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>{""metrics"": {...}, ""dependencies"": {...}}</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the same JSON the dashboard"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "API serves, on disk for scripting, dashboards, or archiving.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Both are wired end to end: <code>emit-metrics</code> action input, docs/c"
       & "i-cd.md row,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the action-parity gate.  <code>--emit-metrics</code> output is uploaded "
       & "as a CI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "artifact (see C7).  One new server-routing test pins the <code>/api/deps</co"
       & "de> route.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-shell-auto-completion--adacovex-completion""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c3-shell-auto-completion--adacovex-completion"">C3: shell auto-completion"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>adacovex completion</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex completion</code> (alias <code>--completion[=SHELL]</code>"
       & ") prints a static"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "completion script for <strong>bash</strong>, <strong>fish</strong>, <strong>"
       & "zsh</strong>, or <strong>pwsh</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>SHELL</code> auto-detected from <code>$SHELL</code>; unknown shells f"
       & "all back to bash)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The scripts complete the subcommands and every long flag from the binary"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "own <code>Known_Flags</code> table, so the completion set cannot drift from "
       & "the CLI:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">eval ""$(adacovex completion)""           # b"
       & "ash (default) / auto-detected"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source &lt;(adacovex completion zsh)       # zsh"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex completion fish | source       # fish"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex completion pwsh | Invoke-Expression   # PowerShell"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Zero dependencies: bash uses <code>compgen</code>, zsh <code>_arguments</"
       & "code>, fish a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>complete</code>-based function, pwsh <code>Register-ArgumentCompleter<"
       & "/code>.  The scripts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "complete the current word with a prefix filter against the flag list and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subcommand names, appending nothing for bare-flag completion.  The new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Adacovex.Completion</code> package (spec + body, docstring-complete, n"
       & "o SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "aspects "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " pure string emission) is covered by 13 new CLI-config tests"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(script presence per shell, embedded flag-list check, unknown-shell"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fallback).  <code>completion</code> is deliberately a <strong>CLI-only</stro"
       & "ng> early-exit mode in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the action-parity allow-list (like <code>status</code> / <code>man</code> / "
       & "<code>sbom</code>): CI does not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "need an interactive shell.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-system-tool-probe-cache-sbom-speedup""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4"
       & "-system-tool-probe-cache-sbom-speedup"">C4: system-tool probe cache (SBOM spe"
       & "edup)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The SBOM"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s dev-scope dependency scan probes every referenced system tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version by spawning <code>&lt;tool&gt; &lt;flag&gt;</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " tens of milliseconds per tool.  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "result is now cached on disk under <code>&lt;cache-root&gt;/probes/&lt;tool&"
       & "gt;</code> with a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>7-day TTL</strong>, so unchanged toolchains stop paying the spawn co"
       & "st on every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Measured on an 11-tool toolchain (self-assessment, this repo):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th></th><th>before</th><th>after</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>cold full pipeline</td><td>~490 ms</td><td>~490 ms</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>warm full pipeline</td><td>~430 ms</td><td><strong>~310 ms</strong><"
       & "/td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td>system time (warm)</td><td>~40 ms</td><td><strong>~8 ms</strong></td"
       & "></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>--no-cache</code> disables the probe cache too (it lives under the "
       & "cache root)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The TTL means a toolchain upgrade shows up in the SBOM within a week even on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "machines that never re-probe explicitly.  See"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""../contributing/perf.html#probe-cache"">docs/perf.md</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-make-bench--hyperfine-timings--binary-size""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c5-make-bench--hyperfine-timings--binary-size"">C5: <code>make bench</cod"
       & "e> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " hyperfine timings + binary size</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new <code>bench</code> target times the assessment pipeline with <stron"
       & "g>hyperfine</strong> when"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "installed (bash <code>time</code> fallback: no tooling required), measuring "
       & "cold"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(fresh result + probe cache) and warm (populated caches) runs, and reports"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the <strong>binary size</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " raw and stripped (strip measured on a <code>/tmp</code> copy, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the build output is never modified).  Numbers are machine-dependent on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "purpose: the target is a deterministic <em>recipe</em>, and it is intentiona"
       & "lly"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<em>not</em> part of <code>make check</code> (a slow CI runner must not fail"
       & " a build)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Documented in <a href=""../contributing/perf.html"">docs/perf.md</a>.  Binary "
       & "size check on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "current build: 7.1 MiB, 3.1 MiB stripped (-57%).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-cyclomatic-complexity-gate--no-god-objects""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c6-cyclomatic-complexity-gate--no-god-objects"">C6: cyclomatic-complexity"
       & " gate "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no god objects</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>New <code>make complexity-check</code> static gate (native Ada implementa"
       & "tion), wired into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make check</code>, <code>ci.yml</code>, <code>pr-check.yml</code>, and"
       & " <code>release.yml</code>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>per-file source LOC cap (2000) and a <strong>percentage-of-codebase cap<"
       & "/strong> (10%)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no file may dominate the tree (god objects);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>per-subprogram <strong>cyclomatic complexity</strong> cap (50 decision p"
       & "oints) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " god"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "functions are flagged as refactor candidates;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>per-file total decision-point cap (300).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The gate shipped with the refactors it enforces: the DO-178C markdown"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scanner"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s file-reading loop was extracted into a shared generic line-parser"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(one file-read skeleton, two entry types) and its in-line table parsing into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Parse_Table_Row</code>; the test-result parser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s big loop was split into six"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "line-style handlers (<code>Passed</code>/<code>Failed</code>, TAP, Automake,"
       & " Surefire, Unity)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "plus the category-helper; and the source scanner"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s file-name extraction"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "became a helper.  Worst function complexity fell from 57 to 49, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "highest-complexity file dropped under the file cap. All thresholds are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "configurable flags and are documented in the tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s module docstring.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6b-test-summary-tables-now-parse-in-both-layouts-incl-the-native-on"
       & "e""><a class=""header"" href=""#c6b-test-summary-tables-now-parse-in-both-layout"
       & "s-incl-the-native-one"">C6b: test-summary tables now parse in both layouts (i"
       & "ncl. the native one)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Markdown-table parser only accepted the AUnit-report layout with a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "leading index cell (<code>| - | Category | N | PASS |</code>); the native"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>test_runner</code> layout (<code>| Category | N | PASS |</code>, no in"
       & "dex cell) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "space-padded count cells (<code>| 67 |</code>) were silently skipped, so the"
       & " new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard Tests chart was empty for the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own <code>test_result.md</code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Parse_Table_Row</code> now detects the numeric count cell by its digit"
       & "s in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "either layout, trims column padding from the count and category cells, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "keeps the existing footer-overrides-totals semantics. Seven new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Test-result-parser tests pin the plain layout (with header and separator"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rows). This makes the <a href=""../api-docs/adacovex-test-format.html"">test f"
       & "ormat spec</a>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the single source of truth for what every format "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Markdown tables (both"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "layouts), TAP, Automake, Maven Surefire, Unity and AUnit reports "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " looks"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "like and which line wins when formats mix.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-ci--less-brittle-better-debugging-output""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c7-ci--less-brittle-better-debugging-output"">C7: CI "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " less brittle, better debugging output</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>the composite action folds the assessment output into a <strong>log grou"
       & "p</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>::group::</code>) so the step result never hides the debug detail;</l"
       & "i>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>WARNING</code> lines are re-surfaced as <strong><code>::notice::</"
       & "code> annotations</strong>;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>a new <strong><code>adacovex-assessment</code> artifact</strong> (upload"
       & "ed <code>if: always()</code>, success"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or failure) carries the full untruncated assessment log "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--emit-metrics</code> JSON export when requested "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so a flaky or unmet gate"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "never requires re-running locally to reproduce;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>a standalone <strong>complexity-gate job</strong> runs in <code>ci.yml</"
       & "code> and <code>pr-check.yml</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(visible in each workflow"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s summary table).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>886 tests passing (was 865) across 14 categories: the CLI config category"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "grows from 139 to 152 with the completion-script tests (bash/zsh/fish/pwsh"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "script shape, embedded flag list, unknown-shell fallback), the server"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "routing category grows from 24 to 25 with the <code>/api/deps</code> route t"
       & "est, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the test-result parser category grows from 43 to 50 with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "plain-layout/space-padded table tests. Counts synced with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make test-count</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 720/720 VCs proved across 48 analysed units (unchanged from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "1.18.0): all new code (chart rendering, deps serialization, completion"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scripts, probe cache, complexity tooling, CI wiring) lives in default-off or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "I/O-bound bodies or is Python/bash tooling "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no new proof obligations. 0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unproved, 0 justified. The probe cache and completion packages re-verified"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with <code>adacovex prove --target=. --force</code> under gnatprove 16.1.0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>--steps=10000</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. The new surface extends three existing tags with CLI-relevan"
       & "t"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tests, all wired through the parity gate and native tests:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DASH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " chart cards + <code>/api/deps</code> (server tests category,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard docs);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-CLI</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>--emit-metrics</code> export, <code>completion</code> subcommand"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(config tests);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SBOM</code> / SBOM-dev-deps "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " probe cache (cache.ads/.adb,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "perf docs);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>quality gates "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " complexity-check feature gate (Makefile, ci.yml,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pr-check.yml, release.yml, action-parity allow-list).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <code>docs/cli-reference.md</code> (flags, <code>completion</code>, <"
       & "code>--emit-metrics</code>),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/dashboard.md</code> (charts, REST API), and <code>docs/perf.md</c"
       & "ode> (bench,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "probe cache, binary size).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
