       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1290""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1290"">adacovex 1.29.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-26</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.28.0 -&gt; 1.29.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-dev-dependency-metadata-resolved-from-alr-show-into-the-sbom-and-"
       & "dashboard""><a class=""header"" href=""#c1-dev-dependency-metadata-resolved-from"
       & "-alr-show-into-the-sbom-and-dashboard"">C1: Dev-dependency metadata resolved "
       & "from <code>alr show</code> into the SBOM and dashboard</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Manifest-declared dependencies "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " dev deps from <code>alire-dev.toml</code> and base deps"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that no lockfile or GPR with-clause resolved "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " previously appeared name-only"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with an empty version and licence and no source link. adacovex now invokes t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tool-specific <code>alr show &lt;crate&gt;</code> (which answers from Alire"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s local index, no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "network access) and parses the <code>License:</code>, <code>Version:</code> "
       & "and <code>Website:</code> fields."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The metadata is filled onto the freshly appended entry or, when the crate wa"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "already resolved from the lockfile (so it keeps its solved identity), patche"
       & "d"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "onto the existing entry when those fields were empty.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The SBOM spec output carries the source reference in all three formats:</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>CycloneDX 1.5: <code>externalReferences</code> (type <code>website</code"
       & ">) with the source URL.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>SPDX 2.3: the <code>homepage</code> field.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Markdown: a <code>Source</code> column in the dependencies table (and a "
       & "<code>| Source |</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "row for the root project).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No garbage links are produced: a URL is only ever taken from the release"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "metadata, never guessed from a PURL. The dashboard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>/api/deps</code> JSON now also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ships a <code>website</code> field per component.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-dependency-source-links-prefer-the-resolved-repository""><a class="
       & """header"" href=""#c2-dependency-source-links-prefer-the-resolved-repository"">C"
       & "2: Dependency source links prefer the resolved repository</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dep-details Link row picks the resolved <code>website</code> when it "
       & "is a genuine"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>http(s)</code> URL, and only falls back to a PURL-derived registry lin"
       & "k for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "well-known registries. The old generic GitHub-search fallback for unknown"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ecosystems is gone, because a search URL for a system or generic dependency "
       & "is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "noise.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-dependency-split-layout""><a class=""header"" href=""#c3-dependency-s"
       & "plit-layout"">C3: Dependency split layout</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Collapsed (no detail selected) the dependency tree and the nomnoml diagra"
       & "m fill"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the full container width. Selecting a dependency activates a split layout: t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tree/diagram docks to the left column and the detail card slides into a righ"
       & "t"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "column (stacked on small screens). The detail panel moved out of the tree ca"
       & "rd"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so it serves both the Tree and the Diagram views alike.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-diagram-contrast-and-clickable-boxes""><a class=""header"" href=""#c4"
       & "-diagram-contrast-and-clickable-boxes"">C4: Diagram contrast and clickable bo"
       & "xes</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>nomnoml draws node titles in the <code>stroke</code> colour, which the pr"
       & "evious theme"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "binding set to the muted border (light grey in light mode, near-black in dar"
       & "k"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "mode) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " poor reading contrast on the card fill. The stroke/text now follows the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "primary text colour in both themes. nomnoml renders to a single <code>&lt;ca"
       & "nvas&gt;</code>, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "each box is hit-tested against the layout rectangles returned by the draw an"
       & "d a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "click on a box opens its dependency detail panel.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-chart-text-is-upright-bounded-and-readable""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c5-chart-text-is-upright-bounded-and-readable"">C5: Chart text is upright"
       & ", bounded and readable</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Pie/donut labels and values no longer rotate with each slice.  Charts.cs"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rotates custom properties by the slice midpoint angle, which flipped numbers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "in large or non-half slices upside down.  They now render with no transform."
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Horizontal bar category labels are width-bounded with an ellipsis and th"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rows have a minimum height, so long test-category names no longer clip or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spill off the left edge of the dashboard.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Dependencies by Scope"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " polar centre now sits on a card-coloured disc, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the centre figure no longer draws directly on the vivid scope gradient (the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "grey <code>9</code> that was hard to read in the middle of the ring).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-compliance-tab-is-standards-aware""><a class=""header"" href=""#c6-co"
       & "mpliance-tab-is-standards-aware"">C6: Compliance tab is standards-aware</a></"
       & "h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Compliance section now renders one achievement gauge per standard"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(DO-178C, ISO 26262, IEC 62304) with that standard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s target integrity level,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "achieved percentage and status "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " whether one standard or all are targeted."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The table lists every standard and its level and status, and highlights the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "targeted standard(s) with a chip and outline. The served dashboard targets a"
       & "ll"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "standards by default, and this brings the compliance chart in line with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "badges row (which already listed every standard under <code>--standard=all</"
       & "code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-detailed-proof-guidance""><a class=""header"" href=""#c7-detailed-pro"
       & "of-guidance"">C7: Detailed proof guidance</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Proof tab gains a "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "How to proceed (Proof Guidance)"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " card that turns the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove unproved counts into concrete next steps per category: Global /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "initialises aspects, initialisation at declaration, loop invariants and rang"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "preconditions, strengthened Pre/Post contracts, Postconditions for functiona"
       & "l"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks, and Measure / Decreasing clauses for termination.  When every VC is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proved it reads "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "No unproved VCs "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the proof is complete."
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & "  It reminds the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reader that a justified VC (<code>pragma Assume</code>) never counts as prov"
       & "ed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-duplicate-charts-removed-dry""><a class=""header"" href=""#c8-duplica"
       & "te-charts-removed-dry"">C8: Duplicate charts removed (DRY)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Charts gallery no longer repeats information shown on the Overview,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Proof and Tests tabs: the SPARK-proof donut (duplicated the Overview radar),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the tests pass/fail donut (duplicated the Overview Tests donut and the Tests"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gauge), the scope stacked bar (duplicated the polar ring) and the docstring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "radar (duplicated the Overview coverage donut).  Every chart in the dashboar"
       & "d"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now displays a distinct view of the data.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-terminal-colour-suppressed-in-ci""><a class=""header"" href=""#c9-ter"
       & "minal-colour-suppressed-in-ci"">C9: Terminal colour suppressed in CI</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>ANSI colour was enabled whenever <code>NO_COLOR</code> was unset, so colo"
       & "ur escapes could"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "garble logs on CI runners, which set <code>CI=true</code> but not <code>NO_C"
       & "OLOR</code>. Terminal"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "colour now additionally requires that <code>CI</code> is unset.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c10-american-english-in-live-docs-corrected""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#c10-american-english-in-live-docs-corrected"">C10: American English in live"
       & " docs corrected</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Prose Americanisms in the user documentation and API reference were corre"
       & "cted"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to British English (<code>behaviour</code> -&gt; <code>behaviour</code>, <co"
       & "de>analyse</code>/<code>analyse</code> -&gt;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>analyse</code>) in <code>docs/architecture.md</code>, <code>docs/provi"
       & "ng.md</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/compliance/HLR.md</code> and <code>docs/api-docs/adacovex-test-fo"
       & "rmat.md</code>.  Code"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "identifiers such as <code>prefers-color-scheme</code> and <code>NO_COLOR</co"
       & "de> are untouched.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-dev-dependencies-report-a-real-licence-version-and-source-url""><a"
       & " class=""header"" href=""#h1-dev-dependencies-report-a-real-licence-version-and"
       & "-source-url"">H1: Dev dependencies report a real licence, version and source "
       & "URL</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Before this release a dev dependency such as <code>gnatdoc_bin</code> app"
       & "eared in the SBOM"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as <code>NOASSERTION</code> licence, no version and no source.  <code>alr sh"
       & "ow</code> now supplies"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1</code>, version <code>26.0.0</"
       & "code> and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>https://github.com/AdaCore/gnatdoc</code> repository, so consumers can"
       & " identify and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "licence-scan the exact release.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-the-dependency-detail-popup-is-reachable-from-the-diagram-view""><"
       & "a class=""header"" href=""#h2-the-dependency-detail-popup-is-reachable-from-the"
       & "-diagram-view"">H2: The dependency detail popup is reachable from the diagram"
       & " view</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The detail popup previously lived inside the tree card, so it could not s"
       & "how"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "when the nomnoml diagram was the active view.  It now lives at the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>#tab-deps</code> level and serves any view; combined with the new clic"
       & "kable boxes an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "item can be selected from either view.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>973 tests passing across 14 categories (unchanged: the new dependency"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "enrichment integrates with the existing graph builder without changing the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fixture counts).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 724/724 VCs proved under gnatprove 16.1.0. 0 unproved, 0 justif"
       & "ied."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The new <code>Alr_Show_Crate</code> runs only for manifest-declared crates a"
       & "t graph-build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time and is outside the proof surface (the manifest parser body is not in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK_Mode On).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs. Coverage:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 dev-dep metadata via <code>alr show</code>, H1 real dev-dep"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "licence/version/source; SBOM spec gains <code>externalReferences</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>homepage</code> / Markdown <code>Source</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>RENDER-HTML</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C2 source links, C3 split layout, C4 diagram"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contrast/clicks, C5 chart text, C6 standards-aware compliance,"
