       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1330""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1330"">adacovex 1.33.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-28</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.32.0 -&gt; 1.33.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-test-scope-dependencies-sbom-and-dashboard""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c1-test-scope-dependencies-sbom-and-dashboard"">C1: Test-scope dependenci"
       & "es (SBOM and dashboard)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new <code>test</code> dependency scope joins <code>base</code>, <code>d"
       & "ev</code>, <code>transitive</code>, <code>vendored</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>system</code>.  A dependency is classified <code>test</code> when "
       & "it is used only by the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s tests:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>a crate declared under a <code>[[test-depends-on]]</code> section of <co"
       & "de>alire.toml</code> or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire-dev.toml</code> (the manifest label the parser picks up); or</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>a library with-claused only from a <strong>test project file</strong>: a"
       & " <code>.gpr</code> under a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tests/</code>, <code>test/</code> or <code>t/</code> directory, or a t"
       & "est-named project such as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>test_runner.gpr</code>.  The classification propagates to everything t"
       & "he test"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project pulls in transitively.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The scope is surfaced everywhere the others are: the SBOM"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex:dep_scope</code> property (<code>""test""</code>), the dashboar"
       & "d dependency tree"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "badge, the scope filter checkbox, the scope-stack legend, and the polar"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rings on the Overview and Charts tabs.  <code>Collect_GPR_Files</code> now c"
       & "ollects"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.gpr</code> files under <code>tests/</code>, which it previously skipp"
       & "ed, so test harness"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "projects resolve as dependencies in the first place.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-robust-version-probing-go-version-flag-fallbacks""><a class=""heade"
       & "r"" href=""#c2-robust-version-probing-go-version-flag-fallbacks"">C2: Robust ve"
       & "rsion probing (<code>go version</code>, flag fallbacks)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The version probe now runs <code>go version</code> for the <code>go</code"
       & "> tool (it accepted no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "flag before, so <code>go</code> always reported an empty version).  Probing "
       & "is robust"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "across tools: the probe tries the tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s configured flag first, then falls"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "back through <code>--version</code>, <code>-v</code> and <code>version</code"
       & ">, and takes the first successful"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run.  <code>fossil</code> and <code>git-lfs</code> keep their <code>version<"
       & "/code> subcommand; the fallbacks"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cover any tool whose configured flag fails.  Version tokens are cleaned:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>go version go1.21.5 ...</code> reports <code>1.21.5</code> (leading <c"
       & "ode>go</code> stripped, local"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build tags cut at <code>:</code>), and <code>node --version</code> reports <"
       & "code>26.7.0</code> instead of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>v26.7.0</code>.  The probe-file and tool-set cache namespaces were sal"
       & "ted (<code>.v2</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code>|tools-v3|</code>) so stale 1.32 probe results are never served.</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-alire-dependency-versions-resolved-via-alr-show""><a class=""header"
       & """ href=""#c3-alire-dependency-versions-resolved-via-alr-show"">C3: Alire depen"
       & "dency versions resolved via <code>alr show</code></a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>alr show</code> prints the release as <code>&lt;crate&gt;=&lt;versi"
       & "on&gt;: &lt;description&gt;</code> on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "first line and the licence under <code>License:</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " not the <code>Version:</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Licenses:</code> keys the resolver expected, so manifest-declared Alir"
       & "e crates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(gnatprove, gnatdoc_bin, gnatformat_bin, and any other <code>[[depends-on]]<"
       & "/code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "always reported an empty version and licence.  The <code>alire</code> ecosys"
       & "tem row now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "parses the first-line <code>&lt;crate&gt;=&lt;version&gt;</code> form for th"
       & "e version and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>License:</code> line for the licence.  The adacovex self-SBOM now reco"
       & "rds"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>gnatprove 16.1.0</code>, <code>gnatdoc_bin 26.0.0</code> and <code>gna"
       & "tformat_bin 26.0.0</code> (all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>dev</code> scope) instead of empty versions.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-hard-coded-vendored-library-table-removed-from-the-parser""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#c4-hard-coded-vendored-library-table-removed-from-the-par"
       & "ser"">C4: Hard-coded vendored-library table removed from the parser</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The parser no longer carries a hard-coded table mapping the bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard files to npm package names and versions (flexsearch 0.7.31,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "nomnoml 1.7.0, graphre 0.1.3, charts.css 1.2.0).  Vendored components are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now discovered from the data:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>the component name is the file"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own base name;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>the version is read from the file"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own banner comment when it carries one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(for example <code>FlexSearch.js v0.7.31 (Bundle)</code>);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>the licence and website are resolved live from the package registry unde"
       & "r"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that same name when the registry knows it (flexsearch, nomnoml, graphre);"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "an asset the registry does not know keeps a <code>pkg:generic</code> PURL an"
       & "d no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "guessed metadata.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The authored dashboard modules under <code>resources/css/</code> and <cod"
       & "e>resources/js/</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are never componentised: those directories hold the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own code, not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored packages.  The Credits tab keeps its curated table of the bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "libraries; the SBOM describes what is actually on disk.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-dashboard-search-finds-page-content""><a class=""header"" href=""#c5-"
       & "dashboard-search-finds-page-content"">C5: Dashboard search finds page content"
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The header search index was case-sensitive: queries were lowercased but t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "full-text index of each tab"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s rendered content was not, so page text such as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Orphan Tags"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " (or any HLR tag) could not be found.  The index is now folded"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to lowercase, so searching <code>orphan</code>, a package name, or an HLR ta"
       & "g finds the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tab that holds it.  Dependency names, versions, scopes, licences and PURLs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stay indexed as before.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c6-dependency-diagram-rendered-as-svg-with-real-clickable-nodes""><a "
       & "class=""header"" href=""#c6-dependency-diagram-rendered-as-svg-with-real-clicka"
       & "ble-nodes"">C6: Dependency diagram rendered as SVG with real clickable nodes<"
       & "/a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The nomnoml dependency diagram is now rendered as SVG (<code>nomnoml.rend"
       & "erSvg</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "instead of a bitmap canvas.  Every node is real geometry: each box (and its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "label) is clickable with its exact hitbox "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no manual canvas hit-testing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and no zoom-math drift "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and opens the same split-view detail panel as the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tree.  The diagram scales with its <code>viewBox</code>, so boxes are never "
       & "upside"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "down or clipped, long labels no longer overflow their boxes, and a wide"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "graph scrolls horizontally inside the card.  Hovering a node shows a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tooltip with the dependency name and version.  "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Download SVG"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " now"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "serialises the rendered SVG instead of rasterising the canvas.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-hand-rolled-charts-replace-the-vendored-chartscss""><a class=""head"
       & "er"" href=""#c7-hand-rolled-charts-replace-the-vendored-chartscss"">C7: Hand-ro"
       & "lled charts replace the vendored Charts.css</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s metrics charts no longer depend on the vendored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""https://chartscss.org/"">Charts.css</a> framework (<code>resources/c"
       & "harts.min.css</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the <code>charts-patch.css</code> overlay are deleted).  The Credits tab"
       & " and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES still credit Charts.css "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " as <strong>inspiration</strong> (MIT,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "not bundled): the dashboard ships its own patched, hand-rolled charts that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "borrow Charts.css"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s ring-and-segment visual language.  All six chart cards"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are now hand-rolled with plain CSS/SVG, which fixes the rendering problems"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the framework introduced:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Donuts</strong> (SPARK Proof, Tests Pass/Fail, Overview Tests, O"
       & "verview Doc"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Coverage) are conic-gradient rings with a CSS hole "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the same pattern"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as the polar ring.  The ring colour reflects the covered share: fully"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "green at 100% (previously every slice resolved to the same green,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so partial coverage never showed red), with green + red segments for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "partial coverage.  The centre hole carries the value and caption, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "because the ring is a fixed-size block (not an absolutely positioned"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table cell) the readout line below never overlaps the chart.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Proof Check Types</strong> and <strong>Test Results by Category<"
       & "/strong> are flex rows"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with a fixed, ellipsising label column and a track bar (green proved"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "share with a red unproved remainder for proof categories).  The old"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "column chart rotated its labels with a custom <code>rotate-labels</code> cla"
       & "ss"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that Charts.css does not define, which produced overlapping label"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "boxes and text overflow; the new rows never rotate and long category"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "names ellipsise instead of overflowing.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Overview tab"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Tests donut also keeps its readout line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>N passed, M failed</code> below the ring), so the pass/fail numbers s"
       & "tay"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "visible.  The charts remain dependency-free and follow the theme via CSS"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "variables.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-dashboard-htmlcssjs-modularised""><a class=""header"" href=""#c8-dash"
       & "board-htmlcssjs-modularised"">C8: Dashboard HTML/CSS/JS modularised</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The single authored <code>dashboard.js</code> and <code>dashboard.css</co"
       & "de> are split into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "per-concern modules under <code>resources/js/</code> (theme, tabs, deps, det"
       & "ails,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "nomnoml diagram, search) and <code>resources/css/</code> (base styles includ"
       & "ing the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hand-rolled donut/bar chart styles).  The page shell inlines each module"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "at its own placeholder; <code>tools/gen-dashboard.py</code> bundles them in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dependency order (vendored libraries first, then authored modules).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-test-labelled-vendored-dependencies-across-every-ecosystem""><a cl"
       & "ass=""header"" href=""#c9-test-labelled-vendored-dependencies-across-every-ecos"
       & "ystem"">C9: Test-labelled vendored dependencies across every ecosystem</a></h"
       & "3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>C1 classifies <code>test</code> scope from Alire manifests and test proje"
       & "ct files."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Vendored components (packages under <code>node_modules</code>, <code>vendor/"
       & "</code>, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "other vendored roots) are now classified <code>test</code> the same way, acr"
       & "oss every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "supported ecosystem:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Section labels</strong>: <code>package.json</code> sections whos"
       & "e key contains <code>test</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(for example <code>testDependencies</code> or <code>devTestDependencies</cod"
       & "e>), Cargo"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>[dev-dependencies]</code> (Cargo"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s native test-only section) plus any"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section containing <code>test</code>, composer"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>require-dev</code>, Gemfile"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>group :test</code> blocks, <code>pom.xml</code> <code>&lt;scope&gt;tes"
       & "t&lt;/scope&gt;</code> dependencies,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pyproject.toml</code> test extras and Poetry <code>[tool.poetry.group."
       & "test.*]</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "sections, and <code>Package.swift</code> dependencies declared inside a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>.testTarget(...)</code> block.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>The name heuristic</strong> (test pre/suffix): a component whose"
       & " name starts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or ends with the literal word <code>test</code> is test-labelled.  The heuri"
       & "stic"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now works across every ecosystem "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " not just npm "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " by checking the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "full name and then the last segment after any <code>/</code> or <code>:</cod"
       & "e>, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>@playwright/test</code>, <code>test-case</code>, <code>github.com/stre"
       & "tchr/testify</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>org.testng:testng</code> all match.  Ecosystems without a native test-"
       & "only"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section (<code>go.mod</code>, <code>requirements*.txt</code>) rely on this h"
       & "euristic.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Lockfiles</strong>: the name heuristic also applies to lockfile-"
       & "resolved"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "names "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code> / <code>package-lock.json</code> / <code>yarn.l"
       & "ock</code> next to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "an owner <code>package.json</code>, <code>Cargo.lock</code> crate names, and"
       & " <code>alire.lock</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "crates that the manifest sets leave transitive.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The e2e fixture"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>@playwright/test</code> is the canonical case: it stays a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>devDependencies</code> entry of <code>tests/e2e/package.json</code> (a"
       & "nd a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code> entry) and is classified <code>test</code> by na"
       & "me.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c10-overview-pairing-hoverable-scope-ring-scaled-proof-bars-wider-di"
       & "agram""><a class=""header"" href=""#c10-overview-pairing-hoverable-scope-ring-sc"
       & "aled-proof-bars-wider-diagram"">C10: Overview pairing, hoverable scope ring, "
       & "scaled proof bars, wider diagram</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Four dashboard layout improvements:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Overview row pairing</strong>: the <strong>Doc Coverage</strong>"
       & " donut and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>Dependency Scope</strong> ring now share one row (<code>chart-pair</"
       & "code>), so the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Overview uses its width better instead of stacking two full-width cards.</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Hoverable scope ring</strong>: every coloured segment of the dep"
       & "endency-scope"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rings (Overview and Charts) is a real SVG arc carrying a native tooltip"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with the scope name and its component count (for example <code>test: 3</code"
       & ">), and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the segment"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s opacity rises on hover.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Proof Check Types scaling</strong>: the proof-category bars now "
       & "scale with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the category"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s magnitude exactly like the test-category bars "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "track width is the category"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s share of the largest category, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "407-VC category reads as a longer bar than a 56-VC one (the green/red"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proved/unproved split stays inside the track).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Wider nomnoml diagram</strong>: the SVG now fills the width allo"
       & "cated to the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "diagram card (the space the dependency tree would use) instead of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shrinking to the graph"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s natural size, and centres horizontally inside"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the card; deep graphs still scroll.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Native suite grows to 1063 tests (14 categories).  The HTML/Markdown"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "renderer suite adds checks that the dashboard charts are hand-rolled:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "full and partial donut gradients (green at 100%, green+red split for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "partial proof), the bar-row label/track markup, proof-bar magnitude"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scaling (a smaller category"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s track is a percentage of the largest), the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>chart-pair</code> Overview row, the hoverable SVG scope ring with its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "per-segment <code>scope: count</code> tooltips, and that no <code>charts-css"
       & "</code> markup"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "remains in the served page.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>989 tests (was 973).  The SBOM generator suite gained 16 tests:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>[[test-depends-on]]</code> crates in the publishing and dev manife"
       & "sts are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "classified <code>Scope_Test</code> (base deps stay base);</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>a library with-claused only from a <code>tests/</code> harness project i"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Scope_Test</code> with a <code>pkg:gpr/libt</code> PURL;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>Scope_Property</code> maps every scope including <code>test</code>"
       & ".</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It then grew by a further 44 tests for the vendored test labels:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>@playwright/test</code> (test-named npm package) and a <code>testD"
       & "ependencies</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section package are <code>Scope_Test</code>; a <code>devDependencies</code>-"
       & "only package"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stays vendored;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Cargo <code>[dev-dependencies]</code>, Gemfile <code>group :test</code>,"
       & " Maven"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;scope&gt;test&lt;/scope&gt;</code>, pyproject <code>test</code> ex"
       & "tra, composer <code>require-dev</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and Package.swift <code>.testTarget</code> dependencies are <code>Scope_Test"
       & "</code>;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>the name heuristic across ecosystems: <code>github.com/stretchr/testify<"
       & "/code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(go.mod module path) and <code>test-case</code> (Cargo.lock crate) are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Scope_Test</code>;</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>lockfile-resolved names: <code>@playwright/test</code> via <code>pnpm-lo"
       & "ck.yaml</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>test_utils</code> via <code>alire.lock</code> are <code>Scope_Test</co"
       & "de> (an unlabelled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire.lock</code> crate stays transitive).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard e2e suite (22 tests) gained layout tests: the Overview"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Tests readout, page-content search (<code>orphan</code>), clickable SVG diag"
       & "ram"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "nodes, the test-scope filter checkbox, and the credits-table rows"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(Playwright as a test dependency, Charts.css credited for inspiration).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 723/723 VCs proved across 50 analysed units (unchanged at 1.33."
       & "0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the parser, cache and renderer changes are in default-off or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK-Mode-On-ensuring units; the new <code>test</code>-scope branches in th"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest parser and the renderer prove without new VCs).  Invocation:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex prove</code> (<code>--steps=10000</code>, gnatprove 16.1.0). "
       & " 0 unproved, 0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "justified.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>No new HLRs.  The manifest-scope work reuses <code>HLR-MANIFEST</code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>HLR-SBOM</code> (<code>src/parsers/adacovex-parsers-manifest.ads</code"
       & "> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>src/core/adacovex-types.ads</code>), the version probing reuses the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "system-tool discovery under <code>HLR-SBOM</code>, and the dashboard changes"
       & " reuse"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>HLR-RENDER-HTML</code> / <code>HLR-DASH</code> (<code>src/renderers/ad"
       & "acovex-renderers-html.ads</code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
