       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""adacovex-1380""><a class=""header"" href=""#adac"
       & "ovex-1380"">adacovex 1.38.0</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-30</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.37.0 -&gt; 1.38.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""changes""><a class=""header"" href=""#changes"">Changes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c1-manual-is-now-an-mdbook-project-with-a-read-the-docs-site""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#c1-manual-is-now-an-mdbook-project-with-a-read-the-docs-s"
       & "ite"">C1: Manual is now an mdBook project with a Read the Docs site</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The user documentation under <code>docs/</code> is now a proper <strong>m"
       & "dBook</strong> project:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>docs/book.toml</code> (with <code>src = "".""</code>) and a root <code>d"
       & "ocs/SUMMARY.md</code> table of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contents. Read the Docs builds the public manual from it (<code>.readthedocs"
       & ".yaml</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>mdbook build docs</code>), so the deployed site, the repository pages,"
       & " and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bundled offline manual all share one source of truth. The generated <code>do"
       & "cs/book/</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build output is now <strong>committed with the source</strong> (the <code>.g"
       & "itignore</code> entry was"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dropped), so <code>make book</code> keeps it in sync and the built site trav"
       & "els with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "repository. <code>make book-serve</code> serves the manual locally at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>http://localhost:8000</code>; <code>make docs-serve</code> keeps servi"
       & "ng the raw Markdown.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c2-bundled-offline-manual-served-at-docs""><a class=""header"" href=""#c"
       & "2-bundled-offline-manual-served-at-docs"">C2: Bundled offline manual served a"
       & "t /docs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>--serve</code> server now serves a <strong>bundled offline manu"
       & "al</strong> at <code>/docs</code> (both"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spellings, with and without the trailing slash, reach the same page)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/gen-docs.py</code> runs <code>mdbook build</code> over <code>doc"
       & "s/</code> at build time, inlines"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the generated <code>print.html</code> into one self-contained ASCII page, an"
       & "d bundles it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "into the binary as <code>src/adacovex-docs_template.ads</code> (regenerated "
       & "by"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make book</code>, which is also part of <code>make build</code>). Styl"
       & "esheets are inlined and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "external fonts and interactive scripts are dropped, so the page reads fully"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offline with no network or extra assets. The dashboard footer <strong>Manual"
       & "</strong> link"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the API playground"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>/docs</code> endpoint both open it, so a user on a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "machine without a network connection can still consult the manual.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c3-api-playground-endpoints-are-clickable-links""><a class=""header"" h"
       & "ref=""#c3-api-playground-endpoints-are-clickable-links"">C3: API playground en"
       & "dpoints are clickable links</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The API playground endpoint buttons now carry a real link on the endpoint"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "path: clicking the path opens the raw URL in a new tab, while clicking the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rest of the button still runs the endpoint live in the playground. JSON"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "responses that reference endpoint paths (for example the <code>/api/...</cod"
       & "e> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/badge/...</code> values in <code>/api/endpoints</code>) get those pat"
       & "hs linkified too, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "user can jump straight from a URL in the payload to the live endpoint. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "endpoint catalog now lists <code>/docs</code> as an <code>html</code> endpoi"
       & "nt.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c4-yace-token-colours-follow-the-pinned-theme""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#c4-yace-token-colours-follow-the-pinned-theme"">C4: yace token colours fo"
       & "llow the pinned theme</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The vendored yace highlighter"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s token colours are driven by the dashboard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--tok-*</code> CSS variables. The variables had a light default and a "
       & "dark"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)</code> block, but no explicit ligh"
       & "t override,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so a user who pinned the light theme on a dark OS still saw dark token"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "colours. The CSS now defines the token colours explicitly per theme"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>:root</code>, <code>[data-theme=""light""]</code>, <code>[data-theme=""d"
       & "ark""]</code>), so the highlighted"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JSON always matches the active dashboard theme, not the OS.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c5-complexity-check-skips-the-mdbook-build-output""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#c5-complexity-check-skips-the-mdbook-build-output"">C5: complexity-ch"
       & "eck skips the mdBook build output</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>complexity</code> subcommand"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s directory walk now skips <code>book</code> directories,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so the committed mdBook build output (<code>docs/book/</code>) is excluded f"
       & "rom the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source-quality scan. The build output contains minified single-line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JavaScript (the search index alone is a 1.4 MB line, far beyond the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Max_Line</code> buffer), which printed a spurious "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "line exceeds Max_Line buffer"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "error on every scan and, in constrained environments, could push the scan"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "into heap exhaustion. The gate now scans assessed source only, matching the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "existing <code>obj</code> / <code>bin</code> / <code>dist</code> / <code>bui"
       & "ld</code> exclusions.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c7-book-links-check-gate-keeps-the-committed-manual-in-sync""><a clas"
       & "s=""header"" href=""#c7-book-links-check-gate-keeps-the-committed-manual-in-syn"
       & "c"">C7: book-links-check gate keeps the committed manual in sync</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A new <code>make book-links-check</code> gate (wired into <code>make chec"
       & "k</code>, via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/check-book-links.py</code>) stops the committed mdBook build out"
       & "put"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>docs/book/</code>) from drifting from the <code>docs/</code> source. "
       & " It rebuilds the book"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from a temp copy of <code>docs/</code> and fails when the committed output d"
       & "iffers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "byte for byte.  It also verifies that every link inside the bundled offline"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manual resolves against the bundled assets or the deliberately-not-bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prefixes shared with <code>tools/gen-docs.py</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The manual is now <strong>complete</strong>: every page under <code>docs/"
       & "</code> (the 64"
