       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c8-mdbook-search-works-in-the-bundled-offline-manual""><a class=""head"
       & "er"" href=""#c8-mdbook-search-works-in-the-bundled-offline-manual"">C8: mdBook "
       & "search works in the bundled offline manual</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The bundled manual served at <code>/docs</code> is searchable <strong>off"
       & "line</strong> with mdBook"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "own search. In 1.38 the mdBook search machinery was dropped from the bundle"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(mdbook"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s elasticlunr search index is a multi-MB single blob that would"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overflow the gnatprove frontend as one Ada string constant) and the search"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "box was hidden, so the manual in the binary had no search. <code>tools/gen-d"
       & "ocs.py</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "now bundles the whole mdBook search stack "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code>elasticlunr</code>, <code>mark</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>searcher</code>, and the search index itself "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and keeps the search box visible."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The index is split into fixed-size chunks, each its own Ada constant (so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "no single constant exceeds the gnatprove limit), and the server streams the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "chunks back as one response when the page requests it, so no worker task"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "materialises a multi-megabyte body.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The search index is now committed with the rest of <code>docs/book</code>"
       & " so the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bundle stays deterministic. No parallel search index or widget: the search"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "button runs mdbook"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own code against mdbook"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own index, exactly like the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "online site.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c9-dashboard-shows-obvious-docs-links-and-a-split-api-view""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#c9-dashboard-shows-obvious-docs-links-and-a-split-api-view"""
       & ">C9: Dashboard shows obvious docs links and a split API view</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard header gains a prominent <strong>docs links bar</strong> be"
       & "low the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "title/actions and above the tab selection. The API playground is rearranged"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "into a split-screen layout (endpoint nav left, live response preview right),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the footer no longer carries the raw <code>/api/*</code> links or the <c"
       & "ode>?theme=</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "embed hint "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see H2.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c10-docs-reorganised-into-audience-folders""><a class=""header"" href="""
       & "#c10-docs-reorganised-into-audience-folders"">C10: Docs reorganised into audi"
       & "ence folders</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The manual pages now live in folders that mirror their audience, so the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "navigation shows the structure at a glance: <code>docs/usage/</code> holds t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "end-user guides (installation, CLI reference, dashboard, SBOM, standards,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "platforms, VCS, CI/CD, target projects), <code>docs/contributing/</code> hol"
       & "ds the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contributor and maintainer guides (developer guide, proving, architecture,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "requirements, performance, STE100, LLM usage), and the top level keeps the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "index plus the maintainer references (HLR/LLR, test report, credits,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "third-party notices) next to the <code>proof/</code>, <code>compliance/</cod"
       & "e>, <code>badges/</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>api-docs/</code>, and <code>changelogs/</code> outputs.  <code>docs/SU"
       & "MMARY.md</code> groups the TOC"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "into Getting started / Using adacovex / Contributing / Maintainer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "references, and every cross-link, README link, AGENTS.md doc-links entry,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>tools/doc-links.map</code>, <code>tools/rst2md.py</code> guide table, "
       & "and generated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>api-docs</code> page was updated in the same change.  The manual index"
       & " no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "longer carries the maintainer-only build and generated-output instructions;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "those moved to the developer guide (<code>docs/contributing/developer-guide."
       & "md</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so end-user pages stay focused on using adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""c11-maintainer-only-make-targets-scoped-out-of-end-user-docs""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#c11-maintainer-only-make-targets-scoped-out-of-end-user-d"
       & "ocs"">C11: Maintainer-only make targets scoped out of end-user docs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>End-user pages no longer reference <code>make</code>/dev targets: <code>c"
       & "i-cd.md</code> scopes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make action-parity-check</code>, <code>make coverage-gate</code>, <cod"
       & "e>make release</code>, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release workflow to the developer guide and swaps the debugging-guide"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make prove</code> for the user-facing <code>adacovex prove</code>; <co"
       & "de>installation.md</code> builds"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from source with <code>alr build</code> (the user-facing route) instead of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make build</code>; and <code>cli-reference.md</code> points contributo"
       & "rs at the developer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "guide instead of <code>make complexity-check</code>.  The action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own <code>alr build</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "steps remain, since they describe what the action does for the user.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""fixes""><a class=""header"" href=""#fixes"">Fixes</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h1-vendored-yacejs-now-appears-in-the-sbom""><a class=""header"" href="""
       & "#h1-vendored-yacejs-now-appears-in-the-sbom"">H1: Vendored yace.js now appear"
       & "s in the SBOM</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The vendored JavaScript bundles (<code>graphre.js</code>, <code>nomnoml.j"
       & "s</code>, <code>flexsearch.js</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>yace.js</code>) sat at the <code>resources/</code> root, but the vendo"
       & "red <code>yace.js</code> lived"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "under <code>resources/js/</code> with the authored dashboard modules. The SB"
       & "OM asset"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scanner treats <code>resources/js/</code> as authored dashboard code and ski"
       & "pped it, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "yace never became a dependency component. <code>yace.js</code> now sits at t"
       & "he"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>resources/</code> root with the other vendored libraries, the layout c"
       & "learly"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "separates dependency JavaScript from dashboard JavaScript, and the SBOM list"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "yace (MIT, v1.1.0, <code>pkg:generic/yace</code>) alongside the other bundle"
       & "d libraries.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h3-docs-subpages-are-served-again""><a class=""header"" href=""#h3-docs-"
       & "subpages-are-served-again"">H3: /docs subpages are served again</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>Docs_Subpath</code> slicing assumed the request path started at"
       & " index 1, but"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Get_Path</code> returns a slice of the request line, so every <code>/d"
       & "ocs/&lt;subpath&gt;</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "kept a leading slash and returned 404 "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " only <code>/docs</code> and <code>/docs/</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolved.  The six-character prefix is now stripped from the slice"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s actual"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "first index, so every page, stylesheet, and badge of the bundled manual"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "serves (an e2e test pins the exact, nested, and extensionless subpaths plus"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a missing-page 404).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h5-idle-connections-no-longer-pin-the-server-worker-pool""><a class="""
       & "header"" href=""#h5-idle-connections-no-longer-pin-the-server-worker-pool"">H5:"
       & " Idle connections no longer pin the server worker pool</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard server"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s fixed-size worker pool (4 workers) blocks each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "worker on the next request of a keep-alive connection.  Browsers hold"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "several idle connections open, so once all four workers were waiting on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "silent connections, the next request queued forever "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the e2e suite"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "started hitting 60-second timeouts on <code>/docs</code> subpages as it grew"
       & ".  Each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "accepted socket now carries a 5-second receive timeout, and a timed-out"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(or dropped) connection is closed in the worker"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s error path (which"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "previously leaked the socket).  A worker frees instead of pinning the pool f"
       & "orever,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the request is served.  (The timeout was originally 5s; H10 below"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shortens it to half a second so a multi-asset docs burst fans out across"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the pool instead of waiting one timeout per queued connection.)  The e2e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "suite returns to 28 passing in ~14 seconds.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h4-bundled-manual-no-longer-overflows-the-gnatprove-frontend""><a cla"
       & "ss=""header"" href=""#h4-bundled-manual-no-longer-overflows-the-gnatprove-front"
       & "end"">H4: Bundled manual no longer overflows the gnatprove frontend</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The complete-book offline manual is a 4 MB asset set, and <code>gen-docs."
       & "py</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "emitted it as one giant <code>&amp;</code>-concatenation chain (300k+ string"
       & " literals)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s frontend parses that tree fine, but gnatprove"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s flow analysis blew"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its stack (<code>Storage_Error stack overflow</code> at <code>adacovex-docs_"
       & "template.ads</code>),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "aborting <code>make prove</code> and therefore <code>make check</code> and e"
       & "very release."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Experiments showed the limit is the constant size itself (a single string"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "constant over ~1 MB overflows whatever its structure), so the generated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spec now holds one <code>aliased constant String</code> per asset (the multi"
       & "-MB"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "search index is split into fixed-size chunks, each its own constant "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " 166"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bodies in all), each well under the limit, never concatenated into one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "value "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " with an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Asset_Bodies</code> access-to-constant table and an <code>Asset_Index<"
       & "/code> subtype so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Content (Idx)</code> needs no unchecked bounds reasoning. The served b"
       & "ytes are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unchanged (each asset constant carries the identical content), the server"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "routes through the same <code>Find</code> lookup and streams the bodies (see"
       & " C8), and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the bundle-links check still passes.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h2-dashboard-docs-links-moved-from-the-footer-to-a-top-bar""><a class"
       & "=""header"" href=""#h2-dashboard-docs-links-moved-from-the-footer-to-a-top-bar"""
       & ">H2: Dashboard docs links moved from the footer to a top bar</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard no longer lists the raw <code>/api/*</code> URIs or the <co"
       & "de>?theme=</code> embed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hint in the footer. The footer now carries a single "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Generated by adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "line, and two obvious links "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <strong>Documentation (offline manual)</strong> (<code>/docs</code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <strong>Explore the API</strong> (jumps to the API tab) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " sit in a prominent bar at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the <strong>top of the page</strong>, below the dashboard title and above th"
       & "e tab"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "selection, where a user sees them immediately. The API playground is now a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>split-screen</strong> layout mirroring the Dependencies tab: endpoin"
       & "ts grouped by"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "purpose in a left-hand nav, live JSON/SVG/HTML response preview docked on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the right (stacking on narrow screens).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h6-mdbook-detected-as-a-system-dev-dependency""><a class=""header"" hre"
       & "f=""#h6-mdbook-detected-as-a-system-dev-dependency"">H6: mdbook detected as a "
       & "system dev dependency</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The SBOM"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s system-tool discovery now recognises <strong>mdbook</strong>: it joined th"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "curated <code>System_Tools</code> table, so a project whose build files refe"
       & "rence"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>mdbook</code> (for example a Markdown manual"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>mdbook build</code>) gets it registered"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as a <code>system</code>-scope dev dependency (<code>pkg:generic/mdbook</cod"
       & "e>). The detection"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stays data-driven "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adding a tool is one table entry, and the scan remains a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generic word-match over build files, not a hardcoded call site.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h7-read-the-docs-build-deploys-again""><a class=""header"" href=""#h7-re"
       & "ad-the-docs-build-deploys-again"">H7: Read the Docs build deploys again</a></"
       & "h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code>.readthedocs.yaml</code> build failed in CI with <code>mdbook: "
       & "not found</code> even"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "though <code>cargo install mdbook</code> succeeded. Read the Docs runs the i"
       & "nstall and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build jobs in separate shells, and cargo writes the binary into the Rust"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "toolchain"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s bin directory, which is not on the build job"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s PATH. The build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "command now resolves the cargo-installed <code>mdbook</code> binary (<code>f"
       & "ind</code> under"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>$HOME</code>) and prepends its directory to PATH before building, so t"
       & "he build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "survives Rust toolchain upgrades without a hardcoded version path.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h9-docs-search-result-links-resolve-again""><a class=""header"" href=""#"
       & "h9-docs-search-result-links-resolve-again"">H9: Docs search-result links reso"
       & "lve again</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Clicking an mdBook search result in the bundled manual returned 404.  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/docs</code> router dispatched on the query-string-stripped path (so <"
       & "code>?highlight=</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reached the docs route), but the asset lookup that followed read the <em>raw"
       & "</em>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "request path, so every search result carrying <code>?highlight=...</code> (m"
       & "dBook"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "mark-the-search-term parameter) was looked up as <code>changelogs/"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & ".html?highlight="
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and never found.  The docs asset key now derives from the query-stripped pat"
       & "h,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so a search-result link such as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/docs/usage/cli-reference.html?highlight=serve#--serve</code> resolves"
       & " to the page,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "then the browser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own fragment + mark handling scrolls to the heading and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "highlights the term "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " exactly as it does under <code>mdbook serve</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h10-docs-pages-load-quickly-again""><a class=""header"" href=""#h10-docs"
       & "-pages-load-quickly-again"">H10: Docs pages load quickly again</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The bundled manual felt slow to open: a ~15-asset page (HTML + several CS"
       & "S +"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JS) took roughly six seconds to load.  The 4-worker server pool pinned each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "worker to its keep-alive connection for a 5-second idle receive timeout, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "once four sockets were held by the browser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s parallel asset requests, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "remaining connections queued in the accept backlog for ~5s until a worker"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "released.  The idle timeout is now half a second: a worker that finishes a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "keep-alive exchange returns to <code>Accept_Socket</code> quickly, the burst"
       & " fan-outs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "across the pool, and a docs page loads in well under a second.  Workers are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "released faster on idle connections, which also means a stale or abandoned"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "connection is reaped sooner than before.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h11-offline-manual-subpages-drop-their-font-links""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#h11-offline-manual-subpages-drop-their-font-links"">H11: Offline manu"
       & "al subpages drop their font links</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>tools/gen-docs.py</code> dropped the bundling-irrelevant font style"
       & "sheet link from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "each bundled page, but its pattern only matched the index page"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>href=""fonts/"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "css""</code> shape.  Subpages link the same stylesheet with a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>path_to_root</code> prefix (<code>../fonts/"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "css</code>), so those kept the reference and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "browser issued a <code>/fonts/...css</code> 404 on every subpage.  The drop "
       & "now matches"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "any leading <code>../</code> prefix, so no bundled page references the unbun"
       & "dled font"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "asset.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""h8-hlr-tags-are-no-longer-read-from-string-literals""><a class=""heade"
       & "r"" href=""#h8-hlr-tags-are-no-longer-read-from-string-literals"">H8: HLR tags "
       & "are no longer read from string literals</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The source scanner extracted HLR traceability tags from <code>--</code> s"
       & "equences"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inside string literals, treating them as comment starts. The bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manual"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s generated constants embed examples such as <code>-- HLR-XXXX</code> in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "HTML and JS string data, so those examples registered as orphan source"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tags and the self-assessment fell to DAL-C Unmet. The scanner now tracks"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "string literals (including <code>""""</code> escapes) and only starts a commen"
       & "t at a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--</code> outside one; tags inside strings are data, not traces. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "self-assessment returns to DAL-C Achieved.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""test-suite""><a class=""header"" href=""#test-suite"">Test Suite</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The native suite grows from 1169 to 1173 tests. The server routing catego"
       & "ry"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adds four checks for the <code>/docs</code> and <code>/docs/</code> routes a"
       & "nd two near-miss paths"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>/docs2</code>, <code>/manual</code>) that must stay 404s. The scanner"
       & " category adds three"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks that a <code>-- HLR-*</code> string literal is not a source tag while"
       & " a real"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "comment tag after a string still is.  H9"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s query-string handling adds no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "native assertions (the routing table already pins <code>/docs</code> and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>Strip_Query</code> path), and H10"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s timeout is timing behaviour the suite"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot assert deterministically "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " both are covered manually and by the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard e2e suite.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>All 1173 tests pass (1176-1181 when mdbook is on PATH, depending on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "system-tool assertions in the SBOM category).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""proof-results""><a class=""header"" href=""#proof-results"">Proof Results"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Platinum, 0 unproved, 0 justified, 725 VCs (725 proved) under gnatprove"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "16.1.0 "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the total reported by <code>adacovex prove</code> and mirrored in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>/api/metrics</code>, the 16.1.0 proof ledger, and the self-assessment "
       & "docs. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manual-bundling, dashboard, and SBOM changes are build-time or I/O-bound"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "code that adds no analysed Ada, so the VC total stays at the Platinum bar."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The <code>Route</code> expression function gains one more <code>elsif</code>"
       & " for the <code>/docs/</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "trailing-slash spelling and remains proved by definition.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""traceability""><a class=""header"" href=""#traceability"">Traceability</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DOC</code> / <code>HLR-DASH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C1 mdBook manual + Read the Docs, C2 bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offline manual at <code>/docs</code>, C8 mdBook search in the bundle, C10 au"
       & "dience"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "folders, H2 docs links moved to the top bar, H7 Read the Docs build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "deploy, <code>tools/gen-docs.py</code>, and the <code>make book</code> targe"
       & "t.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-DASH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C3 API playground clickable links, C4 yace theme variables,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "C6 refreshed Charts preview + new API tab preview and the completed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dashboard walk-through, C9 the docs-links bar and split API view.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SBOM</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " H1 vendored yace.js in the SBOM, H6 mdbook as a system dev"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dependency, and the vendored/dashboard JavaScript layout separation.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-ARCH</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " C5 complexity-check <code>book</code> directory exclusion, C7 the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "book-links-check gate and the complete-book restructure, H4 the chunked"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "blob that keeps the bundled manual provable.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>HLR-SERVER</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " H3 the <code>Docs_Subpath</code> off-by-one fix, H5 the worker-pool"
       & ASCII.LF
