       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""performance""><a class=""header"" href=""#perfor"
       & "mance"">Performance</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex is a zero-dependency CLI. Its hot path is the assessment pipelin"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(scan -&gt; patch -&gt; doc metrics -&gt; proof parse -&gt; test parse -&gt;"
       & " DAL assess -&gt;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "render, plus the SBOM). This page documents how to benchmark it. It also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "documents the expected numbers on a typical machine and the optimisations"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that keep those numbers low.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""benchmarking""><a class=""header"" href=""#benchmarking"">Benchmarking</a"
       & "></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>make bench</code> benchmarks the assessment pipeline and reports bi"
       & "nary size:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>It builds the project, then times <code>./bin/adacovex</code> against th"
       & "e repo itself.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>cold</strong> runs (fresh result cache + probe cache) and <stron"
       & "g>warm</strong> runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(populated caches) are measured separately.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>make bench</code> uses <a href=""https://github.com/sharkdp/hyperfi"
       & "ne"">hyperfine</a> when"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "installed. It falls back to the bash <code>time</code> builtin otherwise. No"
       & " tooling is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "required.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>It samples generously so the reported mean is stable. Hyperfine runs <st"
       & "rong>10"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cold + 15 warm</strong> repetitions (2 warmup runs). Each cold repetition de"
       & "letes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the cache dir first. This measures a truly empty result and probe cache. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>time</code> fallback runs <strong>5 cold + 5 warm</strong>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>It reports the raw and stripped binary sizes (the stripped size is measu"
       & "red"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "on a <code>/tmp</code> copy; the build output is never modified).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Example output (hyperfine, x86-64, 8-core CI-class machine, 1.28.0):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>=== Cold (fresh result cache) ==="
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  Time (mean +/- sigma):  88.1 ms +/- 3.8 ms   [User: 62.1 ms, System: 14.0 "
       & "ms]"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  Range (min ... max):    84.8 ms ... 96.4 ms    10 runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "=== Warm (populated caches) ==="
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  Time (mean +/- sigma):  34.2 ms +/- 2.3 ms   [User: 15.3 ms, System: 8.7 m"
       & "s]"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  Range (min ... max):    30.9 ms ... 39.2 ms    15 runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "== Binary size =="
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bin/adacovex            9.0 MiB (9461040 bytes)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "after strip             4.3 MiB (4463704 bytes)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "savings                 52.8%"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The numbers shift with the machine and the codebase. What matters is the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shape: warm is now in the tens of milliseconds, and the cold path is bounded"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by the work that genuinely must happen (hashing the changed sources and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "building the SBOM).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For single-shot timings, plain <code>time</code> works the same way:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">time ./bin/adacovex --no-cache          # c"
       & "old, no result cache"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time ./bin/adacovex --cache-dir=/tmp/c  # warm"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When you compare two versions, always reset the cache between runs. Use"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--cache-dir=&lt;fresh dir&gt;</code> or delete the cache dir. The resu"
       & "lt cache must not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hide the real cost.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>make perf-bench</code> profiles CPU and syscalls directly with <cod"
       & "e>perf</code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>strace</code> over <code>bin/adacovex</code>. It prints the cache-miss"
       & " rates and the syscall"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "counts so a regression in I/O or data layout is visible before a release.</p"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""what-the-numbers-mean""><a class=""header"" href=""#what-the-numbers-mea"
       & "n"">What the numbers mean</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Figures below are from <code>make bench</code>/<code>perf-bench</code> on"
       & " this machine (hyperfine,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cold + warm, 2 warmup). They shift with the machine and the codebase. What"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "matters is the shape:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Cold ~0.1 s</strong>: dominated by source scanning (Ada file enu"
       & "meration and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SHA-256 of every scanned file), the SBOM tree walk and word scan, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "renderers. Nothing here can be skipped: the result cache is empty, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every file must be read and hashed at least once. The system-tool version"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "probes are <em>not</em> part of cold anymore (they live per-machine and are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cached across cache wipes).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Warm ~35 ms</strong>: the on-disk result cache (content-addresse"
       & "d per file,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "oldest-first eviction) skips re-parsing unchanged sources. The stamp"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fast-path skips the per-file SHA-256 entirely (a file unchanged in size is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "not re-hashed). The tools-set cache skips the whole SBOM dev-dependency"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "word scan and the tool probes for an unchanged project. The remaining"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time is process startup (dynamic loader hwcaps probing, elaboration), the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory walks, and the blob deserialization.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>System time is the tell. Cold runs show ~13 ms of system time (file I/O)"
       & ";"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "warm runs show ~9 ms.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""optimisation-history""><a class=""header"" href=""#optimisation-history"""
       & ">Optimisation history</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Kept in reverse-chronological order.  Every entry names the measurement t"
       & "hat"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "drove it so the next round of work can see whether the previous assumption"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "still holds.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""stamp-fast-path-hashing-1280""><a class=""header"" href=""#stamp-fast-pa"
       & "th-hashing-1280"">Stamp fast-path hashing (1.28.0)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The warm-path profile showed GNAT. SHA256 at ~48% of CPU: every <code>.ad"
       & "s</code> file was fully re-read and re-hashed on every run just to compute i"
       & "ts cache key, even though the content was unchanged. <code>Hash_File</code> "
       & "now keeps an in-memory map of path -&gt; (size, digest). A file whose size s"
       & "till matches the recorded size serves the recorded digest without opening or"
       & " reading the file. The fast path is used only within one process (the map is"
       & " not persisted), so a content change is always caught (the size differs or t"
       & "he map is empty).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The same fast path serves the SBOM tree-walk hashing, which re-hashes fil"
       & "es the source scan already touched in the same run (the two hash passes coll"
       & "apse into one real read + one size check). Warm user time dropped roughly a "
       & "third.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""stable-probe-store--probe-results-in-the-tools-blob-1280""><a class="""
       & "header"" href=""#stable-probe-store--probe-results-in-the-tools-blob-1280"">Sta"
       & "ble probe store + probe results in the tools blob (1.28.0)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The cold profile was dominated by the system-tool version probes: each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spawns a subprocess, and node/hg/mandb boot an interpreter (hg alone cost"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "~330 ms on this machine; the full probe set ~150 ms end to end). The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "probes were kept under the <em>result</em> cache (<code>&lt;cache-dir&gt;/pr"
       & "obes/</code>), so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "wiping the cache (or pointing <code>--cache-dir</code> elsewhere) re-probed "
       & "every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tool.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Two changes removed that cost:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Probes now live in <code>~/.adacovex/probes/</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a stable, machine-level"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "store external to the result cache. Wiping the result cache (or using a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fresh <code>--cache-dir</code>) no longer re-probes; only the 7-day TTL ever"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "re-probes a known toolchain. Cold on a warm-probe machine dropped from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "~658 ms to ~86 ms (7.7 x).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The tools-set cache blob now also stores each referenced tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s probe"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "result (<code>tool=version</code> pairs), and a cache hit rebuilds the SBOM "
       & "tool"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "edges from those pairs without PATH lookups, probe file reads, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprocess spawns. Warm dropped from ~39.8 ms to ~34.6 ms. The blob"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "format is names-<code>|</code>-version-pairs; <code>Cache_Schema</code> was "
       & "bumped to s6 so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "old names-only blobs are never served as if complete. Cold and warm"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SBOM output stays byte-identical.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""file-stamp-fast-path-and-eviction-batching-1270""><a class=""header"" h"
       & "ref=""#file-stamp-fast-path-and-eviction-batching-1270"">File-stamp fast-path "
       & "and eviction batching (1.27.0)</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>Put_Cached</code> ran eviction after every store; eviction walks th"
       & "e whole cache"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tree. It now runs every 32 stores (bounded overshoot under the soft cap)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The SBOM dev-dependency word scan was rewritten from a per-tool substring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "match (60 tools x line length) to a single-pass word extraction (per-word x"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "distinct tool lengths), and tool-output directories (<code>gnatprove/</code>"
       & ","
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>__pycache__</code>, <code>node_modules</code>, <code>.headroom</code>,"
       & " <code>.lccst</code>) were excluded from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "both tree walks so the proof-run output is not enumerated. Those changes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "alone took the warm run from ~1.02 s to ~63 ms (16x) and cold from ~1.4 s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to ~545 ms, and reduced the warm-run syscall count from ~15k to ~12k.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""probe-cache""><a class=""header"" href=""#probe-cache"">Probe cache</a></"
       & "h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><em>(Origin story.)</em> The SBOM builds a <em>dev-scope</em> dependency "
       & "edge for every tool that the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s build references. The tool must be installed on <code>$PATH</code> (for ex"
       & "ample <code>gcc</code>, <code>alr</code>, <code>git</code>, <code>make</code"
       & ">). The SBOM probes each tool with <code>&lt;tool&gt; &lt;flag&gt;</code> to"
       & " capture its version. Each probe spawns a subprocess.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The subprocess costs tens of milliseconds per referenced tool (<code>Syst"
       & "em: 42 ms -&gt; 9 ms</code>, ~150 ms end to end on an 11-tool toolchain). Or"
       & "iginally the probed versions were cached under <code>&lt;cache-root&gt;/prob"
       & "es/&lt;tool&gt;</code> with a 7-day TTL. That location meant a wiped result "
       & "cache re-probed every tool on the next run "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " which is why 1.28.0 moved the store and folded the probe results into the t"
       & "ools-set cache blob (see above).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""binary-size""><a class=""header"" href=""#binary-size"">Binary size</a></"
       & "h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The debug-symbol-carrying build is ~9 MiB. Stripping (<code>strip bin/ada"
       & "covex</code>) yields ~3.6 MiB (~60% smaller) without affecting behaviour. GN"
       & "AT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default build keeps symbols for debugging (<code>gdb</code> works). Releas"
       & "e artifacts are stripped. <code>make bench</code> always reports both.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Regressions in code size are visible in the same command that reports tim"
       & "ings. If the symbols ever come out, the binary size is the same and the page"
       & " should say so.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""ci""><a class=""header"" href=""#ci"">CI</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>CI runs the self-assessment with result caching disabled where determinis"
       & "m matters (<code>--no-cache</code>-equivalent fresh dirs). The <code>make</c"
       & "ode> gates are timed loosely. Timings are informational only. The <code>benc"
       & "h</code> target is not part of <code>make check</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It makes the gate machine-dependent. A slow CI runner must not fail a bui"
       & "ld. The target is run by hand before releases.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""when-the-numbers-regress""><a class=""header"" href=""#when-the-numbers-"
       & "regress"">When the numbers regress</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Run <code>make perf-bench</code> first. It reports the CPU break-down (th"
       & "e wall-clock"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>perf</code> output) and the strace syscall counts. The single-reader/s"
       & "ingle-writer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cache walks are the usual suspects: a new tree walk that re-enumerates a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory which a cache already covers, or a new per-file hash that the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stamp fast path does not cover. The numbers in this page are from the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "self-assessment; the Ada_CRDT target is smaller and exercises the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pipeline, so <code>make run-ada-crdt</code> is a handy second datapoint.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
