       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""ste100-technical-names-for-adacovex""><a clas"
       & "s=""header"" href=""#ste100-technical-names-for-adacovex"">STE100 Technical Name"
       & "s for adacovex</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English (Section 1, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Words"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ") defines a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "controlled vocabulary. Most words in that vocabulary are standard STE words."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Some concepts have no accurate standard STE word. For those concepts, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project approves a <strong>Technical Name (TN)</strong>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A Technical Name is a non-STE word that the project explicitly approves. "
       & "The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project approves it because no standard STE word describes the concept with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the same precision. A TN has a single mandatory part of speech and a defined"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scope. The scope is restricted to the software domain of adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>This page is the controlled list of Technical Names for adacovex. Writers"
       & " of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "user documentation, API documentation, docstrings, and changelogs must use"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "these terms as defined here. If you need a term that is not in this list,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "add it to the list first, then use it.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""categories-for-ada-technical-names""><a class=""header"" href=""#categor"
       & "ies-for-ada-technical-names"">Categories for Ada Technical Names</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Group the Technical Names by their structural role in the software domain"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Hardware and System Entities.</strong> Physical components, buse"
       & "s, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "microarchitectures that the Ada code interacts with. For example, CPU core.<"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Ada Language Constructs.</strong> Specific language features tha"
       & "t generic"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "English words cannot replace without losing technical precision. For"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "example, pragma, discriminant, rendezvous, task.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Domain and Mathematical Terms.</strong> Algorithmic, mathematica"
       & "l, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "mission-specific logic terms. For example, telemetry, checksum,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "quaternion.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Code Identifier Names.</strong> Exact package, type, subtype, su"
       & "bprogram, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "variable names as declared in the source code. For example,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>System.Storage_Elements</code>, <code>Buffer_Size</code>. This categor"
       & "y also covers exact"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "file names, tool commands, and flag names that appear in documentation.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""required-data-fields-for-each-entry""><a class=""header"" href=""#requir"
       & "ed-data-fields-for-each-entry"">Required data fields for each entry</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>ASD-STE100 requires strict controls over how approved words are documente"
       & "d."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Every Technical Name in this dictionary has all five fields:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><strong>Approved Word (TN)</strong></td><td>The exact word or identi"
       & "fier.</td><td><strong>Pragma</strong></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><strong>Part of Speech</strong></td><td>STE permits a word as only <"
       & "em>one</em> part of speech (Noun, Verb, Modifier).</td><td>Noun</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><strong>Approved Meaning / Definition</strong></td><td>Clear, unambi"
       & "guous definition restricted to the adacovex domain.</td><td>A compiler direc"
       & "tive in the Ada programming language.</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><strong>Non-Approved Alternatives</strong></td><td>Terms that author"
       & "s must NOT use instead of this TN.</td><td><em>Compiler directive</em>, <em>"
       & "Annotation</em></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><strong>Example Sentence</strong></td><td>A compliant STE sentence d"
       & "emonstrating usage.</td><td><em>Add the <strong>pragma</strong> to the top o"
       & "f the package specification.</em></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""key-rules-for-ada-technical-names""><a class=""header"" href=""#key-rule"
       & "s-for-ada-technical-names"">Key rules for Ada Technical Names</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Nouns stay nouns.</strong> Technical Names are almost always app"
       & "roved as Nouns"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or Modifiers. Never approve a code action as a verb if a standard STE verb"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exists. For example, use the approved verb <em>Calculate</em> instead of cre"
       & "ating"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a TN verb <em>Compute</em>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Exact case matching.</strong> Treat Ada identifiers (<code>Pasca"
       & "l_Case</code> or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>UPPER_CASE</code>) as literal Technical Names. Use the exact casing in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "documentation. This rule distinguishes language concepts from code"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entities.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>No synonyms.</strong> If the project approves <em>Task</em> as a"
       & " TN for an Ada"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "concurrent execution unit, do not use words like <em>Thread</em>, <em>Proces"
       & "s</em>, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<em>Job</em> for that concept.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>One part of speech per word.</strong> A TN is a Noun or a Modifi"
       & "er, never both."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "When you need the action, use the standard STE verb that matches the noun"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "form.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""standard-entry-template""><a class=""header"" href=""#standard-entry-tem"
       & "plate"">Standard entry template</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-markdown"">### Technical Name: Task"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "- **Part of Speech:** Noun"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "- **Category:** Ada Language Construct"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "- **Definition:** A standalone unit of concurrent execution in Ada."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "- **Approved Form:** Task (singular), Tasks (plural)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "- **Do Not Use:** Thread, Process, Job, Execution Unit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "- **Correct Example:** *The main **task** waits for the sensor **task** to f"
       & "inish.*"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "- **Incorrect Example:** *The main process waits for the sensor thread to co"
       & "mplete.*"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""dictionary""><a class=""header"" href=""#dictionary"">Dictionary</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""category-ada-language-constructs""><a class=""header"" href=""#category-"
       & "ada-language-constructs"">Category: Ada Language Constructs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-package""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-pack"
       & "age"">Technical Name: Package</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A named collection of related declarations "
       & "in Ada. A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package has a visible specification and a private body.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Package (singular), Packages (plural)</l"
       & "i>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Module, Library unit, Component</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>A <strong>package</strong> groups "
       & "the related subprograms.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>A module groups the related subp"
       & "rograms.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-package-body""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name"
       & "-package-body"">Technical Name: Package Body</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The implementation part of a package. It co"
       & "ntains the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bodies of the subprograms that the package specification declares.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Package Body (singular), Package Bodies "
       & "(plural)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Implementation file, Source file (when ambi"
       & "guous)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <strong>package body</strong> "
       & "implements the declared subprograms.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The implementation file implemen"
       & "ts the declared subprograms.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-specification""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-nam"
       & "e-specification"">Technical Name: Specification</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The visible declaration part of a package o"
       & "r subprogram."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "In Ada, the specification is the <code>.ads</code> file of a package.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Specification (singular), Specifications"
       & " (plural)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Header, Interface file, Definition</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The package <strong>specification<"
       & "/strong> declares the public subprograms.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The package header declares the "
       & "public subprograms.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-subprogram""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-s"
       & "ubprogram"">Technical Name: Subprogram</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A named unit of executable code in Ada. A s"
       & "ubprogram is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "either a procedure or a function.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Subprogram (singular), Subprograms (plur"
       & "al)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Routine, Method, Function (for the general "
       & "concept)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>Every <strong>subprogram</strong> "
       & "in the source tree has a docstring.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>Every routine in the source tree"
       & " has a docstring.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-procedure""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-pr"
       & "ocedure"">Technical Name: Procedure</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A subprogram that performs an action and do"
       & "es not return a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "value.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Procedure (singular), Procedures (plural"
       & ")</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Routine, Operation</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <strong>procedure</strong> wri"
       & "tes the report to a file.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The routine writes the report to"
       & " a file.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-function""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-fun"
       & "ction"">Technical Name: Function</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A subprogram that returns a value.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Function (singular), Functions (plural)<"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Method, Callable</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <strong>function</strong> retu"
       & "rns the number of cores.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The method returns the number of"
       & " cores.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-task""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-task"">T"
       & "echnical Name: Task</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A unit of concurrent execution in the Ada l"
       & "anguage.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Task (singular), Tasks (plural)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Thread, Process, Job, Execution Unit</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The HTTP server runs a pool of fou"
       & "r <strong>tasks</strong>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The HTTP server runs a pool of f"
       & "our threads.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-pragma""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-pragm"
       & "a"">Technical Name: Pragma</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A compiler directive in the Ada programming"
       & " language.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Pragma (singular), Pragmas (plural)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Compiler directive, Annotation, Attribute</"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <strong>pragma</strong> <code>"
       & "SPARK_Mode</code> enables SPARK analysis.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The compiler directive <code>SPA"
       & "RK_Mode</code> enables SPARK analysis.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-aspect""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-aspec"
       & "t"">Technical Name: Aspect</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A declaration-level property in Ada 2012 th"
       & "at attaches"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contracts to a declaration. Examples are <code>Pre</code>, <code>Post</code>"
       & ", and <code>Global</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Aspect (singular), Aspects (plural)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Property, Annotation, Attribute</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <strong>aspect</strong> <code>"
       & "Pre</code> states the precondition.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The property <code>Pre</code> st"
       & "ates the precondition.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-contract""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-con"
       & "tract"">Technical Name: Contract</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The set of preconditions, postconditions, a"
       & "nd global"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dependencies that describe subprogram behaviour for the proof tool.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Contract (singular), Contracts (plural)<"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Agreement, Promise, Guarantee</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>gnatprove proves the <strong>contr"
       & "acts</strong> of every subprogram.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>gnatprove proves the guarantees "
       & "of every subprogram.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-generic""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-gene"
       & "ric"">Technical Name: Generic</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Modifier</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A unit that is parameterised and that a cal"
       & "ler instantiates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with actual parameters. Used with the nouns package, subprogram, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "procedure.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Generic (as modifier only)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Template, Parameterised unit (as a noun)</l"
       & "i>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>A <strong>generic</strong> package"
       & " instantiates a vector type.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>A template package instantiates "
       & "a vector type.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-type""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-type"">T"
       & "echnical Name: Type</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A named set of values and the operations on"
       & " those values in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Type (singular), Types (plural)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Datatype, Data type (when the Ada type is m"
       & "eant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <strong>type</strong> <code>IR"
       & "_Int32</code> is a bounded integer type.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The datatype <code>IR_Int32</cod"
       & "e> is a bounded integer type.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-object""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-objec"
       & "t"">Technical Name: Object</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A variable or constant that has a type in A"
       & "da.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Object (singular), Objects (plural)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Instance (when the Ada object is meant), Va"
       & "riable (when a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "constant is also possible)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The proof checks that every <stron"
       & "g>object</strong> is initialised.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The proof checks that every inst"
       & "ance is initialised.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-spark""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-spark"""
       & ">Technical Name: SPARK</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The formally analysable subset of Ada that "
       & "the gnatprove"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof tool verifies. adacovex targets the Platinum SPARK level.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> SPARK (exact capitals)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Spark, spark, Ada subset (when SPARK is mea"
       & "nt)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The source is written in <strong>S"
       & "PARK</strong> and proved with gnatprove.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The source is written in Spark a"
       & "nd proved with gnatprove.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""category-domain-and-mathematical-terms""><a class=""header"" href=""#cat"
       & "egory-domain-and-mathematical-terms"">Category: Domain and Mathematical Terms"
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-verification-condition-vc""><a class=""header"" href=""#t"
       & "echnical-name-verification-condition-vc"">Technical Name: Verification Condit"
       & "ion (VC)</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A logical statement that a proof tool must "
       & "prove. gnatprove"
