       & "e (when the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest is meant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <strong>manifest</strong> decl"
       & "ares the gnatprove dependency.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The configuration file declares "
       & "the gnatprove dependency.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-alirelock""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-al"
       & "irelock"">Technical Name: alire.lock</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The solved dependency list that Alire write"
       & "s. It records"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the exact versions of every resolved crate.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> alire.lock (exact file name)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Lock file (when alire.lock is meant), Depen"
       & "dency file</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The parser reads <strong>alire.loc"
       & "k</strong> to build the dependency graph.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The parser reads the lock file t"
       & "o build the dependency graph.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-gnat-project-file-gpr""><a class=""header"" href=""#techn"
       & "ical-name-gnat-project-file-gpr"">Technical Name: GNAT Project File (.gpr)</a"
       & "></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A build description file with the <code>.gp"
       & "r</code> extension. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof run targets the root <code>.gpr</code> file of the target project.</li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> GNAT Project File (singular), .gpr (abbr"
       & "eviation)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Project file (when the .gpr file is meant),"
       & " Build file</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>gnatprove runs against the root <s"
       & "trong>.gpr</strong> file.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>gnatprove runs against the root "
       & "build file.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-gnatproveout""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name"
       & "-gnatproveout"">Technical Name: gnatprove.out</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The output file that gnatprove writes. It c"
       & "ontains the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof summary and the VC counts. The assessment pipeline parses it.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> gnatprove.out (exact file name)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Proof output (when the file is meant), The "
       & "out file</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The parser reads <code>obj/gnatpro"
       & "ve/gnatprove.out</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The parser reads the proof outpu"
       & "t file.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-aunit""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-aunit"""
       & ">Technical Name: AUnit</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The Ada unit-test framework. The test-resul"
       & "t parser reads"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "AUnit output.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> AUnit</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Test framework (when AUnit is meant), Test "
       & "suite (when the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "framework is meant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The native tests run under <strong"
       & ">AUnit</strong>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The native tests run under the t"
       & "est framework.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-spark_mode""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-s"
       & "park_mode"">Technical Name: SPARK_Mode</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The Ada pragma or aspect that enables SPARK"
       & " analysis for a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unit. Use the exact spelling with the underscore.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> SPARK_Mode (exact spelling)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> SPARK mode, Spark_Mode, Spark mode</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The package declares <code>SPARK_M"
       & "ode =&gt; On</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The package declares SPARK mode "
       & "on.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-hlr-tag""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-hlr-"
       & "tag"">Technical Name: HLR Tag</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> A source comment of the form <code>-- HLR-X"
       & "XXX</code> that traces a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source element to a high-level requirement.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> HLR Tag (singular), HLR Tags (plural), H"
       & "LR-XXXX (the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tag form)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Tag (when the HLR tag is meant), Annotation"
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The subprogram carries the <strong"
       & ">HLR tag</strong> <code>-- HLR-ARCH</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The subprogram carries the annot"
       & "ation <code>-- HLR-ARCH</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-cyclonedx""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-cy"
       & "clonedx"">Technical Name: CycloneDX</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The SBOM exchange schema that adacovex uses"
       & " for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CycloneDX 1.5 JSON SBOM format.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> CycloneDX (exact form)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Cyclonedx, Cyclone DX, SBOM format (when Cy"
       & "cloneDX is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "meant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <code>sbom</code> subcommand e"
       & "mits <strong>CycloneDX</strong> 1.5 JSON.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The sbom subcommand emits Cyclon"
       & "e DX 1.5 JSON.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-spdx""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-spdx"">T"
       & "echnical Name: SPDX</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The software package data exchange schema t"
       & "hat adacovex"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "uses for the SPDX 2.3 JSON SBOM format.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> SPDX (exact capitals)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Spdx, spdx, License schema (when SPDX is me"
       & "ant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The <code>sbom</code> subcommand a"
       & "lso emits <strong>SPDX</strong> 2.3 JSON.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The sbom subcommand also emits S"
       & "pdx 2.3 JSON.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-ansi""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-ansi"">T"
       & "echnical Name: ANSI</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Modifier</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The escape-code standard used for colour ou"
       & "tput in a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "terminal. Always use it with the noun codes.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> ANSI (as modifier, for example ANSI esca"
       & "pe codes)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Terminal codes, Colour codes</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The report uses <strong>ANSI</stro"
       & "ng> escape codes for colour.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The report uses terminal codes f"
       & "or colour.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-no_color""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-no_"
       & "color"">Technical Name: NO_COLOR</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The environment variable that disables colo"
       & "ur output. When"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "it is set, the ANSI report prints without colour.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> NO_COLOR (exact capitals)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> No color variable, The colour switch (when "
       & "the variable is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "meant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The report honours the <strong>NO_"
       & "COLOR</strong> environment variable.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The report honours the No color "
       & "environment variable.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-gnatformat""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-g"
       & "natformat"">Technical Name: gnatformat</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The GNAT source formatter. The <code>make f"
       & "mt</code> target runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatformat on the Ada sources.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> gnatformat (exact lower-case)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Formatter (when gnatformat is meant), Gnat "
       & "format</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em><code>make fmt</code> runs <strong"
       & ">gnatformat</strong> on the sources.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em><code>make fmt</code> runs the f"
       & "ormatter on the sources.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-verification-report""><a class=""header"" href=""#technic"
       & "al-name-verification-report"">Technical Name: Verification Report</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The generated report file <code>VERIFICATIO"
       & "N.md</code>. It records the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "assessment results of the target project.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Verification Report (singular), VERIFICA"
       & "TION.md (the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "file name)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Report file (when VERIFICATION.md is meant)"
       & ", Assessment"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "report (after the first use)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The renderer writes the <strong>ve"
       & "rification report</strong> to <code>VERIFICATION.md</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The renderer writes the report f"
       & "ile to <code>VERIFICATION.md</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-traceability-matrix""><a class=""header"" href=""#technic"
       & "al-name-traceability-matrix"">Technical Name: Traceability Matrix</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The generated report file <code>TRACE.md</c"
       & "ode>. It maps every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "high-level requirement to the source elements that implement it.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Traceability Matrix (singular), TRACE.md"
       & " (the file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "name)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Trace table, Mapping file (when TRACE.md is"
       & " meant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The renderer writes the <strong>tr"
       & "aceability matrix</strong> to <code>TRACE.md</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The renderer writes the mapping "
       & "file to <code>TRACE.md</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-timezone""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-tim"
       & "ezone"">Technical Name: Timezone</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The named region or fixed offset that defin"
       & "es local time"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for the operator.  It includes IANA names (for example <code>Asia/Singapore<"
       & "/code>)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and fixed UTC/GMT offsets (for example <code>UTC+8</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Timezone (singular), Timezones (plural)<"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Time zone (two words), Zone (when Timezone "
       & "is meant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The report shows the time in the o"
       & "perator"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <strong>timezone</strong>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The report shows the time in the"
       & " operator"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s time zone.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-utc""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-utc"">Tec"
       & "hnical Name: UTC</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The coordinated universal time standard.  I"
       & "t is the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "zero-offset reference that adacovex uses to display fixed offsets.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> UTC (exact capitals)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Universal time, Greenwich Mean Time (when U"
       & "TC is meant)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>The report shows the offset as <co"
       & "de>UTC+08:00</code>.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>The report shows the offset in u"
       & "niversal time.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-gmt""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-gmt"">Tec"
       & "hnical Name: GMT</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The Greenwich mean time standard.  adacovex"
       & " accepts <code>GMT</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as a synonym for <code>UTC</code> in fixed offset values.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> GMT (exact capitals)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Greenwich time, London time</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em><code>GMT+8</code> is a valid fixe"
       & "d offset value.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em><code>Greenwich time +8</code> i"
       & "s a valid fixed offset value.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4 id=""technical-name-iana""><a class=""header"" href=""#technical-name-iana"">T"
       & "echnical Name: IANA</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Modifier</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Definition:</strong> The Internet Assigned Numbers Authority.  A"
       & "lways use it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with the noun name to mean the tz database zone identifiers.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Approved Form:</strong> IANA (exact capitals, as modifier, for e"
       & "xample IANA"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "name)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Olson, tz database (as a modifier)</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em><code>Asia/Singapore</code> is an "
       & "<strong>IANA</strong> name.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em><code>Asia/Singapore</code> is a"
       & " tz database name.</em></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
