       & "ve"":true,""docs"":{""0"":{""body"":""This page is the index for all adacovex docume"
       & "ntation. Pick a section\\nrelevant to you, or read the pages in the order be"
       & "low. All documentation uses British English and ASD-STE100 Simplified Techni"
       & "cal\\nEnglish. The controlled Technical Names dictionary lives in STE100 Tec"
       & "hnical Names. Use it\\nbefore you use a technical word in any doc, docstring"
       & ", or changelog."",""breadcrumbs"":""Adacovex manual "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex Documentation"",""id"":""0"",""title"":""adacovex Documentation""},""1"":{""bo"
       & "dy"":""Installation "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " install the binary or the GitHub\\nAction. Target projects "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " what a target project must\\ncontain."",""breadcrumbs"":""Adacovex manual "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Getting started"",""id"":""1"",""title"":""Getting started""},""10"":{""body"":""git clon"
       & "e --depth 1 https://github.com/bladeacer/adacovex.git\\ncd adacovex && alr b"
       & "uild # or: --branch vX.Y.Z for a released tag alr build produces bin/adacove"
       & "x (with a bin/covex alias). A stock Alire\\ntoolchain ( gnat_native + gprbui"
       & "ld) plus the standard GNAT runtime is all\\nthat is needed. No other depende"
       & "ncies. (Contributors use the richer make build workflow; see the developer g"
       & "uide.)"",""breadcrumbs"":""Installing adacovex "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Building from source"",""id"":""10"",""title"":""Building from source""},""100"":{""bod"
       & "y"":""The served dashboard ( --serve) and the proof-aware SBOM both record the"
       & " assessment standard and its native level\\nlabel, so a browser or a Cyclone"
       & "DX / SPDX / Markdown consumer sees the right\\nname for the selected standar"
       & "d.\\nLike the sbom subcommand, --serve defaults to all standards when no --s"
       & "tandard / --asil / --class flag is given. The dashboard renders\\nevery stan"
       & "dard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s level at the shared tier. An explicit standard flag\\nnarrows it. The SBOM"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s adacovex:standard / adacovex:level properties: -- flag adacovex:standard a"
       & "dacovex:level --dal=C DO-178C DAL-C --asil=B ISO 26262 ASIL B --class=A IEC "
       & "62304 Class A --standard=all DO-178C, ISO 26262, IEC 62304 DAL-C / ASIL B / "
       & "Class A The adacovex:dal_target property always carries the shared tier ( DA"
       & "L-A.. DAL-D) regardless of the labelling standard. --standard=all joins all\"
       & "\nthree standard names and level labels into the single adacovex:standard an"
       & "d adacovex:level properties. One document carries every standard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s\\nassessment."",""breadcrumbs"":""Compliance Standards (DO-178C / ISO 26262 / "
       & "IEC 62304) "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Dashboard and SBOM standard-awareness"",""id"":""100"",""title"":""Dashboard and SB"
       & "OM standard-awareness""},""1000"":{""body"":""The --serve dashboard now renders fo"
       & "ur live charts (vendored Charts.css v1.2.0, MIT): SPARK proof donut "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " proved vs unproved VCs; Test results bar chart "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " per-category pass counts; Proof check-types bar chart "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " proved checks per check kind; Docstring coverage bar chart "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " documented vs undocumented\\nsubprograms per unit. Charts.css is vendored a"
       & "s resources/charts.min.css and inlined into the self-contained dashboard tem"
       & "plate ( resources/dashboard.html), so the dashboard keeps its zero-dependenc"
       & "y, single-file, offline-serving property "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no CDN, no network. The chart cards are generated by the new Renderers. HTM"
       & "L. Render_Charts and injected through the template"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s __CHARTS__ placeholder. Charts update live with the metrics (the JSON API "
       & "below feeds the same data the dashboard shows). See docs/dashboard.md and do"
       & "cs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md."",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.19.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " C1: dashboard charts powered by Charts.css"",""id"":""1000"",""title"":""C1: dashbo"
