       & " Changes"",""id"":""1028"",""title"":""Changes""},""1029"":{""body"":""Vendored dependenci"
       & "es can now participate in the SPARK proof without\\nmodifying their sources."
       & " The same .adacovex/patches/<relative-path> file\\nthat overlays docstrings "
       & "can carry proof aspects: a patch containing any\\nof SPARK_Mode, Pre =>, Pos"
       & "t =>, or Global => is detected by the new Adacovex.Prove_Patch.Has_Proof and"
       & " becomes a proof patch; a docstring-only\\npatch keeps working as a pure ove"
       & "rlay and never engages the proof machinery. The prove subcommand merges proo"
       & "f patches before running gnatprove\\n( Run_Prove integration in adacovex-pro"
       & "ve.adb): Count_Proof_Patches scans <target>/.adacovex/patches/ for .ads and "
       & ".adb patch files; a target with no proof patches is proved against its\\nown"
       & " tree exactly as before. Build_Patched_Copy copies the target tree (excludin"
       & "g .git, obj,\\nand .adacovex) into <target>/obj/adacovex-proof/ and overwrit"
       & "es each\\nproof-patched source with its merged form "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " package-level aspects\\nspliced onto the package declaration line (a packag"
       & "e body ... is\\ndeclaration included), and each aspect-carrying subprogram d"
       & "eclaration\\nreplaced by the patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declaration block. The merge engine ( Apply)\\nmatches on name and normali"
       & "sed parameter profile, so an overloaded\\nsubprogram patches its exact signa"
       & "ture and never a same-named sibling;\\nthe default in mode is equivalent to "
       & "a bare mode ( in out and out\\nstay distinct). Spec declarations terminate a"
       & "t their ;, body\\ndeclarations at their is "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a patched body declaration is replaced\\nwithout touching the body proper. "
       & "An unmatched patch reference fails\\nloudly instead of being silently droppe"
       & "d. gnatprove runs against the copy"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s root project and the resulting gnatprove.out is copied back to <target>/ob"
       & "j/gnatprove/gnatprove.out\\nfor the assessment pipeline. The copy lives unde"
       & "r the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s obj/,\\nso it is excluded from scanning, manifest graphs, and the prove in"
       & "put\\nhash. The originals are never touched. Proof-patch contents are folded"
       & " into the prove result-cache key, so a\\npatch edit invalidates the cached p"
       & "roof and forces a re-prove. The two patch shapes: a spec patch ( .ads) re-de"
       & "clares the vendored spec with contracts; a body patch ( .adb) opts the vendo"
       & "red body into the proof "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " gnatprove analyses a unit"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s body only when the body itself declares SPARK_Mode => On, so a SPARK-clean"
       & " vendored body needs both. Where the body is SPARK-clean and opted in, gnatp"
       & "rove proves the patched contracts (the documented Vecmath. Clamp worked exam"
       & "ple proves its Post => Clamp\'Result in Lo .. Hi outright "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all of its VCs proved, none unproved); where it is not (e.g. bodies that ca"
       & "ll `Ada. Text_IO , which is SPARK_Mode Off`), gnatprove skips the I/O bodies"
       & " by design and reports the unit out of proof scope "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a proof patch never drags the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
