       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Generated outputs"",""id"":""141"",""title"":""Generated outputs""},""142"":{""body"":""T"
       & "he test suite is native and zero-dependency. src/tests/ holds one file per c"
       & "ategory (scanner, config, types, renderers, SBOM, VCS, and more). Each file "
       & "exposes a Run (R : in out Runner\'Class) procedure wired into src/tests/test"
       & "_runner.adb. A test is a R. Check (Condition, \\""Description\\"") call. The r"
       & "unner counts them, prints a per-category table, and writes docs/test_result."
       & "md. -- src/tests/adacovex_scanner_tests.adb (pattern to follow)\\nAdacovex.P"
       & "arsers.Source.Scan_Ads_File (Tmp_File, Pkg, Success);\\nR.Check (Success, \\"
       & """Test 1: parse succeeded\\""); After adding or removing tests: make test # re"
       & "build + run; rewrites docs/test_result.md\\nmake test-count # sync every anc"
       & "hored count across the repo (AGENTS.md, # README, Makefile, CI workflows, ma"
       & "nifests, agents-tree.map) The count-sync is enforced by make check. A test c"
       & "hange that skips the sync fails the gate. Tests write to /tmp scratch dirs a"
       & "nd clean up after themselves. The default on-disk result cache ( ~/.adacovex"
       & "/cache) is shared. Tests that exercise caching use content-hashed keys. They"
       & " never depend on each other"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s state."",""breadcrumbs"":""Contributor guide: codebase structure and setup "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Testing"",""id"":""142"",""title"":""Testing""},""143"":{""body"":""The pure-stdlib Pytho"
       & "n gates keep the docs and the dashboard in step with\\nthe code. They are th"
       & "e drop-in replacements for the npm tools (stylelint,\\nand more) that a Java"
       & "Script toolchain would use; adacovex keeps its dev\\ntooling Python-only by "
       & "convention: tools/csslint.py ( make csslint-check) enforces the 4px spacing "
       & "rule:\\nevery margin, padding, and gap pixel length is a multiple of 4px.\\n"
       & "It runs inside make build and make check. tools/check-docs.py ( make docs-ch"
       & "eck) fails when any paragraph in the\\nuser docs, README, or human changelog"
       & "s exceeds four sentences, and it\\nrejects em dashes and Latin abbreviations"
       & " ( i.e., e.g., etc.). tools/para-split.py rewraps over-long paragraphs to co"
       & "mply. tools/gen-dashboard.py bundles the dashboard resources into src/adacov"
       & "ex-dashboard_template.ads and minifies the authored CSS and\\nJavaScript (co"
       & "mments stripped, whitespace collapsed) before inlining. Edit the dashboard u"
       & "nder resources/, never the generated template. After\\nany docs or resource "
       & "change, run make docs-check and make csslint-check\\nbefore committing."",""br"
       & "eadcrumbs"":""Contributor guide: codebase structure and setup "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Documentation and dashboard tooling"",""id"":""143"",""title"":""Documentation and "
       & "dashboard tooling""},""144"":{""body"":""make prove runs gnatprove through the pro"
       & "ve subcommand and enforces the\\nPlatinum gate: 0 unproved VCs and 0 justifi"
       & "ed VCs. The rules that keep the\\nproof tractable: Every user assertion and "
       & "every runtime check must be proved. No pragma Assume / pragma Annotate justi"
       & "fications. No pragma SPARK_Mode (Off) anywhere except Types.Implementation a"
       & "nd Complexity (the two non-formal- Ada.Containers packages. Non-formal Ada.C"
       & "ontainers are illegal in SPARK_Mode-On code "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " gnatprove rejects\\nthem; the evidence is in docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md. m"
       & "ake spark-off-check enforces this. I/O- and container-heavy units are defaul"
       & "t-off bodies or carry per-subprogram SPARK_Mode => On aspects. They never ca"
       & "rry an explicit Off pragma. The proof result is anchored in docs/proof/ (the"
       & " per-version VC ledger). make proof-status syncs the VC count and SPARK leve"
       & "l into the docs."",""breadcrumbs"":""Contributor guide: codebase structure and s"
       & "etup "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " SPARK proof discipline"",""id"":""144"",""title"":""SPARK proof discipline""},""145"":"
       & "{""body"":""Assess another project: adacovex --target=PATH --dal=C (see Target "
       & "projects). Dogfood: make run-self (adacovex against itself) and make run-ada"
       & "-crdt (against the sibling ../Ada_CRDT checkout, strict mode). Both\\nmust s"
       & "tay green. Coverage gate between releases: make coverage-gate compares docst"
       & "ring\\ncoverage between the latest two release tags. Prepare a release: make"
       & " bump-version VERSION=x.y.z, write the changelog\\n( docs/changelogs/adacove"
       & "x-x.y.z.md, canonical format enforced by make changelog-check), then make re"
       & "lease VERSION=x.y.z. Keep docs current: every code change updates the releva"
       & "nt user docs,\\nthe Ada docstrings that feed docs/api-docs, and the changelo"
       & "g, then\\nre-runs the sync gates ( make docs-check, make action-parity-check"
       & ", make agents-tree, make doc-links, make link-check). Stale docs are a\\nrel"
       & "ease blocker. Debug: adacovex --verbose prints pipeline step diagnostics. ad"
       & "acovex status reports toolchain + platform state. --no-cache bypasses the\\n"
       & "on-disk result cache when inputs changed without content changing."",""breadcr"
       & "umbs"":""Contributor guide: codebase structure and setup "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Common workflows"",""id"":""145"",""title"":""Common workflows""},""146"":{""body"":""CLI"
       & " reference "
