       & Character'Val(147)
       & " generated package docs and the\\nreference pages (docstring spec, test form"
       & "ats, SPARK/DAL/ASIL/Class levels) CONTRIBUTING.md "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " contribution process and changelog format"",""breadcrumbs"":""Contributor guide"
       & ": codebase structure and setup "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Related pages"",""id"":""146"",""title"":""Related pages""},""147"":{""body"":""adacovex "
       & "runs gnatprove, reads its summary, and grades the result against\\nthe SPARK"
       & " assurance levels. This page\\nis the guide to both halves: how proving work"
       & "s under adacovex, and how to write proofs "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " contracts in your own code, and "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " when the code\\nis vendored and cannot be modified "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " proof patches that add the\\ncontracts for you."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and"
       & " writing SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Proving and writing SPARK proofs"",""id"":""147"",""title"":""Proving and writing S"
       & "PARK proofs""},""148"":{""body"":""adacovex prove --target=. The prove subcommand "
       & "(full options: CLI reference "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the prove subcommand): Resolves gnatprove without requiring the target to d"
       & "eclare it:\\nmanifest pin > global pin > $PATH > cached toolchain > download"
       & ". Full\\norder and per-method detail: Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " GNATprove toolchain resolution. Runs gnatprove against the target (or again"
       & "st a patched tree copy\\nwhen proof patches are present "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see Proof patches below) and\\nwrites the summary to <target>/obj/gnatprove"
       & "/gnatprove.out "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the same\\nlocation the assessment pipeline discovers. Falls through to the"
       & " full assessment. The assessment parses the fresh\\nsummary. One command bot"
       & "h proves and assesses. The --require-* CI gates\\napply to the proof run dir"
       & "ectly ( --require-spark=Platinum --require-proof=100 and more; see CLI refer"
       & "ence "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " CI threshold gates). The result cache serves unchanged targets so repeated "
       & "runs are cheap. --force bypasses the cache and forces a full gnatprove reana"
       & "lysis. A target\\nwithout a gnatprove.out at all is graded Stone with proof "
       & "metrics N/A.\\nRun prove to generate one."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writin"
       & "g SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Proving a project with adacovex"",""id"":""148"",""title"":""Proving a project with"
       & " adacovex""},""149"":{""body"":""gnatprove reports verification conditions (VCs) p"
       & "er check category. The\\nsummary in gnatprove.out breaks them down as: Categ"
       & "ory What it covers Run-time checks Index bounds, overflow, division-by-zero,"
       & " range checks "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " absence of run-time errors Assertions User pragma Assert statements and pre"
       & "/postcondition checks Functional contracts Pre / Post / Global contract sati"
       & "sfaction Data dependencies Flow analysis: uninitialized reads, effective Glo"
       & "bal contracts Initialization All objects initialized before first use Termin"
       & "ation Loop_Variant / recursion bounds (subprograms proved terminating) The h"
       & "onest proved count is total - justified - unproved (flow plus\\nprovers). Th"
       & "e assurance level is\\nderived from how many of each category were discharge"
       & "d: Stone "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no proof run or nothing analyzable; Bronze "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " flow analysis clean (data dependencies, initialization); Silver "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " run-time checks proved, assertions proved; Gold "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " functional contracts proved on top; Platinum "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every VC proved: 0 unproved (and, in adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own\\ngate, 0 justified "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no pragma Annotate justifications). Justified VCs count neither as proved n"
       & "or as unproved. Only unproved VCs\\ndowngrade the level. For a DAL assessmen"
       & "t, the level must meet the requirement\\nof the tier ( --dal=C needs Bronze,"
       & " --dal=A needs Gold, and more) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see DAL levels."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " What a proof contains"",""id"":""149"",""title"":""What a proof contains""},""15"":{""b"
       & "ody"":""Missing Effect No .ads sources No packages scanned; metrics report zer"
       & "o No gnatprove.out SPARK level Stone, proof metrics N/A No test summary Test"
       & " metrics N/A; DAL Tests passing criterion Unmet No HLR.md HLR coverage N/A; "
       & "DAL traceability criteria Unmet"",""breadcrumbs"":""Target project requirements "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Missing data"",""id"":""15"",""title"":""Missing data""},""150"":{""body"":""A proof star"
       & "ts with contracts in the source, written as Ada aspects: package Body_Vec is"
       & " function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer) retur"
       & "n Integer with Pre => Lo <= Hi, Post => Clamp\'Result in Lo .. Hi; end Body_"
       & "Vec; Rules that matter in practice: SPARK_Mode => On selects what gnatprove "
       & "analyses. Without it a unit\\nis out of proof scope. It can be declared on t"
       & "he package\\n( package P with SPARK_Mode => On is), on individual subprogram"
       & "s, or\\nboth "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own source uses package-level On on pure units and\\nper-subprogram On asp"
       & "ects inside default-off bodies. A body is analysed only when the body itself"
       & " opts in. Declaring SPARK_Mode => On on the spec does not make gnatprove ana"
       & "lyse the body.\\nThe body must declare it too (on the package body line or p"
       & "er subprogram).\\nThis is the rule that makes proof patches necessary for ve"
       & "ndored code "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see\\nbelow. I/O bodies are skipped by design. A body that calls Ada.Text_I"
       & "O (which\\nis SPARK_Mode Off) cannot be analysed. gnatprove reports the unit"
       & " out of\\nproof scope. This never drags the assessed level down "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " it means those\\nbodies are not proved. Contracts are proved against the bo"
       & "dy. gnatprove proves that every\\npossible body execution satisfies the decl"
       & "ared Pre/ Post. Callers must in\\nturn establish the Pre before calling. --s"
       & "teps controls the proof budget. gnatprove"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default step limit can\\nproduce solver-timeout false negatives. adacovex "
       & "runs with --steps 10000\\nby default so such timeouts are not reported as un"
       & "proved. An explicit --steps=N overrides. The goal for a clean proof: every V"
       & "C in every category proved, 0 unproved,\\n0 justified."",""breadcrumbs"":""Provi"
       & "ng and writing SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Writing proofs: SPARK contracts"",""id"":""150"",""title"":""Writing proofs: SPARK "
       & "contracts""},""151"":{""body"":""Patch files at <target>/.adacovex/patches/ exist "
       & "so vendored code you\\ncannot modify still counts toward the audit. Their be"
       & "st-known job is\\noverlaying docstrings for strict-mode coverage. A patch ca"
       & "n also carry SPARK proof aspects so vendored dependencies participate in the"
       & " proof\\nwith real contracts "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " without forking or touching their sources."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writ"
       & "ing SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Proof patches: proving vendored dependencies"",""id"":""151"",""title"":""Proof pat"
       & "ches: proving vendored dependencies""},""152"":{""body"":""Three facts force the d"
       & "esign: Strict mode counts vendored code. By default adacovex scans every\\nd"
       & "irectory except the always-excluded ones. The excluded directories are .git,"
       & " obj, tests, config, and .adacovex. A vendored dependency"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s\\nmissing docstrings and missing contracts count against the target. --rel"
       & "axed skips vendored dirs but drops the audit to a quick pass "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " not\\nan option for a compliance assessment. gnatprove analyses a body only"
       & " when the body itself opts in. (The\\nrule from Writing proofs above.) A\\nv"
       & "endored spec with no contracts contributes nothing to the proof. A\\nvendore"
       & "d body without SPARK_Mode is skipped entirely. The vendored sources are immu"
       & "table. The dependency ships as-is. You\\ncannot add contracts to it. Re-publ"
       & "ishing a patched fork defeats the\\npoint of vendoring. A proof patch is the"
       & " merge of these three constraints. It re-declares the\\nvendored spec with c"
       & "ontracts ( .ads patch). It opts the vendored body into\\nthe proof ( .adb pa"
       & "tch). The prove subcommand merges both into a patched\\ntree copy before run"
       & "ning gnatprove "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the originals are never touched."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK "
       & "proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Why proof patches are necessary"",""id"":""152"",""title"":""Why proof patches are "
       & "necessary""},""153"":{""body"":""Count_Proof_Patches scans <target>/.adacovex/patc"
       & "hes/ for .ads and .adb files. A patch carrying any of SPARK_Mode, Pre =>, Po"
       & "st =>,\\nor Global => is a proof patch. A docstring-only patch never engages"
       & "\\nthe proof machinery. A target with no proof patches is proved against its"
       & "\\nown tree exactly as before. Build_Patched_Copy copies the target tree (ex"
       & "cluding .git, obj,\\nand .adacovex) into <target>/obj/adacovex-proof/ and ov"
       & "erwrites each\\nproof-patched source with its merged form. gnatprove runs ag"
       & "ainst the copy"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s root project and the resulting gnatprove.out is copied back to <target>/ob"
       & "j/gnatprove/gnatprove.out\\nfor the assessment pipeline. Patch contents are "
       & "folded into the prove result-cache key, so a patch\\nedit invalidates the ca"
       & "ched proof and forces a re-prove ( --force also\\nbypasses the cache). The p"
       & "atched copy lives under the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s obj/, so it is excluded from\\nscanning, manifest graphs, and the prove in"
       & "put hash."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " How proof patches are applied"",""id"":""153"",""title"":""How proof patches are ap"
       & "plied""},""154"":{""body"":""A spec patch mirrors the vendored spec: same package "
       & "name, same subprogram\\ndeclarations (with docstrings, since strict mode req"
       & "uires them), plus the\\naspects you want gnatprove to prove: -- .adacovex/pa"
       & "tches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads\\npackage VT100 with SPARK_Mode => On is -- "
       & "Scroll a region of the screen up. -- @param From Starting line of scroll reg"
       & "ion. -- @param To Ending line of scroll region. procedure Scroll_Screen (Fro"
       & "m : in Natural; To : in Natural) with Pre => From <= To; end VT100; The merg"
       & "e splices the package-level aspect onto the original package\\ndeclaration l"
       & "ine and replaces each aspect-carrying subprogram declaration\\nwith the patc"
       & "h"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declaration block. Subprograms the patch does not re-declare\\nwith aspect"
       & "s are left untouched, so a patch can add a contract to one\\nsubprogram with"
       & "out disturbing its siblings."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK proof"
       & "s "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Writing a spec patch ( .ads)"",""id"":""154"",""title"":""Writing a spec patch ( .a"
       & "ds)""},""155"":{""body"":""The spec patch declares the contracts. The body patch i"
       & "s what makes\\ngnatprove actually analyse the vendored body (the body-must-o"
       & "pt-in rule). It\\nlives at the body"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s relative path and mirrors the body"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declarations with stub bodies that the merge ignores "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the original implementation is\\npreserved: -- .adacovex/patches/demo/deps/"
       & "vecmath/vecmath.adb\\npackage body Vecmath with SPARK_Mode => On is function"
       & " Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer) return Integer"
       & " with SPARK_Mode => On is begin null; -- stub: the original body\'s implemen"
       & "tation is kept end Clamp; end Vecmath; The merge replaces the original decla"
       & "ration (up to its is) with the\\npatch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s aspect-carrying declaration and keeps the original body proper, so\\nthe c"
       & "opy gnatprove sees is package body Vecmath with SPARK_Mode => On is ... <ori"
       & "ginal implementation> .... A fully SPARK-clean body needs only the\\npackage"
       & "-level aspect. The per-subprogram aspect covers bodies with a mix of\\nclean"
       & " and I/O-bound subprograms."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK proofs"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Writing a body patch ( .adb)"",""id"":""155"",""title"":""Writing a body patch ( .a"
       & "db)""},""156"":{""body"":""The merge matches each patched declaration against the "
       & "original by name and\\nnormalised parameter profile: Matching is whitespace-"
       & "insensitive. A single-line parameter list matches a\\nmulti-line one. The de"
       & "fault in mode is equivalent to a bare mode ( X : in Integer matches X : Inte"
       & "ger). in out and out are distinct modes. an overloaded subprogram patches it"
       & "s exact signature "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a patched\\ntwo-argument Scroll_Screen replaces the two-argument original, "
       & "never a\\nsame-named sibling; a spec declaration terminates at its ;, a body"
       & " declaration at its is; a patched subprogram with no match in the original f"
       & "ails loudly (the\\npatch is skipped and reported) rather than silently dropp"
       & "ing the contract."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Matching rules"",""id"":""156"",""title"":""Matching rules""},""157"":{""body"":""A vendo"
       & "red package whose spec and body carry no contracts: -- demo/deps/vecmath/vec"
       & "math.ads (vendored, unmodified)\\npackage Vecmath is function Clamp (Value :"
       & " in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer) return Integer;\\nend Vecmath"
       & "; -- demo/deps/vecmath/vecmath.adb (vendored, unmodified)\\npackage body Vec"
       & "math is function Clamp (Value : in Integer; Lo : in Integer; Hi : in Integer"
       & ") return Integer is begin if Value < Lo then return Lo; elsif Value > Hi the"
       & "n return Hi; else return Value; end if; end Clamp;\\nend Vecmath; The two pa"
       & "tch files from above (spec with Pre => Lo <= Hi, Post => Clamp\'Result in Lo"
       & " .. Hi, and body with SPARK_Mode => On) merge into the copy unchanged in beh"
       & "aviour. gnatprove\\nproves the contract: 2 VCs (the Clamp postcondition and "
       & "its termination\\ncheck), 0 unproved. A caller in the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own code can then rely on the\\ncontract without the vendored sources ever"
       & " changing."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Worked example: Vecmath.Clamp"",""id"":""157"",""title"":""Worked example: Vecmath."
       & "Clamp""},""158"":{""body"":""SPARK-clean body + body patch "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " gnatprove proves the patched\\ncontracts outright (the example above). I/O-"
       & "bound body (calls Ada.Text_IO, which is SPARK_Mode Off) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "\\ngnatprove skips the I/O bodies by design and reports the unit out of proo"
       & "f\\nscope. The contracts are still declared and the mechanism is exercised,\"
       & "\nbut the body is not proved "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and crucially, it never drags the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s\\nproof level down. This is the VT100 dogfood case in Ada_CRDT."",""breadcru"
       & "mbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " When contracts prove "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and when they are skipped"",""id"":""158"",""title"":""When contracts prove "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and when they are skipped""},""159"":{""body"":""Spec patch without a body patch."
       & " A SPARK-clean vendored body stays out\\nof proof scope. gnatprove reports "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "no checks generated"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " or skips the unit.\\nAdd the .adb patch to opt the body in. A patched decla"
       & "ration that does not match anything. Check the name and\\nthe parameter list"
       & " (modes included) against the original. The merge reports could not be merge"
       & "d ... (unmatched subprogram or oversized file) and skips\\nthe patch. Patchi"
       & "ng the wrong overload. The match is profile-aware, so a patch\\nentry replac"
       & "es exactly the signature it re-declares "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " verify you wrote the\\nsame parameter list as the overload you mean. Expect"
       & "ing contracts to prove against a non-SPARK body. Ada.Text_IO\\nand other SPA"
       & "RK_Mode Off dependencies cannot be analysed; the patch still\\napplies, but "
       & "the proof does not cover those bodies."",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing S"
       & "PARK proofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Common pitfalls"",""id"":""159"",""title"":""Common pitfalls""},""16"":{""body"":""adacov"
       & "ex currently targets Ada/SPARK sources. Non-Ada projects (C/C++, Python,\\nJ"
       & "S, and more) that want the compliance/SBOM tooling provide their own alire.t"
       & "oml / alire-dev.toml to manage the Ada dependencies needed to build\\nadacov"
       & "ex itself. Running adacovex from such a repo scans it and uses its\\nmanifes"
       & "t. We are working on support for other languages. Watch for updates."",""bread"
       & "crumbs"":""Target project requirements "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Non-Ada projects"",""id"":""16"",""title"":""Non-Ada projects""},""160"":{""body"":""SPAR"
       & "K assurance levels "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Stone to\\nPlatinum, per-category objectives CLI reference "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the prove subcommand\\n"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " flags, gnatprove resolution, the fall-through assessment CLI reference "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " CI threshold gates\\n"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " --require-spark / --require-proof / --require-tests Target project requirem"
       & "ents "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " what a project must provide Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " proof patches\\n"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the design, the merge engine, and the patched-copy pipeline The proof ledge"
       & "r "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " how adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own 487-VC\\nproof is tracked"",""breadcrumbs"":""Proving and writing SPARK pr"
       & "oofs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " See also"",""id"":""160"",""title"":""See also""},""161"":{""body"":"""",""breadcrumbs"":""ad"
       & "acovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex Architecture Decisions"",""id"":""161"",""title"":""adacovex Architecture "
       & "Decisions""},""162"":{""body"":""adacovex uses Alire as its packaging and delivery"
       & " mechanism. The publishing manifest alire.toml declares zero dependencies. I"
       & "t declares no libraries beyond the GNAT runtime. It declares no tool depende"
       & "ncies. In particular gnatprove is not a declared dependency. adacovex analys"
       & "es gnatprove.out files produced externally. The prove subcommand resolves a "
       & "gnatprove executable at run time (per-project manifest, $PATH, cached toolch"
       & "ain, or download). Development-only tools ( gnatprove, gnatdoc_bin, gnatform"
       & "at_bin) are declared in alire-dev.toml, which is never published to the Alir"
       & "e community index."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Dependency Management: Alire"",""id"":""162"",""title"":""Dependency Management: Al"
       & "ire""},""163"":{""body"":""alire.toml: The clean publishing manifest. Declares no "
       & "dependencies at\\nall, so alr install covex (or alr build from source) pulls"
       & " nothing beyond\\nthe binary and the GNAT compiler. Used for SBOM generation"
       & " and dependency\\ngraph scanning. alire-dev.toml: The development manifest. "
       & "Extends alire.toml with\\ndev-only tools ( gnatprove, gnatdoc_bin, gnatforma"
       & "t_bin) needed for make prove, make doc, and make fmt. Used for toolchain res"
       & "olution when\\nrunning alr exec. When both files exist, Build_Dependency_Gra"
       & "ph reads both: a dependency\\ndeclared in alire.toml is classified Scope_Bas"
       & "e (explicit/clean dep) and\\none declared only in alire-dev.toml is Scope_De"
       & "v. The scope is surfaced in\\nthe SBOM as the adacovex:dep_scope property ( "
       & "base / dev / transitive / vendored), so it is always clear which file a depe"
       & "ndency came from. alire-dev.toml is also consulted for gnatprove detection\\"
       & "n( Manifest_Declares_GNATprove checks both manifests)."",""breadcrumbs"":""adaco"
       & "vex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Manifest distinction ( alire.toml vs alire-dev.toml)"",""id"":""163"",""title"":""M"
       & "anifest distinction ( alire.toml vs alire-dev.toml)""},""164"":{""body"":""adacove"
       & "x declares gnatprove only in its own alire-dev.toml (keeping the\\npublishin"
       & "g alire.toml clean). The prove subcommand resolves the gnatprove\\nexecutabl"
       & "e in this order: Per-project manifest (authoritative): if <target>/alire.tom"
       & "l / <target>/alire-dev.toml declares a gnatprove dependency, the pinned\\ngn"
       & "atprove binary crate is deployed standalone into ~/.adacovex/toolchain/\\nvi"
       & "a alr -n get gnatprove=<version> and executed directly (the version-set\\nex"
       & "pression, for example ^16.1.0, is reduced to the bare version alr\\naccepts)"
       & ". This isolates the proof run from the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s other dev-manifest\\ntools and never swaps manifests. A manifest pin alway"
       & "s wins. When the pinned\\nversion cannot be deployed, the run fails instead "
       & "of falling back. Global version pin: the ADACOVEX_GNATPROVE_VERSION environm"
       & "ent\\nvariable or the [prove] gnatprove-version key in ~/.adacovex/adacovex."
       & "toml, deployed standalone via alr -n get gnatprove=<version>. It uses the sa"
       & "me never-fall-back\\nsemantics. It is folded into the proof result-cache ide"
       & "ntity. $PATH: a gnatprove already installed (for example alr install gnatpro"
       & "ve). Cached toolchain: ~/.adacovex/toolchain/. The download layout\\n( <tool"
       & "chain>/bin/gnatprove) is used. A previously alr get-deployed gnatprove_*/ cr"
       & "ate is also used. Download: last-resort platform toolchain bundle. Effective"
       & " order: manifest pin > global pin (config/env) > PATH > cache >\\ndownload. "
       & "If a project manifest declares gnatprove but alr is missing,\\ninstall Alire"
       & " first. The remaining fallbacks then apply. The make doc / make fmt targets "
       & "still swap alire-dev.toml over alire.toml for the duration of gnatdoc / gnat"
       & "format (the _dev_cmd\\nMakefile recipe backs up alire.toml / alire.lock / al"
       & "ire/, swaps, runs,\\nand restores via a trap). prove does not use that swap."
       & " It deploys only\\nthe single gnatprove crate. The assessment and SBOM pipel"
       & "ine always scans the publishing alire.toml, so\\ndev-only tool declarations "
       & "never leak into dependency graphs or SBOMs."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Archite"
       & "cture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " GNATprove toolchain resolution ( prove subcommand)"",""id"":""164"",""title"":""GNA"
       & "Tprove toolchain resolution ( prove subcommand)""},""165"":{""body"":""Beyond the "
       & "Alire graph, Discover_System_Dev_Deps adds the system binaries a project int"
       & "eracts with at development time ( python3, git, gnatprove, make, and more) a"
       & "s Scope_Dev SBOM components. It scans the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s dev-facing files (Makefile variants, .sh / .py / .gpr / .yml / .toml / .ad"
       & "s / .adb) for a curated toolchain list and registers every referenced tool t"
       & "hat is actually installed on $PATH under a pkg:generic/<tool> purl. Tools re"
       & "ferenced nowhere in the project, or referenced but not installed, are skippe"
       & "d. A Makefile at the project root implies make. The scan runs after the cach"
       & "ed manifest graph is resolved (so cache hits and misses agree). Each registe"
       & "red tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s version is probed by running --version (or a tool-specific subcommand such"
       & " as fossil"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s version) and extracting the version token, so the SBOM records the install"
       & "ed version. A probe that fails or prints no digit token leaves the version e"
       & "mpty. The source file declaring the System_Tools table is skipped by the sca"
       & "n. Otherwise, every installed tool on the list can be registered as a self-r"
       & "eference."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " System-tool dev dependencies (SBOM)"",""id"":""165"",""title"":""System-tool dev de"
       & "pendencies (SBOM)""},""166"":{""body"":""Discover_Generic_Vendored walks the targe"
       & "t tree for vendor roots\\n( node_modules, vendor, third_party, and the other"
       & " recognised names).\\nEach directory inside a vendor root that carries an ec"
       & "osystem manifest\\n( package.json, Cargo.toml, go.mod, pyproject.toml, compo"
       & "ser.json, Gemfile, pom.xml, Package.swift, requirements*.txt) becomes one\\n"
       & "component with its ecosystem purl ( pkg:npm/..., pkg:cargo/..., and\\nmore)."
       & " Its scope defaults to vendored. A component is classified test when the pro"
       & "ject manifest that owns the\\nvendor root declares it under a test-only labe"
       & "l: package.json sections whose key contains test (for example testDependenci"
       & "es); Cargo [dev-dependencies] (Cargo"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s native test-only section) and any\\nsection containing test; composer requ"
       & "ire-dev; Gemfile group :test blocks; pom.xml dependencies whose <scope> is t"
       & "est; pyproject.toml test extras and Poetry [tool.poetry.group.test.*]\\nsect"
       & "ions; Package.swift dependencies declared inside a .testTarget(...) block. T"
       & "he name heuristic is the fallback for every ecosystem. A component\\nwhose n"
       & "ame starts or ends with the literal word test is test-labelled.\\nThe check "
       & "covers the full name and then the last segment after any / or :, so @playwri"
       & "ght/test, test-case, github.com/stretchr/testify and org.testng:testng all m"
       & "atch. Ecosystems without a native test-only\\nsection ( go.mod, requirements"
       & "*.txt) rely on this heuristic. The heuristic also applies to lockfile-resolv"
       & "ed names: pnpm-lock.yaml / package-lock.json / yarn.lock entries next to an\"
       & "\nowner package.json, Cargo.lock crate names, and alire.lock crates\\nthat t"
       & "he manifest sets leave transitive. The scope is surfaced as the SBOM adacove"
       & "x:dep_scope property ( test)\\nand in the dashboard dependency badges, scope"
       & " filter, legend, and rings.\\nThe Alire-side [[test-depends-on]] sections an"
       & "d test project files are\\nthe other source of test scope; see the SBOM refe"
       & "rence."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Vendored components and test-labelled dependencies (SBOM)"",""id"":""166"",""titl"
       & "e"":""Vendored components and test-labelled dependencies (SBOM)""},""167"":{""body"
       & """:""adacovex follows the Unix philosophy of doing one thing well: Single-purp"
       & "ose pipeline: Each step (scanning, proof parsing, test parsing, DAL assessme"
       & "nt, rendering) is a focused, composable unit. Text-based interfaces: Input a"
       & "nd output are plain text (Ada source, .out files, Markdown reports, ANSI ter"
       & "minal output). No library dependencies: Only the GNAT runtime is used. No ex"
       & "ternal\\nlibraries or frameworks. Alire is the packaging/delivery mechanism "
       & "but adds\\nno runtime dependency. adacovex declares no library or tool depen"
       & "dencies\\n(gnatprove is resolved at run time by the prove subcommand). Compo"
       & "sable tools: The prove subcommand runs GNATprove and then falls through to t"
       & "he standard assessment pipeline. The sbom subcommand generates a proof-aware"
       & " SBOM independently. Exit codes: 0 for success (DAL achieved), 1 for complia"
       & "nce failure. This enables straightforward CI integration. Minimal user code:"
       & " users write as little code as possible while getting\\nmaximum value. The t"
       & "ool accepts third-party and generated code as it is. It recognises common do"
       & "cstring conventions (Ada -- @param, Google Args:/ Returns:, Sphinx :param:/ "
       & ":returns:). It recognises common test-result formats (TAP, Automake, Surefir"
       & "e, Unity). It lowers foreign type names ( int32_t, size_t, and more) onto bo"
       & "unded Ada types. Nothing needs to be rewritten to be assessed."",""breadcrumbs"
       & """:""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Unix Philosophy"",""id"":""167"",""title"":""Unix Philosophy""},""168"":{""body"":""adaco"
       & "vex declares no library dependencies beyond the GNAT runtime. All data struc"
       & "tures use either: GNAT runtime containers ( Ada.Containers.Vectors for unbou"
       & "nded collections) Fixed-size string buffers ( Max_Line = 262144, Max_Path = "
       & "4096, etc.) for bounded I/O Max_Path and Max_Line scale with the auto-detect"
       & "ed host word size\\n( System.Word_Size), keeping the classic 4096 / 262144 v"
       & "alues on 64-bit\\nhosts while using proportionally smaller limits on narrowe"
       & "r machines. The\\nsemantic limits ( Max_Id_Str, Max_Desc_Str, Max_Filename) "
       & "are not\\nstorage-size dependent and remain fixed. Max_Line is deliberately "
       & "generous (256 KiB on 64-bit) so that single-line declarations from heavily c"
       & "ode-generated projects parse cleanly. When a physical line does exceed the b"
       & "uffer, adacovex never truncates it and then processes it. Truncation can sil"
       & "ently produce a partial (and wrong) result. Instead the parser drains the re"
       & "mainder, reports the file and line to standard error, and fails that parse e"
       & "xplicitly. The source scanner counts the skipped file in Skipped_Ct, which f"
       & "orces the DAL assessment to Unmet and the exit code to 1 (no compliance clai"
       & "m can be made for unread code). The same explicit-failure contract applies t"
       & "o every parser: HLR/LLR markdown, GNATprove output (text and JSON), test res"
       & "ults, and Alire manifest / lockfile / GPR dependency graphs. An exact buffer"
       & "-length line is not an overflow (it parses normally), and paths exceeding Ma"
       & "x_Path are likewise reported and skipped rather than crashing. Overflow cont"
       & "ract (two tiers). Path and line buffers fail loudly. An\\noverlong physical "
       & "line is drained and reported ( line exceeds Max_Line buffer). The file is no"
       & "t parsed. Skipped_Ct increments. DAL becomes Unmet. An overlong path is repo"
       & "rted and the file/subtree is skipped. No partial results ever flow downstrea"
       & "m. Semantic text fields (subprogram names, HLR/LLR IDs, descriptions, docstr"
       & "ing tag names/values, CLI strings) are clamped to their fixed buffer with th"
       & "e length field ( Name_Len, Id_Len, D_Len, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & ") recording the recorded prefix, so adversarial or generated\\ninput can nev"
       & "er raise Constraint_Error. Clamping keeps the scan correct.\\nThe full token"
       & " is still consumed so following tokens are not misparsed. Why no chunking / "
       & "LEB128. adacovex audits in memory. Counts (packages,\\nsubprograms, HLR tags"
       & ", tests, SBOM components) are unbounded vectors. Each scanned unit is proces"
       & "sed line-at-a-time into fixed per-item buffers. A single Ada declaration doe"
       & "s not admit streaming/chunked parsing. Truncating a declaration is worse tha"
       & "n a loud failure. Chunking can gain nothing. LEB128 (variable-length integer"
       & " encoding) is a serialization concern and does not apply to an in-memory CLI"
       & " audit. The design therefore scales to arbitrarily large codebases by dynami"
       & "c allocation, bounded per-item buffers, and explicit overflow handling, with"
       & "out streaming encodings. The bounded-buffer constants are tabulated in docs/"
       & "api-docs/adacovex-types.md ( Max_Line, Max_Path, Max_Desc_Str, Max_Filename,"
       & " Max_Id_Str). This ensures adacovex can be built and run on any system with "
       & "a GNAT toolchain,\\nwithout requiring any additional package installation be"
       & "yond Alire for\\ntoolchain management."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture"
       & " Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Zero-Library-Dependency Design"",""id"":""168"",""title"":""Zero-Library-Dependency"
       & " Design""},""169"":{""body"":""adacovex itself is SPARK-proven at Platinum level ("
       & "all VCs proved,\\nAoRTE-free). The tool analyses GNATprove output ( gnatprov"
       & "e.out) to assess\\nSPARK assurance levels (Stone through Platinum) for targe"
       & "t projects. The tool does not perform verification itself. It parses and rep"
       & "orts on proof\\nresults produced by GNATprove. This keeps the tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s scope narrow and aligns\\nwith the Unix philosophy of composing specialise"
       & "d tools."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " SPARK Formal Verification"",""id"":""169"",""title"":""SPARK Formal Verification""},"
       & """17"":{""body"":""By default (strict mode) adacovex scans and counts every direc"
       & "tory except the\\nalways-excluded ones. Vendored code is included. For third"
       & "-party code you\\ncannot modify, use docstring patch files at <target>/.adac"
       & "ovex/patches/<relative-path> (see Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Patch System). Or run in\\nrelaxed mode ( --relaxed, skip dirs, no patches)"
       & " (see Strict vs relaxed mode). Vendored code can also take part in the SPARK"
       & " proof. A patch carrying SPARK_Mode / Pre / Post / Global aspects is a proof"
       & " patch. The prove subcommand merges it into a patched tree copy. The copy us"
       & "es .ads spec contracts and .adb body patches that opt a SPARK-clean vendored"
       & " body into the proof. See Proving and writing proofs for how to write them. "
       & "See Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Proof patches for the design."",""breadcrumbs"":""Target project requirements "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Vendored code and strict mode"",""id"":""17"",""title"":""Vendored code and strict "
       & "mode""},""170"":{""body"":""Proof scope is the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own units. adacovex proves the Ada/SPARK\\ncode it is run against, never t"
       & "hird-party dependencies. GNATprove units that\\nare skipped (for example sta"
       & "ndard-library or vendor code that GNATprove\\nitself does not analyse) are t"
       & "racked via Units_Skipped and reported in the\\nANSI and Markdown reports. Th"
       & "ey are out of proof scope by design, not a\\nproof failure. Justifications a"
       & "re an accepted discharge mechanism. A Total row"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Justified count (GNATprove pragma Annotate justifications for decidedly\\n"
       & "unprovable checks, such as non-functional foreign-language calls) is counted"
       & "\\nneither as proved nor as unproved: Proved = Total - Justified - Unproved."
       & "\\nJustified VCs do not downgrade the SPARK level. Only unproved VCs do.\\nT"
       & "his is pinned by unit tests. Gold is the minimum compliance baseline. Platin"
       & "um is the ideal. Min_SPARK_For thresholds (A=Gold, B=Silver, C=Bronze, D/E=S"
       & "tone) are the\\ngate for DAL compliance. Platinum is achieved and reported w"
       & "hen every\\nfunctional contract is proved, but it is a best-effort target, n"
       & "ot a\\ncompliance requirement at any DAL level."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Arc"
       & "hitecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Proof scope and justification policy"",""id"":""170"",""title"":""Proof scope and j"
       & "ustification policy""},""171"":{""body"":""The src/ir/ layer starts an intermediat"
       & "e representation for\\ncross-compilation assessments, so the tool can reason"
       & " about types as they\\nexist on a target rather than only as they appear in "
       & "Ada source: Adacovex.Target_Profiles defines bounded machine-integer types\\"
       & "n( IR_Int8.. IR_Int64, IR_UInt8.. IR_UInt64) with Size clauses and a Target_"
       & "Config record (host/target/pointer word sizes). The types are\\nSPARK-proved"
       & ": Checked_Add32 / Checked_Add64 show overflow is detected,\\nnot undefined. "
       & "Adacovex.IR_Synthesiser lowers foreign type names ( int8_t, size_t, usize, p"
       & "trdiff_t, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & ") onto the bounded IR types and synthesizes\\npackage declarations from a co"
       & "mma/whitespace-separated type list. Adacovex.IR_Bounds is a gnatprove fixtur"
       & "e deriving synthesized-style int32_t / int64_t types and proving their Add32"
       & " / Add64 overflow\\nchecks, so absence of integer overflow on the lowered ty"
       & "pes is\\nmachine-checked."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " IR Synthesiser"",""id"":""171"",""title"":""IR Synthesiser""},""172"":{""body"":""The DAL"
       & " assessment evaluates four criteria: All HLRs defined in docs/compliance/HLR"
       & ".md are traced by -- HLR-XXXX tags in source No orphan tags (every in-source"
       & " HLR maps to a defined HLR) All tests passing (zero failures in test_result."
       & "md) Minimum SPARK proof level met (varies by DAL level) DAL-C is the default"
       & " target level. Higher levels (A, B) require stricter proof levels (Gold, Sil"
       & "ver respectively)."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " DO-178C DAL Compliance"",""id"":""172"",""title"":""DO-178C DAL Compliance""},""173"":"
       & "{""body"":""The scanner walks the target directory tree, skipping always-exclud"
       & "ed directories ( .git, obj, tests, config, .adacovex). For each .ads file fo"
       & "und, it extracts: Package name from filename Subprogram declarations ( proce"
       & "dure, function, generic procedure, generic function, and overriding / not ov"
       & "erriding variants) Docstring annotations ( -- prefix with optional @param, @"
       & "return, @field, @formal tags, plus Google Args:/ Returns: blocks and Sphinx "
       & ":param:/ :returns: fields) HLR traceability tags ( -- HLR-XXXX) In strict mo"
       & "de (default), the scanner also applies docstring patches from .adacovex/patc"
       & "hes/ to document vendored/third-party code without modifying the originals."""
       & ",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Source Scanning"",""id"":""173"",""title"":""Source Scanning""},""174"":{""body"":""The ."
       & "adacovex/patches/ directory overlays docstring information onto\\nthird-part"
       & "y or vendored code that cannot be modified directly, so strict mode\\ncan st"
       & "ill reach 100% docstring coverage without touching the originals."",""breadcru"
       & "mbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Patch System"",""id"":""174"",""title"":""Patch System""},""175"":{""body"":""In strict m"
       & "ode (default), all directories except .git, obj, tests, config, and .adacove"
       & "x are scanned. Vendored dependencies (for example a copy of\\nvt100 in demo/"
       & "deps/vt100/) are scanned, and their undocumented subprograms\\ncount against"
       & " docstring coverage. Patches document them in place."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacove"
       & "x Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Why patches exist"",""id"":""175"",""title"":""Why patches exist""},""176"":{""body"":""A"
       & " patch file is a valid Ada .ads file containing only the subprogram\\ndeclar"
       & "ations to document, each preceded by a docstring: -- Package-level comment ("
       & "optional, not used by patch engine).\\npackage VT100 is -- Summary of the pr"
       & "ocedure. -- @param Name Description. procedure Some_Procedure (Name : in Som"
       & "e_Type); -- Another procedure with no params. procedure No_Param_Proc; end V"
       & "T100; Rules: File name must match the original .ads (for example vt100.ads)."
       & " Subprogram names must match the originals exactly. Only subprograms with pr"
       & "eceding docstrings ( -- lines) are merged. Overloaded subprograms: one patch"
       & " entry per overload. Each patches the next\\nundocumented original with the "
       & "same name. The scanner merges Has_Docstring, Doc_Param_Ct, and Doc_Return in"
       & "to\\nthe matching originals."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Patch file format"",""id"":""176"",""title"":""Patch file format""},""177"":{""body"":""<"
       & "target-project>/.adacovex/patches/<relative-path> <relative-path> is the pat"
       & "h from the target root to the .ads file. Example:\\nto patch Ada_CRDT/demo/d"
       & "eps/vt100/vt100.ads, create Ada_CRDT/.adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100"
       & ".ads. The .adacovex\\ndirectory is always excluded from source scanning."",""b"
       & "readcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Patch file location"",""id"":""177"",""title"":""Patch file location""},""178"":{""body"
       & """:""The same .adacovex/patches/<relative-path> file can carry SPARK proof asp"
       & "ects in addition to docstrings, so vendored dependencies participate in the "
       & "SPARK proof without modifying their sources. A patch file that includes any "
       & "of SPARK_Mode, Pre =>, Post =>, or Global => (detected by Adacovex. Prove_Pa"
       & "tch. Has_Proof) is a proof patch. A patch with only docstrings remains a doc"
       & "string overlay and never engages the proof machinery. This section is the de"
       & "sign. For the user-facing guide "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " how proving works, writing SPARK contracts, and the .ads/ .adb patch files "
       & "with worked examples and pitfalls "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see Proving and writing proofs. package VT100 with SPARK_Mode => On is -- S"
       & "croll a region of the screen up. -- @param From Starting line of scroll regi"
       & "on. -- @param To Ending line of scroll region. procedure Scroll_Screen (From"
       & " : in Natural; To : in Natural) with Pre => From <= To; end VT100; The prove"
       & " subcommand merges proof patches before running gnatprove: Count_Proof_Patch"
       & "es scans <target>/.adacovex/patches/ ( .ads and .adb patch files). A target "
       & "with no proof patches is proved against\\nits own tree exactly as before. Bu"
       & "ild_Patched_Copy copies the target tree (excluding .git, obj,\\nand .adacove"
       & "x) into <target>/obj/adacovex-proof/ and overwrites each proof-patched sourc"
       & "e with its merged form "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " package-level aspects spliced onto the package declaration line (for a pack"
       & "age body ... is declaration too), and each aspect-carrying subprogram declar"
       & "ation replaced by the patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declaration block. The merge matches on name and normalised parameter prof"
       & "ile ( Param_Profile), so an overloaded subprogram patches its exact signatur"
       & "e and never a same-named sibling. The default in mode is equivalent to a bar"
       & "e mode. in out and out are distinct. A spec declaration terminates at its ;,"
       & " a body declaration at its is "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so a patched body declaration is replaced without touching the body proper."
       & " The original vendored sources are never touched. gnatprove runs against the"
       & " copy"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s root project ( <copy>/<basename>.gpr)\\nand the resulting gnatprove.out is"
       & " copied back to <target>/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out for the assessment pipe"
       & "line. The\\ncopy lives under the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
