       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Result caching"",""id"":""180"",""title"":""Result caching""},""181"":{""body"":""adacove"
       & "x uses a native zero-dependency test framework ( Adacovex.Test_Support) with"
       & " 1181 tests across 16 categories. No external test framework (AUnit, and mor"
       & "e) is required. Test results are written to docs/test_result.md in a parseab"
       & "le Markdown table format."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Testing"",""id"":""181"",""title"":""Testing""},""182"":{""body"":""The complexity subcom"
       & "mand walks the whole target and scores many languages\\n(C, C++, C#, Go, Jav"
       & "a, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Ruby, PHP, Rust,\\nShell, Kotlin, and the"
       & " YAML/JSON/TOML/XML/Markdown/reStructuredText\\nfamilies) alongside Ada. Per"
       & "-subprogram analysis stays Ada-specific; the\\nother languages contribute fi"
       & "le-level lines of code and decision counts. --excludes=EXT,EXT skips listed "
       & "file extensions and is rejected unless the complexity subcommand is given, s"
       & "o it can never run on its own. make complexity-check gates the tree through "
       & "the same thresholds."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Complexity check"",""id"":""182"",""title"":""Complexity check""},""183"":{""body"":""ada"
       & "covex honours the operating system"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s timezone by default. The resolved\\noffset comes from Ada.Calendar.Time_Zo"
       & "nes.UTC_Time_Offset, the standard\\nAda runtime, which reads the TZ variable"
       & " and the system timezone through\\nthe C library, so the default is always t"
       & "he operator"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s wall clock\\n(DST-aware). status reports the effective timezone, the curre"
       & "nt date and\\ntime in it, and how many dated release changelogs the target c"
       & "arries under docs/changelogs. --tz / --timezone override the display zone fo"
       & "r one invocation. The\\nvalue is either a well-known IANA name (for example "
       & "Asia/Singapore) or a\\nfixed UTC/ GMT offset ( UTC+8, GMT+8, UTC+08, GMT+08,"
       & " UTC+08:30). adacovex ships no timezone database, so a named zone\\nresolves"
       & " from a built-in table of common IANA names and their standard-time\\noffset"
       & "s. A zone that may observe daylight saving time (marked in the\\ntable), or "
       & "one the table lacks, is probed against the platform tzdata\\n( zdump validat"
       & "es the name, date +%z reads the current offset, both\\nthrough one shell com"
       & "mand) for the DST-correct offset; the table offset is\\nthe fallback when th"
       & "e probe is unavailable. The date/time rendering\\ncompensates for GNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s local-time calendar accessors, so the displayed wall\\nclock is correct in"
       & " every zone. HLR-TZ covers this behaviour."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architec"
       & "ture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Timezone resolution"",""id"":""183"",""title"":""Timezone resolution""},""184"":{""body"
       & """:""Two cheap Python gates keep the dashboard and the hand-written docs in\\n"
       & "step with the code, and both run inside make check: tools/csslint.py ( make "
       & "csslint-check) enforces the dashboard spacing\\nconvention: every margin, pa"
       & "dding, and gap pixel length is a\\nmultiple of 4px. It also runs inside make"
       & " build. tools/check-docs.py ( make docs-check) fails when any paragraph in t"
       & "he\\nuser docs, README, or human changelogs exceeds four sentences, and it\\"
       & "nrejects em dashes and Latin abbreviations ( i.e., e.g., etc.). tools/para-s"
       & "plit.py rewraps over-long paragraphs to comply. The generated docs/api-docs "
       & "pages are excluded from the paragraph rule;\\nits source docstrings carry th"
       & "e same rule."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Build and documentation gates"",""id"":""184"",""title"":""Build and documentation "
       & "gates""},""185"":{""body"":""adacovex supports the same platforms Alire itself sup"
       & "ports. Because Alire is\\nthe packaging and delivery mechanism, adacovex inh"
       & "erits Alire"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s\\nsupported-platform matrix. The crate builds via alr build. It is distrib"
       & "uted\\nthrough the Alire community index ( alr install covex). The release w"
       & "orkflow\\nbuilds it with the Alire toolchain: Binary distribution: Linux x86"
       & "-64, Windows x86-64, and macOS x86-64\\n(the platforms for which Alire publi"
       & "shes binary releases and GNAT FSF\\ntoolchains, including cross compilers fo"
       & "r ARM, RISC-V, and AVR). From source: any platform with a GNAT FSF 9.2+ comp"
       & "iler on which Alire\\ncan be built (Alire lists FreeBSD and OpenBSD among bu"
       & "ildable hosts). GitHub release bundles: built on GitHub"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Linux runners and distributed\\nas adacovex-vX.Y.Z.tar.gz for every tag. T"
       & "he GitHub Actions composite action pins gnat-version (default 16.1.0) via al"
       & "ire-project/setup-alire, and CI runs on ubuntu-latest, so the CI-verified\\n"
       & "platform is Linux x86-64. The tool itself is written in portable Ada 2012 us"
       & "ing\\nonly the GNAT runtime, so no adacovex code is platform-specific beyond"
       & " what the\\nGNAT runtime and Alire toolchain provide."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacov"
       & "ex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Supported Platforms"",""id"":""185"",""title"":""Supported Platforms""},""186"":{""body"
       & """:""adacovex follows one version across every delivery channel, and each chan"
       & "nel is\\nversion-locked to the same release: Single source of truth: the ver"
       & "sion field in alire.toml / alire-dev.toml is the single source, resolved by "
       & "installation method. tools/gen-version.py regenerates src/adacovex_version_i"
       & "nfo.ads at build time (and make bump-version). It reads the first available "
       & "of ADACOVEX_VERSION (release builds), alire-dev.toml (source checkouts), or "
       & "alire.toml (dependency-managed installs). For dependency-managed installs, t"
       & "he published crate builds from its release manifest, so the toml associated "
       & "with the covex binary for dependency management carries the version. Adacove"
       & "x. Version in src/adacovex.ads re-exports the version. As a result, --versio"
       & "n, the man page, the SBOM tool version, and the result-cache namespace all d"
       & "erive from the manifest and can never drift. Release builds bundle the relea"
       & "se tag instead via the ADACOVEX_VERSION environment variable (release workfl"
       & "ow / make release). CI is tied to the release version: the GitHub Actions co"
       & "mposite action\\n( action.yml) is version-matched to the adacovex binary. Th"
       & "e release workflow bundles adacovex-vX. Y. Z.tar.gz and `adacovex-action-vX."
       & " Y. Z.tar.gz for everyvX. Y. Z tag, and the action downloads the binary for "
       & "the tag it is referenced by (@vX. Y. Z runs that exact version). Floating ta"
       & "gs (vMAJOR , vMAJOR. MINOR , latest ) are force-pushed at release time so @l"
       & "atest /@v1 /@v1.3` always resolve to the newest matching release. CI platfor"
       & "m/compiler: CI validates the self-assessment (build, prove,\\ntests) with th"
       & "e pinned gnat-version on ubuntu-latest, so the CI-proven\\ncombination is th"
       & "e released binary built against that exact toolchain. Attestation: every rel"
       & "ease bundle is attested with actions/attest (OIDC), and the release notes li"
       & "nk the\\nsigned attestation."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Delivery and Versioning"",""id"":""186"",""title"":""Delivery and Versioning""},""187"
       & """:{""body"":""The Alire GNAT toolchain"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s bundled ld (2.44) emits a benign message\\n( error in ...(.sframe); no .sf"
       & "rame will be created) when it reads the .sframe section that newer system bi"
       & "nutils wrote into the glibc startup\\nobjects. The link still succeeds. make"
       & " build filters only this one message;\\nall compiler and gnatprove warnings "
       & "remain fully visible, so nothing real is\\never suppressed."",""breadcrumbs"":"""
       & "adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Build-time linker output (SFrame)"",""id"":""187"",""title"":""Build-time linker ou"
       & "tput (SFrame)""},""188"":{""body"":""adacovex itself is read-only. It merely scans"
       & " your codebase for target docstrings and proofs. It does not make edits in p"
       & "lace or on your behalf."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Read Only"",""id"":""188"",""title"":""Read Only""},""189"":{""body"":""adacovex lets you"
       & " write proofs and decide where proofs are pointless (for\\nexample code that"
       & " has to involve manual memory management). You just have to\\njustify your r"
       & "ationale. The tool is not rigid. It does not expect 100% proving\\nfor all u"
       & "se cases. You write the proofs yourself, so there is no magic or hidden abst"
       & "ractions here."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Flexible"",""id"":""189"",""title"":""Flexible""},""19"":{""body"":""adacovex [options]\\"
       & "nadacovex sbom [--format=cyclonedx-json|spdx-json|md] [--out=PATH] [--standa"
       & "rd=NAME|--dal=LEVEL|--asil=LEVEL|--class=LEVEL]\\nadacovex prove [--target=P"
       & "ATH] [prove options]\\nadacovex status [--target=PATH]\\nadacovex man [--che"
       & "ck|--force] [--dir=PATH]\\nadacovex completion [bash|fish|zsh|pwsh]"",""breadc"
       & "rumbs"":""adacovex CLI Reference "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Usage"",""id"":""19"",""title"":""Usage""},""190"":{""body"":""When adacovex runs, it exe"
       & "cutes these steps in sequence: 0. Parse CLI args -> CLI_Config record (prove"
       & " / sbom / diff / man / complexity / normal)\\n0a. Early-exit modes -> --help"
       & " / --version / man / status / complexity exit before the pipeline\\n1. Deter"
       & "mine ANSI color -> NO_COLOR check\\n2. (prove mode) Run GNATprove -> fresh o"
       & "bj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out\\n3. Scan source files -> Package_Vectors.Vector "
       & "(subprograms, HLR tags, docstrings)\\n4. Apply docstring patches -> Merge .a"
       & "dacovex/patches/ (strict mode only)\\n5. Compute doc metrics -> Docstring_Me"
       & "trics (coverage %)\\n6. Parse GNATprove output -> Proof_Summary (VC counts, "
       & "SPARK level)\\n7. Parse test results -> Test_Summary (pass/fail counts)\\n8."
       & " Assess DAL compliance -> DAL_Assessment (Achieved / Unmet + reasons)\\n9. R"
       & "ender ANSI summary -> stdout (terminal report)\\n10. Emit SVG badges -> <svg"
       & "-dir>/*.svg (if enabled)\\n11. Emit Markdown reports -> <md-dir>/VERIFICATIO"
       & "N.md + TRACE.md (if enabled)\\n12. Emit automatic SBOM -> <target>/sbom.json"
       & " | sbom.spdx.json | docs/compliance/SBOM.md (unless --no-sbom)\\n13. Start H"
       & "TTP server -> :<port> (if --serve; serves the dashboard, the JSON API, the S"
       & "VG badges, and the bundled offline manual at /docs)\\n14. Set exit code -> 0"
       & " if Achieved, 1 if Unmet Differential modes ( --compare-base / --coverage-de"
       & "lta) run before the\\npipeline and snapshot a base revision via Adacovex.VCS"
       & " (git worktree add,\\nhg archive, svn export, fossil open on a copied DB, or"
       & " a git worktree\\nagainst the jj store), assess base and current tree, repor"
       & "t the delta, and\\nexit. man installs the generated man page ( Adacovex.Rend"
       & "erers.Man) into\\nthe local man database ( ~/.local/share/man, Linux/WSL) an"
       & "d refreshes it with mandb."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Pipeline (execution order)"",""id"":""190"",""title"":""Pipeline (execution order)"""
       & "},""191"":{""body"":""adacovex and Alire both default to the GCC-based GNAT ( gna"
       & "t_native)\\ncompiler. No action is needed. Only swap if you specifically wan"
       & "t an\\nLLVM-backend GNAT (for example GNAT LLVM) for your target project "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " for\\nexample to exercise dissimilar redundancy via diverse code generation"
       & ". GNAT LLVM is not yet packaged as a standard Alire toolchain crate, so two\"
       & "\npaths exist: Alire-managed compiler (preferred when available). If a GNAT "
       & "LLVM binary\\nrelease becomes available in the Alire index, declare it in yo"
       & "ur alire.toml / alire-dev.toml: [[depends-on]]\\ngnat_llvm = \\""*\\"" alr the"
       & "n selects it automatically for that project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s builds. You can also\\npick a default compiler for all projects with alr t"
       & "oolchain --select --disable-assistant and choosing the LLVM GNAT. System-ins"
       & "talled GNAT LLVM. Install GNAT LLVM on $PATH, then force the\\nAda toolchain"
       & " in the root .gpr so gprbuild does not fall back to the\\nGCC GNAT: for Tool"
       & "chain_Name (\\""Ada\\"") use \\""GNAT_LLVM\\""; You can confirm which compiler b"
       & "uilt a given .ali file by its first line\\n( GNAT vs GNAT-LLVM). Notes: GNAT"
       & " LLVM and GCC GNAT are not guaranteed ABI-compatible. Compile all Ada in\\na"
       & " project with the same compiler. GNAT LLVM"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s -fstack-check support is partial and some features\\n( Scalar_Storage_Orde"
       & "r, Convention C++) differ from GCC GNAT. SPARK proof results are compiler-in"
       & "dependent, so covex prove and the\\nDAL assessment are unaffected by the cho"
       & "ice."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex Architecture Decisions "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Swapping the GNAT compiler (LLVM backend)"",""id"":""191"",""title"":""Swapping the"
       & " GNAT compiler (LLVM backend)""},""192"":{""body"":""This table groups adacovex de"
       & "pendencies by category. Alire-managed\\ndependencies are listed under their "
       & "Alire crate names."",""breadcrumbs"":""Dependencies "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Dependencies"",""id"":""192"",""title"":""Dependencies""},""193"":{""body"":""These are r"
       & "equired to build or run adacovex. Dependency Category Managed by Notes GNAT "
       & "runtime Core GNAT toolchain Required. No other library is needed. GNAT compi"
       & "ler Core GNAT toolchain Required for build. gnatprove Core Alire (dev) or PA"
       & "TH Required for covex prove. Resolved at run time."",""breadcrumbs"":""Dependenc"
       & "ies "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Core"",""id"":""193"",""title"":""Core""},""194"":{""body"":""These are required to devel"
       & "op, test, or document adacovex. Dependency Category Managed by Notes Alire ("
       & " alr) Development System PATH Required for build, test, and release. gnatpro"
       & "ve Development Alire (dev) Required for make prove. gnatdoc Development Alir"
       & "e (dev) Required for make doc. gnatformat Development Alire (dev) Required f"
       & "or make fmt. Python 3 Development System Required for tools/*.py scripts. Pl"
       & "aywright Development npm/pnpm Required for make e2e."",""breadcrumbs"":""Depende"
       & "ncies "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Development"",""id"":""194"",""title"":""Development""},""195"":{""body"":""These are opt"
       & "ional but improve the workflow. Dependency Category Managed by Notes hyperfi"
       & "ne Good to have System Improves make bench with stable timings. strace Good "
       & "to have System Required for make perf-bench. linux-tools-common ( perf) Good"
       & " to have System Required for make perf-bench. mandb Good to have System Refr"
       & "eshes the man page after adacovex man."",""breadcrumbs"":""Dependencies "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Good to have"",""id"":""195"",""title"":""Good to have""},""196"":{""body"":""adacovex is"
       & " a zero-dependency CLI. Its hot path is the assessment pipeline\\n(scan -> p"
       & "atch -> doc metrics -> proof parse -> test parse -> DAL assess ->\\nrender, "
       & "plus the SBOM). This page documents how to benchmark it. It also\\ndocuments"
       & " the expected numbers on a typical machine and the optimisations\\nthat keep"
       & " those numbers low."",""breadcrumbs"":""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Performance"",""id"":""196"",""title"":""Performance""},""197"":{""body"":""make bench be"
       & "nchmarks the assessment pipeline and reports binary size: It builds the proj"
       & "ect, then times ./bin/adacovex against the repo itself. cold runs (fresh res"
       & "ult cache + probe cache) and warm runs\\n(populated caches) are measured sep"
       & "arately. make bench uses hyperfine when\\ninstalled. It falls back to the ba"
       & "sh time builtin otherwise. No tooling is\\nrequired. It samples generously s"
       & "o the reported mean is stable. Hyperfine runs 10\\ncold + 15 warm repetition"
       & "s (2 warmup runs). Each cold repetition deletes\\nthe cache dir first. This "
       & "measures a truly empty result and probe cache. The time fallback runs 5 cold"
       & " + 5 warm. It reports the raw and stripped binary sizes (the stripped size i"
       & "s measured\\non a /tmp copy; the build output is never modified). Example ou"
       & "tput (hyperfine, x86-64, 8-core CI-class machine, 1.28.0): === Cold (fresh r"
       & "esult cache) === Time (mean +/- sigma): 88.1 ms +/- 3.8 ms [User: 62.1 ms, S"
       & "ystem: 14.0 ms] Range (min ... max): 84.8 ms ... 96.4 ms 10 runs\\n=== Warm "
       & "(populated caches) === Time (mean +/- sigma): 34.2 ms +/- 2.3 ms [User: 15.3"
       & " ms, System: 8.7 ms] Range (min ... max): 30.9 ms ... 39.2 ms 15 runs == Bin"
       & "ary size ==\\nbin/adacovex 9.0 MiB (9461040 bytes)\\nafter strip 4.3 MiB (44"
       & "63704 bytes)\\nsavings 52.8% The numbers shift with the machine and the code"
       & "base. What matters is the\\nshape: warm is now in the tens of milliseconds, "
       & "and the cold path is bounded\\nby the work that genuinely must happen (hashi"
       & "ng the changed sources and\\nbuilding the SBOM). For single-shot timings, pl"
       & "ain time works the same way: time ./bin/adacovex --no-cache # cold, no resul"
       & "t cache\\ntime ./bin/adacovex --cache-dir=/tmp/c # warm When you compare two"
       & " versions, always reset the cache between runs. Use --cache-dir=<fresh dir> "
       & "or delete the cache dir. The result cache must not\\nhide the real cost. mak"
       & "e perf-bench profiles CPU and syscalls directly with perf and strace over bi"
       & "n/adacovex. It prints the cache-miss rates and the syscall\\ncounts so a reg"
       & "ression in I/O or data layout is visible before a release."",""breadcrumbs"":""P"
       & "erformance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Benchmarking"",""id"":""197"",""title"":""Benchmarking""},""198"":{""body"":""Figures bel"
       & "ow are from make bench/ perf-bench on this machine (hyperfine,\\ncold + warm"
       & ", 2 warmup). They shift with the machine and the codebase. What\\nmatters is"
       & " the shape: Cold ~0.1 s: dominated by source scanning (Ada file enumeration "
       & "and\\nSHA-256 of every scanned file), the SBOM tree walk and word scan, and "
       & "the\\nrenderers. Nothing here can be skipped: the result cache is empty, so\"
       & "\nevery file must be read and hashed at least once. The system-tool version\"
       & "\nprobes are not part of cold anymore (they live per-machine and are\\ncache"
       & "d across cache wipes). Warm ~35 ms: the on-disk result cache (content-addres"
       & "sed per file,\\noldest-first eviction) skips re-parsing unchanged sources. T"
       & "he stamp\\nfast-path skips the per-file SHA-256 entirely (a file unchanged i"
       & "n size is\\nnot re-hashed). The tools-set cache skips the whole SBOM dev-dep"
       & "endency\\nword scan and the tool probes for an unchanged project. The remain"
       & "ing\\ntime is process startup (dynamic loader hwcaps probing, elaboration), "
       & "the\\ndirectory walks, and the blob deserialization. System time is the tell"
       & ". Cold runs show ~13 ms of system time (file I/O);\\nwarm runs show ~9 ms."","
       & """breadcrumbs"":""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " What the numbers mean"",""id"":""198"",""title"":""What the numbers mean""},""199"":{"""
       & "body"":""Kept in reverse-chronological order. Every entry names the measuremen"
       & "t that\\ndrove it so the next round of work can see whether the previous ass"
       & "umption\\nstill holds."",""breadcrumbs"":""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Optimisation history"",""id"":""199"",""title"":""Optimisation history""},""2"":{""body"
       & """:""CLI reference "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every command, flag, and exit\\ncode. Web dashboard "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the HTML report and JSON API. SBOM "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the software-bill-of-materials generator. Standards "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " DO-178C, ISO 26262, and IEC 62304\\nlevels. Platforms "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " supported platforms and toolchain\\nstate. VCS support "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " differential assessment across git, hg,\\nsvn, fossil, and jj. CI/CD "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the GitHub Action and the workflow summary. Changelog "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " release history."",""breadcrumbs"":""Adacovex manual "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Using adacovex"",""id"":""2"",""title"":""Using adacovex""},""20"":{""body"":""Flag Defau"
       & "lt Mode Description --target=PATH . (CWD) both Target project root directory"
       & " --manifest=PATH auto-detected both Override project manifest path --dal=LEV"
       & "EL C both DO-178C DAL level (A-E, also the shared rigour tier) --asil=LEVEL "
       & "- both ISO 26262 level: A| B| C| D| QM --class=LEVEL - both IEC 62304 safety"
       & " class: A| B| C --standard=NAME do178c both do178c| iso26262| iec62304| all "
       & "--serve off both Start HTTP dashboard server (standard-aware, light/dark/sys"
       & "tem themes) --serve-workers=N 4 serve HTTP server task-pool worker count --t"
       & "heme=NAME system serve Dashboard theme: light| dark| system --port=N 8080 se"
       & "rve Dashboard server port --tz=ZONE / --timezone=ZONE OS timezone both Displ"
       & "ay timezone (IANA name or UTC/GMT offset) --excludes=EXT,EXT empty complexit"
       & "y Skip comma-separated file extensions --emit-svg=PATH <target>/docs/badges "
       & "both Output directory for SVG badges --no-svg off both Suppress SVG badge ou"
       & "tput --emit-markdown=PATH off both Output directory for Markdown reports --e"
       & "mit-metrics=PATH off both Write a JSON export of metrics + dependency graph "
       & "to PATH --completion[=SHELL] - - Print shell completion script (bash/fish/zs"
       & "h/pwsh, auto-detected) and exit --skip-dir=NAME demo,deps,examples relaxed D"
       & "irectory name to skip (repeatable) --relaxed off both Disable strict mode (s"
       & "kip dirs, no patches) --compare-base=REF off both Differential mode vs a bas"
       & "e rev (git/hg/svn/fossil/jj) --coverage-delta=REF off both Docstring-coverag"
       & "e gate vs a base rev (git/hg/svn/fossil/jj) --cache on both Enable on-disk r"
       & "esult caching --no-cache off both Disable result caching (always re-scan/re-"
       & "parse/re-prove) --cache-dir=PATH ~/.adacovex/cache/<ver>/<schema> both Cache"
       & " directory for analysis results --cache-max=N 4096 both Max cache entries be"
       & "fore oldest-first eviction --no-sbom off both Skip the automatic SBOM writte"
       & "n at the end of every assessment --sbom-format=FMT cyclonedx-json both Forma"
       & "t of the automatic SBOM: cyclonedx-json| spdx-json| md --require-spark=LVL o"
       & "ff both Fail loudly (exit 1) if SPARK level < LVL (Stone..Platinum) --requir"
       & "e-docstrings=PCT off both Fail loudly if docstring coverage < PCT% (0-100) -"
       & "-require-tests=N off both Fail loudly if passing test count < N --require-pr"
       & "oof=PCT off both Fail loudly if proved-VC coverage < PCT% (0-100) --verbose "
       & "off both Verbose diagnostics --version - - Print the bundled version and exi"
       & "t man - - Install the man page into the local man database man --check - - E"
       & "xit 0 if the installed man page matches the binary version, 1 otherwise man "
       & "--force - - Reinstall the man page even when it already matches (repair) man"
       & " --dir=PATH ~/.local/share/man - Install the man page under PATH/man1 instea"
       & "d --help - both Print usage and exit prove-mode flags are also accepted by t"
       & "he main command. They are validated\\nonly in prove mode. The flags are: --j"
       & "obs/ -j, --level, --timeout, --steps, --memlimit, --force, --no-loop-unrolli"
       & "ng, --no-inlining, --suppress-warnings, --quiet. See The prove subcommand."","
       & """breadcrumbs"":""adacovex CLI Reference "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Flags"",""id"":""20"",""title"":""Flags""},""200"":{""body"":""The warm-path profile show"
       & "ed GNAT. SHA256 at ~48% of CPU: every .ads file was fully re-read and re-has"
       & "hed on every run just to compute its cache key, even though the content was "
       & "unchanged. Hash_File now keeps an in-memory map of path -> (size, digest). A"
       & " file whose size still matches the recorded size serves the recorded digest "
       & "without opening or reading the file. The fast path is used only within one p"
       & "rocess (the map is not persisted), so a content change is always caught (the"
       & " size differs or the map is empty). The same fast path serves the SBOM tree-"
       & "walk hashing, which re-hashes files the source scan already touched in the s"
       & "ame run (the two hash passes collapse into one real read + one size check). "
       & "Warm user time dropped roughly a third."",""breadcrumbs"":""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Stamp fast-path hashing (1.28.0)"",""id"":""200"",""title"":""Stamp fast-path hashi"
       & "ng (1.28.0)""},""201"":{""body"":""The cold profile was dominated by the system-to"
       & "ol version probes: each\\nspawns a subprocess, and node/hg/mandb boot an int"
       & "erpreter (hg alone cost\\n~330 ms on this machine; the full probe set ~150 m"
       & "s end to end). The\\nprobes were kept under the result cache ( <cache-dir>/p"
       & "robes/), so\\nwiping the cache (or pointing --cache-dir elsewhere) re-probed"
       & " every\\ntool. Two changes removed that cost: Probes now live in ~/.adacovex"
       & "/probes/ "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a stable, machine-level\\nstore external to the result cache. Wiping the re"
       & "sult cache (or using a\\nfresh --cache-dir) no longer re-probes; only the 7-"
       & "day TTL ever\\nre-probes a known toolchain. Cold on a warm-probe machine dro"
       & "pped from\\n~658 ms to ~86 ms (7.7 x). The tools-set cache blob now also sto"
       & "res each referenced tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s probe\\nresult ( tool=version pairs), and a cache hit rebuilds the SBOM to"
       & "ol\\nedges from those pairs without PATH lookups, probe file reads, or\\nsub"
       & "process spawns. Warm dropped from ~39.8 ms to ~34.6 ms. The blob\\nformat is"
       & " names- |-version-pairs; Cache_Schema was bumped to s6 so\\nold names-only b"
       & "lobs are never served as if complete. Cold and warm\\nSBOM output stays byte"
       & "-identical."",""breadcrumbs"":""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Stable probe store + probe results in the tools blob (1.28.0)"",""id"":""201"","""
       & "title"":""Stable probe store + probe results in the tools blob (1.28.0)""},""202"
       & """:{""body"":""Put_Cached ran eviction after every store; eviction walks the who"
       & "le cache\\ntree. It now runs every 32 stores (bounded overshoot under the so"
       & "ft cap).\\nThe SBOM dev-dependency word scan was rewritten from a per-tool s"
       & "ubstring\\nmatch (60 tools x line length) to a single-pass word extraction ("
       & "per-word x\\ndistinct tool lengths), and tool-output directories ( gnatprove"
       & "/, __pycache__, node_modules, .headroom, .lccst) were excluded from\\nboth t"
       & "ree walks so the proof-run output is not enumerated. Those changes\\nalone t"
       & "ook the warm run from ~1.02 s to ~63 ms (16x) and cold from ~1.4 s\\nto ~545"
       & " ms, and reduced the warm-run syscall count from ~15k to ~12k."",""breadcrumbs"
       & """:""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " File-stamp fast-path and eviction batching (1.27.0)"",""id"":""202"",""title"":""Fi"
       & "le-stamp fast-path and eviction batching (1.27.0)""},""203"":{""body"":""(Origin s"
       & "tory.) The SBOM builds a dev-scope dependency edge for every tool that the\\"
       & "ntarget"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s build references. "
       ;

   Asset_151 : aliased constant String :=
       "The tool must be installed on $PATH (for example gcc, alr, git, make). The S"
       & "BOM probes each tool with <tool> <flag> to capture its version. Each probe s"
       & "pawns a subprocess. The subprocess costs tens of milliseconds per referenced"
       & " tool ( System: 42 ms -> 9 ms, ~150 ms end to end on an 11-tool toolchain). "
       & "Originally the probed versions were cached under <cache-root>/probes/<tool> "
       & "with a 7-day TTL. That location meant a wiped result cache re-probed every t"
       & "ool on the next run "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " which is why 1.28.0 moved the store and folded the probe results into the t"
       & "ools-set cache blob (see above)."",""breadcrumbs"":""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Probe cache"",""id"":""203"",""title"":""Probe cache""},""204"":{""body"":""The debug-sym"
       & "bol-carrying build is ~9 MiB. Stripping ( strip bin/adacovex) yields ~3.6 Mi"
       & "B (~60% smaller) without affecting behaviour. GNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default build keeps symbols for debugging ( gdb works). Release artifacts "
       & "are stripped. make bench always reports both. Regressions in code size are v"
       & "isible in the same command that reports timings. If the symbols ever come ou"
       & "t, the binary size is the same and the page should say so."",""breadcrumbs"":""P"
       & "erformance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Binary size"",""id"":""204"",""title"":""Binary size""},""205"":{""body"":""CI runs the s"
       & "elf-assessment with result caching disabled where determinism matters ( --no"
       & "-cache-equivalent fresh dirs). The make gates are timed loosely. Timings are"
       & " informational only. The bench target is not part of make check. It makes th"
       & "e gate machine-dependent. A slow CI runner must not fail a build. The target"
       & " is run by hand before releases."",""breadcrumbs"":""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " CI"",""id"":""205"",""title"":""CI""},""206"":{""body"":""Run make perf-bench first. It r"
       & "eports the CPU break-down (the wall-clock perf output) and the strace syscal"
       & "l counts. The single-reader/single-writer\\ncache walks are the usual suspec"
       & "ts: a new tree walk that re-enumerates a\\ndirectory which a cache already c"
       & "overs, or a new per-file hash that the\\nstamp fast path does not cover. The"
       & " numbers in this page are from the\\nself-assessment; the Ada_CRDT target is"
       & " smaller and exercises the same\\npipeline, so make run-ada-crdt is a handy "
       & "second datapoint."",""breadcrumbs"":""Performance "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " When the numbers regress"",""id"":""206"",""title"":""When the numbers regress""},""2"
       & "07"":{""body"":""ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English (Section 1, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Words"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ") defines a\\ncontrolled vocabulary. Most words in that vocabulary are stand"
       & "ard STE words.\\nSome concepts have no accurate standard STE word. For those"
       & " concepts, the\\nproject approves a Technical Name (TN). A Technical Name is"
       & " a non-STE word that the project explicitly approves. The\\nproject approves"
       & " it because no standard STE word describes the concept with\\nthe same preci"
       & "sion. A TN has a single mandatory part of speech and a defined\\nscope. The "
       & "scope is restricted to the software domain of adacovex. This page is the con"
       & "trolled list of Technical Names for adacovex. Writers of\\nuser documentatio"
       & "n, API documentation, docstrings, and changelogs must use\\nthese terms as d"
       & "efined here. If you need a term that is not in this list,\\nadd it to the li"
       & "st first, then use it."",""breadcrumbs"":""STE100 Technical Names for adacovex "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " STE100 Technical Names for adacovex"",""id"":""207"",""title"":""STE100 Technical N"
       & "ames for adacovex""},""208"":{""body"":""Group the Technical Names by their struct"
       & "ural role in the software domain. Hardware and System Entities. Physical com"
       & "ponents, buses, or\\nmicroarchitectures that the Ada code interacts with. Fo"
       & "r example, CPU core. Ada Language Constructs. Specific language features tha"
       & "t generic\\nEnglish words cannot replace without losing technical precision."
       & " For\\nexample, pragma, discriminant, rendezvous, task. Domain and Mathemati"
       & "cal Terms. Algorithmic, mathematical, or\\nmission-specific logic terms. For"
       & " example, telemetry, checksum,\\nquaternion. Code Identifier Names. Exact pa"
       & "ckage, type, subtype, subprogram, and\\nvariable names as declared in the so"
       & "urce code. For example, System.Storage_Elements, Buffer_Size. This category "
       & "also covers exact\\nfile names, tool commands, and flag names that appear in"
       & " documentation."",""breadcrumbs"":""STE100 Technical Names for adacovex "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Categories for Ada Technical Names"",""id"":""208"",""title"":""Categories for Ada "
       & "Technical Names""},""209"":{""body"":""ASD-STE100 requires strict controls over ho"
       & "w approved words are documented.\\nEvery Technical Name in this dictionary h"
       & "as all five fields: Field Description Example Approved Word (TN) The exact w"
       & "ord or identifier. Pragma Part of Speech STE permits a word as only one part"
       & " of speech (Noun, Verb, Modifier). Noun Approved Meaning / Definition Clear,"
       & " unambiguous definition restricted to the adacovex domain. A compiler direct"
       & "ive in the Ada programming language. Non-Approved Alternatives Terms that au"
       & "thors must NOT use instead of this TN. Compiler directive, Annotation Exampl"
       & "e Sentence A compliant STE sentence demonstrating usage. Add the pragma to t"
       & "he top of the package specification."",""breadcrumbs"":""STE100 Technical Names "
       & "for adacovex "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Required data fields for each entry"",""id"":""209"",""title"":""Required data fiel"
       & "ds for each entry""},""21"":{""body"":"""",""breadcrumbs"":""adacovex CLI Reference "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Flag details"",""id"":""21"",""title"":""Flag details""},""210"":{""body"":""Nouns stay n"
       & "ouns. Technical Names are almost always approved as Nouns\\nor Modifiers. Ne"
       & "ver approve a code action as a verb if a standard STE verb\\nexists. For exa"
       & "mple, use the approved verb Calculate instead of creating\\na TN verb Comput"
       & "e. Exact case matching. Treat Ada identifiers ( Pascal_Case or UPPER_CASE) a"
       & "s literal Technical Names. Use the exact casing in\\ndocumentation. This rul"
       & "e distinguishes language concepts from code\\nentities. No synonyms. If the "
       & "project approves Task as a TN for an Ada\\nconcurrent execution unit, do not"
       & " use words like Thread, Process, or Job for that concept. One part of speech"
       & " per word. A TN is a Noun or a Modifier, never both.\\nWhen you need the act"
       & "ion, use the standard STE verb that matches the noun\\nform."",""breadcrumbs"":"
       & """STE100 Technical Names for adacovex "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Key rules for Ada Technical Names"",""id"":""210"",""title"":""Key rules for Ada Te"
       & "chnical Names""},""211"":{""body"":""### Technical Name: Task\\n- **Part of Speech"
       & ":** Noun\\n- **Category:** Ada Language Construct\\n- **Definition:** A stan"
       & "dalone unit of concurrent execution in Ada.\\n- **Approved Form:** Task (sin"
       & "gular), Tasks (plural)\\n- **Do Not Use:** Thread, Process, Job, Execution U"
       & "nit\\n- **Correct Example:** *The main **task** waits for the sensor **task*"
       & "* to finish.*\\n- **Incorrect Example:** *The main process waits for the sen"
       & "sor thread to complete.*"",""breadcrumbs"":""STE100 Technical Names for adacovex"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
