       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " AI / LLM Usage in this Project"",""id"":""217"",""title"":""AI / LLM Usage in this "
       & "Project""},""218"":{""body"":""AI tools were used during development for boilerpla"
       & "te generation, contract drafting, and docstring formatting. This is stated p"
       & "lainly rather than hidden. The project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own dogfood target is a zero-dependency, fully documented, SPARK-proven Ad"
       & "a codebase. AI-generated contributions must meet the same bar as hand-writte"
       & "n ones. That bar is 100% docstring coverage, Platinum proof, zero justified "
       & "VCs, and the full make check gate before they count."",""breadcrumbs"":""AI / LL"
       & "M Usage in this Project "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " AI Assistance Disclosure"",""id"":""218"",""title"":""AI Assistance Disclosure""},""2"
       & "19"":{""body"":""Given the use of AI assistance, healthy skepticism is natural a"
       & "nd encouraged.\\nReliability is grounded in proof and design, not implicit t"
       & "rust: Formal Verification: core Ada logic is formally verified. It is Platin"
       & "um\\nunder gnatprove 16.1.0, 725 VCs, 0 unproved (see docs/proof/16.1.0-ledg"
       & "er.md). The proof is re-run by make prove on every change. It is a hard gate"
       & " before any release. Read-Only Engine: adacovex assesses input payloads, bui"
       & "ld artifacts, and\\nreports without modifying your source files in place. An"
       & " AI-assisted tool that\\ncannot write to the tree it audits is a smaller bla"
       & "st radius by design. Open Auditability: fully open source under Apache-2.0. "
       & "Every line, human\\nor AI-written, is inspectable. Still skeptical? See Ken "
       & "Thompson"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s landmark paper, Reflections on Trusting Trust,\\non the fundamental nature"
       & " of trust in software toolchains. The point is that no\\nsoftware, compiler,"
       & " or model is trustworthy purely by assertion. It must be\\ninspectable and i"
       & "ndependently verifiable."",""breadcrumbs"":""AI / LLM Usage in this Project "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Why trust this code?"",""id"":""219"",""title"":""Why trust this code?""},""22"":{""bod"
       & "y"":""Project to analyse. Relative paths are resolved against the current work"
       & "ing\\ndirectory to an absolute path. The path determines the root directory "
       & "for\\nsource scanning, manifest detection, SVG badge output, and patch file\"
       & "\nresolution. Default: the current working directory."",""breadcrumbs"":""adacov"
       & "ex CLI Reference "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " --target=PATH"",""id"":""22"",""title"":""--target=PATH""},""220"":{""body"":""AGENTS.md "
       & "at the repo root is the machine-readable project\\nbrief. It carries the arc"
       & "hitecture tree, the pipeline, the SPARK discipline,\\nthe Makefile targets, "
       & "and the verification gates. An agent (or human) working\\non the tree must r"
       & "ead it first. It must follow it. In particular: Match existing conventions a"
       & "nd prefer editing existing files. Verify\\nnon-trivial changes with the proj"
       & "ect"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s typecheck and tests. Zero library dependency is a hard constraint. Use onl"
       & "y the GNAT runtime.\\nKeep tools/*.py pure-stdlib, typing-annotated Python. "
       & "SPARK proof discipline (enforced by make prove and the spark-off-check gate)"
       & ": zero unproved VCs, zero justified VCs, no SPARK_Mode (Off) outside the Typ"
       & "es.Implementation and Complexity\\ncontainer packages (non-formal Ada.Contai"
       & "ners are illegal in\\nSPARK_Mode-On code; see docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md). "
       & "The quality gate is the contract. make check runs the same gates that\\nCI e"
       & "nforces before a release. A contribution that fails it is not done. Generate"
       & "d files are regenerated, not hand-edited. The version constant,\\nthe dashbo"
       & "ard template package, the architecture tree, the count-synced docs,\\nand th"
       & "e descriptions all come from tools/*.py scripts. Their --check\\nmodes verif"
       & "y they did not drift. The doc-sync tools ( tools/update-test-count.py and to"
       & "ols/update-proof-status.py) derive their file set from the tree itself ( too"
       & "ls/live_files.py). They do not use a hardcoded list. A stale metric cannot s"
       & "urvive anywhere. Generated outputs and historical records (past-release chan"
       & "gelogs, past proof ledgers) are excluded. They keep their release-time numbe"
       & "rs."",""breadcrumbs"":""AI / LLM Usage in this Project "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " How LLM agents work on this codebase"",""id"":""220"",""title"":""How LLM agents wo"
       & "rk on this codebase""},""221"":{""body"":""Every number in this repository"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s documentation is anchored to a generated\\nartifact, not to a human- or AI"
       & "-written claim: VC counts and the SPARK level come from obj/gnatprove/gnatpr"
       & "ove.out (via make proof-status). Test counts come from docs/test_result.md ("
       & "via make test-count). Crate descriptions come from alire/description.txt and"
       & " alire/long-description.txt (via make description). The CI badge docs/badges"
       & "/*.svg files are emitted by the assessment itself.\\nIf a document carries a"
       & " number that does not match the artifact, one of the --check gates in make c"
       & "heck fails loudly. That is the point."",""breadcrumbs"":""AI / LLM Usage in this"
       & " Project "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Verifying claims instead of trusting them"",""id"":""221"",""title"":""Verifying cl"
       & "aims instead of trusting them""},""222"":{""body"":""Because the gates are cheap a"
       & "nd deterministic, the safest workflow is to\\niterate locally and let make c"
       & "heck be the arbiter: make build && make test # native suite must stay 738/73"
       & "8\\nmake prove # Platinum, 0 unproved, 0 justified\\nmake check # full gate:"
       & " static checks, build, test, prove, # doc, sbom, then tree-wide count-sync c"
       & "hecks make check runs the cheap static gates first (ascii, spark-off, change"
       & "log, version source, doc links). A formatting or sync problem fails before t"
       & "he expensive build and SPARK proof. Then it verifies the count-sync checks ("
       & " test-count --check, proof-status --check, description --check). A stale met"
       & "ric anywhere in the tree fails loudly. Regenerated files that are byte-ident"
       & "ical when nothing changed (the version constant, the dashboard template) are"
       & " left untouched. git status stays quiet."",""breadcrumbs"":""AI / LLM Usage in t"
       & "his Project "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Working in a fork or branch (LLM or human)"",""id"":""222"",""title"":""Working in "
       & "a fork or branch (LLM or human)""},""223"":{""body"":""adacovex --serve renders a "
       & "live HTML dashboard at /. It also renders a JSON API at /api/metrics and SVG"
       & " badges at /badge/*.svg. The same numbers that an agent or reviewer quotes f"
       & "rom the CLI are visible and machine-checkable in the browser. The dashboard "
       & "shell is a real file ( resources/dashboard.html). It is bundled at build tim"
       & "e by tools/gen-dashboard.py. Page chrome is a plain HTML edit with no Ada kn"
       & "owledge required. The dynamic cards are injected by the Ada renderer. The th"
       & "eme resolution chain (query param, then explicit --theme, then saved localSt"
       & "orage, then system preference) and the localStorage-only persistence are doc"
       & "umented in dashboard.md."",""breadcrumbs"":""AI / LLM Usage in this Project "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " The served dashboard as a trust surface"",""id"":""223"",""title"":""The served das"
       & "hboard as a trust surface""},""224"":{""body"":""AI assistance raises the pace of "
       & "contribution but does not change the bar: An AI-written docstring that is no"
       & "t provably accurate is a liability, not a\\ncontribution. The 100% docstring"
       & "-coverage gate measures presence. Review\\nmeasures accuracy. Generated code"
       & " must still pass the SPARK proof. A pragma Assume or a SPARK_Mode (Off) outs"
       & "ide the two allowed container packages is rejected\\nby the gates. The chang"
       & "elog, the traceability tags, and the HLRs are written by people.\\nThey are "
       & "also written by agents following AGENTS.md. The changelog-check\\nvalidator "
       & "enforces the canonical format. A machine-generated changelog that\\ndoes not"
       & " conform is caught before release."",""breadcrumbs"":""AI / LLM Usage in this Pr"
       & "oject "
