       & """:{""body"":"""",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Fixes"",""id"":""725"",""title"":""Fixes""},""726"":{""body"":""The vendored JavaScript b"
       & "undles ( graphre.js, nomnoml.js, flexsearch.js, yace.js) sat at the resource"
       & "s/ root, but the vendored yace.js lived\\nunder resources/js/ with the autho"
       & "red dashboard modules. The SBOM asset\\nscanner treats resources/js/ as auth"
       & "ored dashboard code and skipped it, so\\nyace never became a dependency comp"
       & "onent. yace.js now sits at the resources/ root with the other vendored libra"
       & "ries, the layout clearly\\nseparates dependency JavaScript from dashboard Ja"
       & "vaScript, and the SBOM lists\\nyace (MIT, v1.1.0, pkg:generic/yace) alongsid"
       & "e the other bundled libraries."",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H1: Vendored yace.js now appears in the SBOM"",""id"":""726"",""title"":""H1: Vendo"
       & "red yace.js now appears in the SBOM""},""727"":{""body"":""The Docs_Subpath slicin"
       & "g assumed the request path started at index 1, but Get_Path returns a slice "
       & "of the request line, so every /docs/<subpath>\\nkept a leading slash and ret"
       & "urned 404 "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " only /docs and /docs/\\nresolved. The six-character prefix is now stripped "
       & "from the slice"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s actual\\nfirst index, so every page, stylesheet, and badge of the bundled "
       & "manual\\nserves (an e2e test pins the exact, nested, and extensionless subpa"
       & "ths plus\\na missing-page 404)."",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H3: /docs subpages are served again"",""id"":""727"",""title"":""H3: /docs subpages"
       & " are served again""},""728"":{""body"":""The dashboard server"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s fixed-size worker pool (4 workers) blocks each\\nworker on the next reques"
       & "t of a keep-alive connection. Browsers hold\\nseveral idle connections open,"
       & " so once all four workers were waiting on\\nsilent connections, the next req"
       & "uest queued forever "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the e2e suite\\nstarted hitting 60-second timeouts on /docs subpages as it "
       & "grew. Each\\naccepted socket now carries a 5-second receive timeout, and a t"
       & "imed-out\\n(or dropped) connection is closed in the worker"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s error path (which\\npreviously leaked the socket). A worker frees instead "
       & "of pinning the pool forever,\\nand the request is served. (The timeout was o"
       & "riginally 5s; H10 below\\nshortens it to half a second so a multi-asset docs"
       & " burst fans out across\\nthe pool instead of waiting one timeout per queued "
       & "connection.) The e2e\\nsuite returns to 28 passing in ~14 seconds."",""breadcr"
       & "umbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H5: Idle connections no longer pin the server worker pool"",""id"":""728"",""titl"
       & "e"":""H5: Idle connections no longer pin the server worker pool""},""729"":{""body"
       & """:""The complete-book offline manual is a 4 MB asset set, and gen-docs.py\\ne"
       & "mitted it as one giant &-concatenation chain (300k+ string literals).\\nGNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s frontend parses that tree fine, but gnatprove"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s flow analysis blew\\nits stack ( Storage_Error stack overflow at adacovex-"
       & "docs_template.ads),\\naborting make prove and therefore make check and every"
       & " release.\\nExperiments showed the limit is the constant size itself (a sing"
       & "le string\\nconstant over ~1 MB overflows whatever its structure), so the ge"
       & "nerated\\nspec now holds one aliased constant String per asset (the multi-MB"
       & "\\nsearch index is split into fixed-size chunks, each its own constant "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " 166\\nbodies in all), each well under the limit, never concatenated into on"
       & "e\\nvalue "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " with an Asset_Bodies access-to-constant table and an Asset_Index subtype so"
       & " Content (Idx) needs no unchecked bounds reasoning. The served bytes are\\nu"
       & "nchanged (each asset constant carries the identical content), the server\\nr"
       & "outes through the same Find lookup and streams the bodies (see C8), and\\nth"
       & "e bundle-links check still passes."",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H4: Bundled manual no longer overflows the gnatprove frontend"",""id"":""729"","""
       & "title"":""H4: Bundled manual no longer overflows the gnatprove frontend""},""73"""
       & ":{""body"":""Like the sbom subcommand, the dashboard defaults to all standards "
       & "when\\nno --standard / --asil / --class flag is given. The status badges and"
       & "\\nthe compliance card list every standard"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s label at the shared tier (DAL-C,\\nASIL B, Class A). An explicit standard "
       & "flag narrows the dashboard to that\\nsingle standard (for example --asil=B s"
       & "hows only ISO 26262 at ASIL B). See Standards for the cross-standard tier ma"
       & "pping."",""breadcrumbs"":""Web dashboard and JSON API "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Standard-awareness"",""id"":""73"",""title"":""Standard-awareness""},""730"":{""body"":"""
       & "The dashboard no longer lists the raw /api/* URIs or the ?theme= embed\\nhin"
       & "t in the footer. The footer now carries a single "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Generated by adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & "\\nline, and two obvious links "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Documentation (offline manual) ( /docs)\\nand Explore the API (jumps to the"
       & " API tab) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " sit in a prominent bar at\\nthe top of the page, below the dashboard title "
       & "and above the tab\\nselection, where a user sees them immediately. The API p"
       & "layground is now a split-screen layout mirroring the Dependencies tab: endpo"
       & "ints grouped by\\npurpose in a left-hand nav, live JSON/SVG/HTML response pr"
       & "eview docked on\\nthe right (stacking on narrow screens)."",""breadcrumbs"":""Ch"
       & "angelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H2: Dashboard docs links moved from the footer to a top bar"",""id"":""730"",""ti"
       & "tle"":""H2: Dashboard docs links moved from the footer to a top bar""},""731"":{"""
       & "body"":""The SBOM"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s system-tool discovery now recognises mdbook: it joined the\\ncurated Syste"
       & "m_Tools table, so a project whose build files reference mdbook (for example "
       & "a Markdown manual"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s mdbook build) gets it registered\\nas a system-scope dev dependency ( pkg:"
       & "generic/mdbook). The detection\\nstays data-driven "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adding a tool is one table entry, and the scan remains a\\ngeneric word-mat"
       & "ch over build files, not a hardcoded call site."",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H6: mdbook detected as a system dev dependency"",""id"":""731"",""title"":""H6: mdb"
       & "ook detected as a system dev dependency""},""732"":{""body"":""The .readthedocs.ya"
       & "ml build failed in CI with mdbook: not found even\\nthough cargo install mdb"
       & "ook succeeded. Read the Docs runs the install and\\nbuild jobs in separate s"
       & "hells, and cargo writes the binary into the Rust\\ntoolchain"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s bin directory, which is not on the build job"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s PATH. The build\\ncommand now resolves the cargo-installed mdbook binary ("
       & " find under $HOME) and prepends its directory to PATH before building, so th"
       & "e build\\nsurvives Rust toolchain upgrades without a hardcoded version path."
       & """,""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H7: Read the Docs build deploys again"",""id"":""732"",""title"":""H7: Read the Doc"
       & "s build deploys again""},""733"":{""body"":""Clicking an mdBook search result in t"
       & "he bundled manual returned 404. The /docs router dispatched on the query-str"
       & "ing-stripped path (so ?highlight=\\nreached the docs route), but the asset l"
       & "ookup that followed read the raw\\nrequest path, so every search result carr"
       & "ying ?highlight=... (mdBook"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s\\nmark-the-search-term parameter) was looked up as changelogs/"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & ".html?highlight="
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "\\nand never found. The docs asset key now derives from the query-stripped p"
       & "ath,\\nso a search-result link such as /docs/usage/cli-reference.html?highli"
       & "ght=serve#--serve resolves to the page,\\nthen the browser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own fragment + mark handling scrolls to the heading and\\nhighlights the t"
       & "erm "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " exactly as it does under mdbook serve."",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H9: Docs search-result links resolve again"",""id"":""733"",""title"":""H9: Docs se"
       & "arch-result links resolve again""},""734"":{""body"":""The bundled manual felt slo"
       & "w to open: a ~15-asset page (HTML + several CSS +\\nJS) took roughly six sec"
       & "onds to load. The 4-worker server pool pinned each\\nworker to its keep-aliv"
       & "e connection for a 5-second idle receive timeout, so\\nonce four sockets wer"
       & "e held by the browser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s parallel asset requests, the\\nremaining connections queued in the accept "
       & "backlog for ~5s until a worker\\nreleased. The idle timeout is now half a se"
       & "cond: a worker that finishes a\\nkeep-alive exchange returns to Accept_Socke"
       & "t quickly, the burst fan-outs\\nacross the pool, and a docs page loads in we"
       & "ll under a second. Workers are\\nreleased faster on idle connections, which "
       & "also means a stale or abandoned\\nconnection is reaped sooner than before."","
       & """breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " H10: Docs pages load quickly again"",""id"":""734"",""title"":""H10: Docs pages loa"
       & "d quickly again""},""735"":{""body"":""tools/gen-docs.py dropped the bundling-irre"
       & "levant font stylesheet link from\\neach bundled page, but its pattern only m"
       & "atched the index page"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s href=\\""fonts/"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "css\\"" shape. Subpages link the same stylesheet with a path_to_root prefix ("
       & " ../fonts/"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "css), so those kept the reference and the\\nbrowser issued a /fonts/...css 4"
       & "04 on every subpage. The drop now matches\\nany leading ../ prefix, so no bu"
       & "ndled page references the unbundled font\\nasset."",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.38.0 "
