       & "mbs"":""Installing adacovex "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Option 3: download a release bundle from GitHub"",""id"":""9"",""title"":""Option 3"
       & ": download a release bundle from GitHub""},""90"":{""body"":""Vendored manifest ec"
       & "osystems report their licence from the local manifest: package.json ( licens"
       & "e) for npm/pnpm, Cargo.toml for cargo, pyproject.toml / composer.json for py"
       & "pi / composer. When the local\\nmanifest carries no licence, adacovex resolv"
       & "es the version, website, and\\nlicence from the package registry as a best-e"
       & "ffort, online fallback. The\\nresolver dispatches on the ecosystem (the PURL"
       & " type) through a single static\\ntable, so adding a language is one row rath"
       & "er than a new code path: npm "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " npm view <pkg> version license homepage --json, parsed for the\\nthree fiel"
       & "ds from one JSON object. pnpm "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " pnpm show <pkg> version license homepage --json, likewise. cargo (Rust) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " cargo search <pkg>, with the SPDX id read from the (license: ...) token in "
       & "the output. go and other ecosystems with no portable, reliable registry quer"
       & "y keep\\nan empty licence; the vendored manifest scanner still reads any in-"
       & "repo\\nlicence file for them. The npm and pnpm rows answer for all three fie"
       & "lds with a single --json call,\\nso each component boots node once instead o"
       & "f once per field "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a 3x reduction\\nin subprocess starts that keeps the graph build responsive"
       & " on vendored\\nJavaScript trees. The fallback runs only when the offline rea"
       & "d finds nothing,\\nso a vendored package that ships a licence never touches "
       & "the network. The\\nresolved licence flows into every SBOM format (CycloneDX "
       & "licenses, SPDX licenseConcluded / licenseDeclared, Markdown License column) "
       & "and the\\ndashboard detail panel; the resolved version and website appear in"
       & " the\\ndashboard detail panel and the /api/deps JSON. The resolver caches ea"
       & "ch answer in a per-project store under the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s\\nresult cache (the same --cache-dir the scan uses), keyed by the target\\"
       & "ndirectory as well as the ecosystem and package name, with a 7-day TTL, the\"
       & "\nsame scheme as the system-tool version probes. The content-addressed resul"
       & "t\\ncache does not cover these registry calls (each one boots node for npm/p"
       & "npm),\\nso without this layer a warm run still re-paid them; the meta cache "
       & "makes every\\nrepeat run serve the licence, version, and website from disk w"
       & "ith no subprocess\\nspawn, and two projects that share a cache directory nev"
       & "er serve each other"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s\\nresolved licence or version. Bundled dashboard assets (FlexSearch, nomno"
       & "ml, graphre) resolve\\ntheir licence and website live from the package regis"
       & "try when a loose vendored\\ncopy is scanned, preferring pnpm show <pkg> lice"
       & "nse and falling back to npm, yarn, then bun "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the same preference chain as every JavaScript\\ncomponent (see Licence reso"
       & "lution). The SBOM and the\\nCredits tab therefore track the real upstream li"
       & "cence instead of a hard-coded\\ncopy."",""breadcrumbs"":""The sbom subcommand "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
