       & " Traceability"",""id"":""939"",""title"":""Traceability""},""94"":{""body"":""DO-178C is t"
       & "he avionics software standard. It defines how to design,\\nimplement, verify"
       & ", and certify software that flies airplanes. Every line of\\nsafety-critical"
       & " flight software is assessed at one of five DAL (Development\\nAssurance Lev"
       & "el) tiers, from DAL-E (no safety effect) to DAL-A\\n(catastrophic failure ca"
       & "n bring down the aircraft). ISO 26262 is the automotive functional-safety st"
       & "andard. It applies the same\\nrigor to road-vehicle software (braking, steer"
       & "ing, powertrain). Its integrity\\nlevels are called ASIL (Automotive Safety "
       & "Integrity Level), from QM\\n(quality management, no hazard) to ASIL D (highe"
       & "st hazard). IEC 62304 is the medical-device software lifecycle standard. It "
       & "classifies\\nsoftware into safety classes A, B, and C based on the severity "
       & "of harm a\\nfailure can cause. All three demand the same underlying evidence"
       & ": Requirement traceability "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every high-level requirement (HLR) is traced\\nby a -- HLR-XXXX tag in sour"
       & "ce. No orphan tags "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every tag in source maps to a defined HLR. Tests passing "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the test suite has zero failures (except at the lowest\\ntier). Minimum SPA"
       & "RK level "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the formal-proof bar for the selected rigor tier. adacovex computes all fou"
       & "r checks once and re-labels the result per standard.\\nThe same inputs feed "
       & "the same outputs. Only the integrity-level label changes."",""breadcrumbs"":""Co"
