       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.20.0"",""id"":""989"",""title"":""adacovex 1.20.0""},""99"":{""body"":""Each s"
       & "tandard has a dedicated level flag, so your intent is unambiguous on the\\nc"
       & "ommand line (full flag details in the CLI reference). The flags all resolve "
       & "to the same shared\\nrigor tier: Standard Flag Levels Example (tier) DO-178C"
       & " --dal= A, B, C, D, E --dal=C -> DAL-C (Major) ISO 26262 --asil= A, B, C, D,"
       & " QM --asil=B -> ASIL B (Major) IEC 62304 --class= A, B, C --class=A -> Class"
       & " A (Major) You can also use --standard=iso26262 --dal=C to get the same resu"
       & "lt as --asil=B. The dedicated flags exist so a reader of the command line ca"
       & "n see\\n"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "ASIL B"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " (or "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Class A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ") without decoding the shared tier. --standard=all runs one assessment at th"
       & "e shared tier and emits badges\\nand reports for every standard "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " do178c.svg, iso26262.svg, and iec62304.svg "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " without re-scanning, re-proving, or re-parsing anything. The\\nevidence is "
       & "identical across standards. The three badges therefore always\\nagree on Ach"
       & "ieved/Unmet. Only the level label changes."",""breadcrumbs"":""Compliance Standa"
       & "rds (DO-178C / ISO 26262 / IEC 62304) "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Selecting a standard on the CLI"",""id"":""99"",""title"":""Selecting a standard on"
       & " the CLI""},""990"":{""body"":"""",""breadcrumbs"":""Changelogs "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " adacovex 1.20.0 "
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(187)
       & " Changes"",""id"":""990"",""title"":""Changes""},""991"":{""body"":""The --serve dashboard"
       & " is now organised into clickable tabs\\n(Overview / Proof / Tests / Complian"
       & "ce / Dependencies / Charts) instead of a\\nsingle card stack. The new Depend"
       & "encies tab renders the resolved alire.toml / alire.lock graph as a collapsib"
       & "le <details> tree with\\nscope badges ( base / dev / transitive / vendored),"
       & " child counts, and a\\nclient-side name filter. The same graph is already se"
       & "rved at GET /api/deps\\nand via --emit-metrics, so the tab is a view, not a "
       & "new data source. Charts.css rendering is fixed: bar sizes are now emitted as"
       & " 0..1 fractions (not 0..100) so charts.css scales correctly, and the SPARK d"
       & "onut now shows proved vs unproved slices (previously proved vs total duplica"
       & "ted the proved arc and hid regressions). Test-category bars are normalised t"
       & "o the largest category (previously every bar was 100%). The template ( resou"
       & "rces/dashboard.html) is now a centered max-width:1180px layout with a sticky"
       & " tab bar, localStorage-persisted active tab, and hash-routing ( #deps, #proo"
       & "f, etc. compose with ? theme=). The Ada side ( Renderers. HTML) is split int"
       & "o Render_Dashboard_Internal with per-tab builders, a new Render_Deps_HTML tr"
       & "ee builder, and a Render_Charts overload that takes the graph for future sco"
