       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>run-tests</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Build the "
       & "target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s native test suite and run it (requires <code>build: true</code>; the actio"
       & "n runs <code>alr build</code> in the target root first)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>test-command</code></td><td><code>./bin/test_runner</code></td"
       & "><td>Command (relative to workspace root) that runs the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s test suite</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>release-build</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Pass <"
       & "code>--release</code> to <code>alr build</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>assess</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Run the assess"
       & "ment and publish outputs/badges (<code>false</code> for build/test-only jobs"
       & ")</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>compare-base</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Git ref to"
       & " run <code>--compare-base</code> against (fails on regression)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>coverage-delta</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Git ref "
       & "to run <code>--coverage-delta</code> against (fails if coverage dropped)</td"
       & "></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>emit-markdown</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Write <co"
       & "de>VERIFICATION.md</code> + <code>TRACE.md</code> into this directory</td></"
       & "tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>emit-metrics</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Write a JS"
       & "ON export of assessment metrics + the dependency graph to this file</td></tr"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>generate-sbom</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Generat"
       & "e a proof-aware SBOM after the assessment and upload it</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>sbom-format</code></td><td><code>cyclonedx-json</code></td><td"
       & ">SBOM format: <code>cyclonedx-json</code>, <code>spdx-json</code>, or <code>"
       & "md</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>cache</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Cache Alire too"
       & "lchain/deps with <code>actions/cache</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>result-cache</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Persist "
       & "adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s on-disk result cache across runs</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>manifest</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Override the t"
       & "arget project manifest path</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>no-svg</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Suppress SVG "
       & "badge generation</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>relaxed</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Disable stri"
       & "ct mode (skip dirs, no patches)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>skip-dir</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Directory name"
       & " to skip in relaxed mode (repeatable, comma-separated)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>verbose</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Verbose diag"
       & "nostics on stderr</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>no-cache</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Disable ada"
       & "covex on-disk result caching</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>cache-dir</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Override adac"
       & "ovex result cache directory</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>cache-max</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Max adacovex "
       & "result-cache entries before eviction</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-jobs</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>GNATprove pa"
       & "rallelism for the <code>prove</code> subcommand</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-level</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>GNATprove p"
       & "roof effort 0-4</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-timeout</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>GNATprove"
       & " per-check prover timeout in seconds</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-steps</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>GNATprove m"
       & "ax proof steps</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-memlimit</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td>GNATprov"
       & "e prover memory limit in MB</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-force</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Force fu"
       & "ll GNATprove reanalysis (<code>-f</code>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-no-loop-unrolling</code></td><td><code>false</code></td>"
       & "<td>Disable GNATprove automatic loop unrolling</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-no-inlining</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Di"
       & "sable GNATprove contextual-analysis inlining</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-quiet</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Suppress"
       & " GNATprove benign info messages (the default set) from prove output. Quiet i"
       & "s already the default for local runs; this is the explicit prove-mode form. "
       & "<code>--verbose</code> wins</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>prove-suppress-warnings</code></td><td><code>''</code></td><td"
       & ">Comma-separated GNATprove info tags to suppress from prove output (for exam"
       & "ple <code>unrolling-inlining,xyz</code>); a tag <code>S</code> suppresses bl"
       & "ocks tagged <code>[info-S]</code> (or <code>[S]</code>). <code>--verbose</co"
       & "de> wins</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""outputs""><a class=""header"" href=""#outputs"">Outputs</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Output</th><th>Description</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>dal-status</code></td><td><code>Achieved</code> or <code>Unmet"
       & "</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>spark-level</code></td><td>SPARK level detected (Stone..Platin"
       & "um)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>test-count</code></td><td>Number of passing tests</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>coverage-pct</code></td><td>Current docstring coverage (in <co"
       & "de>--coverage-delta</code> mode)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""result-caching""><a class=""header"" href=""#result-caching"">Result cach"
       & "ing</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The action restores <code>~/.adacovex/cache</code> before running adacove"
       & "x. It saves the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cache when the job finishes (<code>result-cache</code>, default <code>true</"
       & "code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every entry is keyed by its artifact"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s SHA-256 content hash. Restoring a cache"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from an earlier run or commit is always safe. Only files that are byte-for-b"
       & "yte"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unchanged are served from it. The remaining files are rescanned and re-parse"
       & "d"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "automatically.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""workflows""><a class=""header"" href=""#workflows"">Workflows</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code></strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " three jobs on push to <code>main</code> and pull"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "requests:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>self-assessment</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " build + prove + assess at <code>--standard=all</code> (so the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "DO-178C, ISO 26262, and IEC 62304 badges/reports are all emitted and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gated), with the Platinum / 100% docstrings / test-count / 100% proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "thresholds.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>adacovex-tests</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " build + native test suite (<code>run-tests</code>, <code>assess: false</cod"
       & "e>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>coverage-gate</code> (push only) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " runs the coverage gate, comparing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "docstring coverage between the latest two release tags (a maintainer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "step; see the <a href=""../contributing/developer-guide.html"">developer guide"
       & "</a>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>.github/workflows/pr-check.yml</code></strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " runs <code>--coverage-delta</code> against"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>pull_request.base.sha</code> to fail PRs that drop docstring coverage."
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong><code>.github/workflows/release.yml</code></strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " on a <code>v*</code> tag, builds the release"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "binary, runs GNATprove, validates the <code>--standard=all</code> self-asses"
       & "sment, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "publishes the GitHub Release (see <a href=""#release-bundling"">Release bundli"
       & "ng</a>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""markdown-summaries-and-loud-failures""><a class=""header"" href=""#markd"
       & "own-summaries-and-loud-failures"">Markdown summaries and loud failures</a></h"
       & "3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every CI run leaves a <strong>Markdown summary at the bottom of the job p"
       & "age</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code>):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The composite action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s assessment step writes an <code>## adacovex assessment</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table. The table shows target, bundled version, compliance label, SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "level, tests, and coverage. It also writes the full raw output.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>An <code>if: always()</code> <strong>Write run summary</strong> step app"
       & "ends a run-overview table."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The table shows version, target, standard, DAL, and job result.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Each workflow adds a <strong><code>summary</code> job</strong> (<code>if"
       & ": always()</code>, <code>needs:</code> all other"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "jobs) that aggregates every job result into one table at the bottom of the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Diagnostics are layered so a failure is debuggable from the Actions UI wi"
       & "thout"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "re-running locally:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The assessment output is folded into a GitHub <strong>log group</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>::group::</code>). The step result stays visible. The detail stays on"
       & "e click"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "away.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>WARNING</code> lines are re-surfaced as <code>::notice::</code> an"
       & "notations.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>An <strong><code>adacovex-assessment</code> artifact</strong> (uploaded "
       & "<code>if: always()</code>) carries the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "full, untruncated assessment output. It also carries the <code>--emit-metric"
       & "s</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JSON export when <code>emit-metrics</code> is set. A flaky or unmet gate nev"
       & "er requires"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a re-run to reproduce.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Badge and SBOM artifacts are uploaded even when the step failed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>if: always()</code>). Partially produced reports stay inspectable.</l"
       & "i>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Threshold failures <strong>fail loudly</strong> at every layer:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>Unmet <code>--require-*</code> gates make the adacovex binary exit non-z"
       & "ero.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The assessment step re-surfaces each <code>CI GATE:</code> line as a Git"
       & "Hub"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>::error::</code> annotation. The annotation is visible at the top of t"
       & "he job"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "page, not just in the log. The step marks the summary table <strong>FAILED</"
       & "strong> with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the unmet gates.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>Write run summary</code> step (runs on failure too) reports the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "failed job result.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The workflow <code>summary</code> job exits <code>1</code> when any depe"
       & "ndency failed. The whole"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run is red even if the failing job was retried. An <code>if: always()</code>"
       & " cleanup"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "step does not mask this.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""debugging-guide-what-to-do-when-you-see-""><a class=""header"" href=""#d"
       & "ebugging-guide-what-to-do-when-you-see-"">Debugging guide: what to do when yo"
       & "u see "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(166)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><th>Output</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Action</th></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>CI GATE: SPARK level X below required Y (--require-spark)</cod"
       & "e></td><td>Proven VCs or <code>gnatprove</code> version drift below the pinn"
       & "ed gate</td><td>Check the <code>gnatprove</code> pin or the <code>gnat-versi"
       & "on</code> input. Re-run <code>adacovex prove</code>. Update <code>--require-"
       & "spark</code> only if the prover legitimately tightened</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>CI GATE: docstring coverage N% below required M% (--require-do"
       & "cstrings)</code></td><td>Missing <code>--</code> docstrings or patches</td><"
       & "td>Run <code>adacovex --verbose</code> to list undocumented subprogs. Add pa"
       & "tches under <code>.adacovex/patches/</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>CI GATE: proved-VC coverage N% below required M% (--require-pr"
       & "oof)</code></td><td>Some VCs unproved/justified</td><td>Inspect <code>gnatpr"
       & "ove.out</code>. Add contracts or fix <code>SPARK_Mode</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>Warning: N source file(s) skipped: line exceeds Max_Line</code"
       & "></td><td>A physical line &gt; <code>Max_Line</code> (262144 on 64-bit)</td>"
       & "<td>Split the declaration. DAL becomes <code>Unmet</code> by design (<code>d"
       & "ocs/architecture.md#overflow-contract</code>)</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>result cache: X hit(s), Y miss(es), Z evicted</code></td><td>C"
       & "ache stats per run</td><td><code>Z&gt;0</code> means <code>--cache-max</code"
       & "> evicted the oldest entries. Increase <code>--cache-max</code>. Pass <code>"
       & "--no-cache</code> to force a full rescan</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>Unknown option --foo (did you mean --bar?)</code></td><td>Typo"
       & "</td><td>Use <code>adacovex --help</code> or <code>adacovex help &lt;topic&g"
       & "t;</code></td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>::notice::WARNING ...</code> annotation</td><td>Non-fatal warn"
       & "ing surfaced from <code>adacovex.out</code></td><td>Download the <code>adaco"
       & "vex-assessment</code> artifact for the full log. Warnings do not fail the ga"
       & "te. They indicate missing tests or proof</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr><td><code>complexity-check</code> failed</td><td>File or function exceed"
       & "s caps (<code>--max-file-loc</code>/<code>--max-file-pct</code>/<code>--max-"
       & "fn-complexity</code>)</td><td>Run <code>adacovex complexity --help</code>. S"
       & "plit god objects or functions</td></tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Better debugging output contract.</strong> <code>ci.yml</code> no"
       & "w has <code>timeout-minutes</code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>concurrency.cancel-in-progress</code>, <code>fetch-tags: true</code>, "
       & "and <code>actions/cache</code> for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "both toolchain and result-cache. After these brittleness fixes, every failur"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "leaves three things without a re-run:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The <code>::error</code>/<code>::notice</code> annotations at the top of"
       & " the job page.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The <code>## adacovex assessment</code> Markdown table in <code>GITHUB_S"
       & "TEP_SUMMARY</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>The <code>adacovex-assessment</code> artifact (full untruncated <code>ad"
       & "acovex.out</code> +"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>adacovex-metrics.json</code> when <code>emit-metrics</code> is set).</"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When the gate is flaky, start from the artifact, not a local repro.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""release-version-bundling""><a class=""header"" href=""#release-version-b"
       & "undling"">Release version bundling</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The release workflow builds the binary from the <code>vX. Y. Z</code> tag"
       & ". It <strong>bundles that version into the binary</strong>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s build step sets <code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code> (from <code>github.ref_name<"
       & "/code>). It regenerates <code>src/adacovex_version_info.ads</code> before <c"
       & "ode>alr build</code>. The shipped <code>adacovex --version</code> reports ex"
       & "actly the tag.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The download step of the published action verifies this with <code>adacov"
       & "ex --version</code> after unpacking the release bundle. Maintainers reproduc"
       & "e the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release locally with <code>make release VERSION=x.y.z</code> (see the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""../contributing/developer-guide.html"">developer guide</a>); a norma"
       & "l source build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reads the version from <code>alire-dev.toml</code> instead.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3 id=""pr-coverage-gate-1""><a class=""header"" href=""#pr-coverage-gate-1"">PR "
       & "coverage gate</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Gate every pull request so docstring coverage does not regress against th"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "base branch. This is exactly what <code>--coverage-delta</code> was built fo"
       & "r:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-yaml""># .github/workflows/pr-check.yml"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "on:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  pull_request:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "jobs:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  coverage-delta:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "    runs-on: ubuntu-latest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "    steps:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      - uses: actions/checkout@v7"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "        with:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          fetch-depth: 0"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      - uses: bladeacer/adacovex@v1"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "        with:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          target: ."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          standard: all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          coverage-delta: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The action exits non-zero when coverage drops, failing the check. This"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "workflow ships in the repo at <code>.github/workflows/pr-check.yml</code>.</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""release-bundling""><a class=""header"" href=""#release-bundling"">Release"
       & " bundling</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every <code>vX. Y. Z</code> tag triggers <code>.github/workflows/release."
       & "yml</code>. The workflow calls the composite action with <code>build</code>,"
       & " <code>release-build</code>, and <code>prove</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It builds the release binary, runs GNATprove, and validates the self-asse"
       & "ssment. Then it packages and publishes:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>adacovex-vX.Y.Z.tar.gz</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the version-matched binary (<code>adacovex</code> plus the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>covex</code> alias). The action downloads this asset for the tag it is"
       & " referenced"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by, so <code>@v1.9.0</code> runs adacovex <code>v1.9.0</code>.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>adacovex-action-vX.Y.Z.tar.gz</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a copy of the composite action itself for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendoring or air-gapped use.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Both bundles are attested with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""https://github.com/actions/attest""><code>actions/attest</code></a>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "on every tag. OIDC attestations appear under the release"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s attestations tab."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The release notes link the signed attestation via the action"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>attestation-url</code> output. They also link a <em>Git Changelog</em>"
       & " compare link"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>compare/v1.9.0...v1.14.0</code>) and the human-readable changelogs.</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Changelog listing.</strong> The <code>Create GitHub Release</code"
       & "> step derives the changelog"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "list from the available <code>docs/changelogs/adacovex-*.md</code> entries. "
       & "The entries"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are between the previous release tag and the released version.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It resolves the previous three-component release tag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>git tag --sort=-version:refname</code>, for example <code>v1.9.0</cod"
       & "e> when releasing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>v1.14.0</code>). Then it lists every changelog whose version is strict"
       & "ly above the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "previous release and at or below the released version. Releasing <code>v1.14"
       & ".0</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "after <code>v1.9.0</code> links the <code>1.10.0</code>..<code>1.14.0</code>"
       & " changelogs in one release.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The list is emitted <strong>newest-first</strong> (version-sorted, not sh"
       & "ell glob order)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The entries read <code>1.14.0</code> down to <code>1.10.0</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The list is derived from the changelog files present in the tree, not fro"
       & "m"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tags. A version that was never released has no entry. A release that skips"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "versions still links every changelog in the range. Each entry links the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "release"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s changelog page on the deployed <strong>Read the Docs</strong> site"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>https://adacovex.readthedocs.io/en/latest/changelogs/adacovex-&lt;v&g"
       & "t;.html</code>),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "not a GitHub blob URL: the manual is an mdBook project and the changelogs ar"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "part of the published book.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>The CI release binary is Linux x86-64 only for now.</strong> The "
       & "release workflow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "runs on <code>ubuntu-latest</code>. It packages the Linux binary and the pre"
       & "built"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GNATprove toolchain bundle for that target. macOS, FreeBSD, Windows, and Lin"
       & "ux"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "aarch64 build adacovex from source via Alire instead. See"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""platforms.html#release-binaries"">Platforms</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Maintainers reproduce the release locally with <code>make release VERSION"
       & "=x.y.z</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(see the <a href=""../contributing/developer-guide.html"">developer guide</a>)"
       & ": it builds"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>--release</code>, generates proofs, validates DAL-C, and bundles <code"
       & ">dist/</code>, then"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tags and pushes to trigger the workflow. The bundled version is always the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s version (<code>src/adacovex_version_info.ads</code> comes from <code>alire"
       & "-dev.toml</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or <code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code> at build time).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""floating-tags""><a class=""header"" href=""#floating-tags"">Floating tags"
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The release workflow force-pushes the floating tags <code>vMAJOR</code>, "
       & "<code>vMAJOR. MINOR</code>, and <code>latest</code>. For example: <code>v1</"
       & "code>, <code>v1.3</code>, and <code>latest</code> from <code>v1.3.0</code>. "
       & "Reference <code>@latest</code> to always get the newest published release.</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Use <code>@v1</code> or <code>@v1.3</code> for the latest release within "
       & "a major or minor version. Pin an exact <code>@vX. Y. Z</code> for a fixed ve"
       & "rsion.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Once the action is listed on the GitHub Actions marketplace, each <code>v"
       & "X. Y. Z</code> tag auto-publishes that version.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""consumer-manifest-prerequisites-avoid-a-broken-ci""><a class=""header"""
       & " href=""#consumer-manifest-prerequisites-avoid-a-broken-ci"">Consumer manifest"
       & " prerequisites (avoid a broken CI)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>prove</code> subcommand and the GitHub Action resolve <code>gnatprov"
       & "e</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through the <em>target project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s</em> manifest. The pinned gnatprove crate is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "deployed via <code>alr -n get gnatprove=&lt;version&gt;</code>. It is run di"
       & "rectly, with no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alr exec</code> over the whole workspace.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For the command to succeed in a clean checkout or on CI, the consumer"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifests must follow two rules:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong><code>alire.toml</code> must be the clean publishing manifest.</s"
       & "trong> It must contain no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dev tooling (<code>gnatprove</code>, <code>gnatdoc_bin</code>, <code>gnatfor"
       & "mat_bin</code>, <code>covex</code>). It must"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contain <strong>no <code>[[pins]]</code></strong>. Alire reads this manifest"
       & " when the action runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alr build</code>. It must resolve with nothing but Alire + GNAT.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong><code>alire-dev.toml</code> must declare <code>covex</code> as a "
       & "normal index dependency</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>covex = ""*""</code>). It must never be pinned to a local path such as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>covex = { path = ""../adacovex"" }</code>. A path pin resolves only on t"
       & "he machine"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that has the sibling checkout. In a consumer workspace or on CI, Alire"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fails the whole workspace load with a confusing error. This happens before"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex or <code>alr</code> runs:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code>ERROR: Failed to load alire.toml:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ERROR:    pins:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ERROR:    covex:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ERROR:    Pin path is not a valid directory: /home/runner/work/&lt;repo&gt;/"
       & "&lt;repo&gt;/../adacovex"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>If you see that, drop the <code>covex</code> path pin. Use <code>covex = "
       & """*""</code>. Strip the dev"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "deps and pins out of <code>alire.toml</code>. Keep them only in <code>alire-"
       & "dev.toml</code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Makefile pattern in many projects keeps the published <code>alire.tom"
       & "l</code> clean."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "It swaps <code>alire-dev.toml</code> over <code>alire.toml</code> only for t"
       & "he duration of a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>prove</code>/<code>fmt</code>/<code>doc</code> target, then restores i"
       & "t. This gives local tooling the dev"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "deps.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
