       & "                    <main>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                        <h1 id=""installing-adacovex""><a class=""header"" href="
       & """#installing-adacovex"">Installing adacovex</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""quick-start""><a class=""header"" href=""#quick-start"">Quick start</a></"
       & "h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Install</strong> via Alire: <code>alr install covex gnatprove &a"
       & "mp;&amp; export PATH=""$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH""</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Assess</strong> your project: <code>adacovex --target=. --dal=C<"
       & "/code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><strong>Serve</strong> the dashboard: <code>adacovex --target=. --serve "
       & "--port=8080</code></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>That is all you need for a local compliance assessment. For CI or release"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "workflows, see <a href=""ci-cd.html"">CI/CD</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex is distributed as the <code>covex</code> Alire crate, a release "
       & "bundle on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GitHub, or a source build. All three routes produce the same binary"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code>adacovex</code>, with a <code>covex</code> alias on Linux).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""option-1-declare-it-in-your-projects-alire-manifest-recommended""><a "
       & "class=""header"" href=""#option-1-declare-it-in-your-projects-alire-manifest-re"
       & "commended"">Option 1: declare it in your project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Alire manifest (recommended)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Put <code>covex</code> in your project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code>alire-dev.toml</code> (never <code>alire.toml</code>, so release"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "builds stay clean), alongside <code>gnatprove</code>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-toml""># &lt;project&gt;/alire-dev.toml"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "[[depends-on]]"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "covex = ""*"""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove = ""^16.1.0"""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Then <code>alr build</code> produces <code>bin/adacovex</code> inside the"
       & " project. <code>covex prove</code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "deploys the pinned gnatprove crate standalone via <code>alr -n get</code> an"
       & "d runs it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directly. Each project pins its own exact toolchain version. No global insta"
       & "ll"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is needed:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">alr build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "./bin/adacovex --target=. --dal=C"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "./bin/adacovex prove --target=.   # deploys gnatprove via alr get, then runs"
       & " it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""option-2-alr-install-global-to-path""><a class=""header"" href=""#option"
       & "-2-alr-install-global-to-path"">Option 2: <code>alr install</code> (global, t"
       & "o <code>$PATH</code>)</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">alr install covex gnatprove"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "export PATH=""$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>covex</code> is the Alire crate name for adacovex"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<a href=""https://alire.ada.dev/crates/covex"">crate page</a>). Once on <code"
       & ">$PATH</code>, it scans"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the current directory by default. A <code>gnatprove</code> installed this wa"
       & "y is picked up"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from <code>$PATH</code> by <code>covex prove</code> when the target project "
       & "declares no manifest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dependency of its own.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""option-3-download-a-release-bundle-from-github""><a class=""header"" hr"
       & "ef=""#option-3-download-a-release-bundle-from-github"">Option 3: download a re"
       & "lease bundle from GitHub</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every <code>vX. Y. Z</code> tag publishes `adacovex-vX. Y.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Z.tar.gz` on the <a href=""https://github.com/bladeacer/adacovex/releases"""
       & ">GitHub Releases page</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.co"
       & "m/bladeacer/adacovex/main/install.sh | bash"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Bundles are attested with <a href=""https://github.com/actions/attest""><co"
       & "de>actions/attest</code></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Release binaries are <strong>Linux x86-64 only</strong>. Other platforms "
       & "build from source"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "via Alire (see <a href=""platforms.html"">Platforms</a>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""building-from-source""><a class=""header"" href=""#building-from-source"""
       & ">Building from source</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<pre><code class=""language-bash"">git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/blad"
       & "eacer/adacovex.git"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cd adacovex &amp;&amp; alr build   # or: --branch vX.Y.Z for a released tag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</code></pre>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>alr build</code> produces <code>bin/adacovex</code> (with a <code>b"
       & "in/covex</code> alias). A stock Alire"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "toolchain (<code>gnat_native</code> + <code>gprbuild</code>) plus the standa"
       & "rd GNAT runtime is all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that is needed. No other dependencies. (Contributors use the richer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>make build</code> workflow; see the <a href=""../contributing/developer"
       & "-guide.html"">developer guide</a>.)</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""version-source-per-installation-method""><a class=""header"" href=""#ver"
       & "sion-source-per-installation-method"">Version source per installation method<"
       & "/a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex --version</code> (and the man page, the SBOM tool version,"
       & " and the result"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cache namespace) resolve the version from <code>tools/gen-version.py</code>."
       & " The version"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "depends on the installation method:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>ADACOVEX_VERSION</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " release builds (the shipped binary always reports the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tag it was built from).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>alire/alire-dev.toml</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " source checkouts (<code>version = ""x.y.z""</code>).</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><code>alire.toml</code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " dependency-managed installs: the toml associated with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>covex</code> binary for dependency management carries the release vers"
       & "ion.</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""keeping-the-man-page-in-sync""><a class=""header"" href=""#keeping-the-m"
       & "an-page-in-sync"">Keeping the man page in sync</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code>adacovex man</code> installs the man page (which embeds the version"
       & ") into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>~/.local/share/man</code>. It refreshes <code>mandb</code> when presen"
       & "t. <code>adacovex man --check</code> exits 0 when the installed page matches"
       & " the binary. A shell prompt"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hook can auto-update. <code>man --force</code> overwrites an up-to-date page"
       & " (for example"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to repair a hand-edited one).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When man-db is missing, the page still installs. Read it with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>man -l ~/.local/share/man/man1/adacovex.1</code>. <code>adacovex statu"
       & "s</code> reports mandb"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "availability up front. See <a href=""platforms.html#local-man-page-linuxwsl"">"
       & "Platforms "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " local man page</a>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for the install roots and man-db behaviour.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "                    </main>"
