       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""non-ada-projects""><a class=""header"" href=""#non-ada-projects"">Non-Ada"
       & " projects</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex currently targets Ada/SPARK sources. Non-Ada projects (C/C++, Py"
       & "thon,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JS, and more) that want the compliance/SBOM tooling provide their own"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>alire.toml</code> / <code>alire-dev.toml</code> to manage the Ada depe"
       & "ndencies needed to build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex itself. Running <code>adacovex</code> from such a repo scans it and"
       & " uses its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>We are working on support for other languages. Watch for updates.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2 id=""vendored-code-and-strict-mode""><a class=""header"" href=""#vendored-cod"
       & "e-and-strict-mode"">Vendored code and strict mode</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>By default (strict mode) adacovex scans and counts every directory except"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "always-excluded ones. Vendored code is included. For third-party code you"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot modify, use docstring <strong>patch files</strong> at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code>&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/patches/&lt;relative-path&gt;</code> (see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""../contributing/architecture.html#patch-system"">Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Patch System</a>). Or run in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "relaxed mode (<code>--relaxed</code>, skip dirs, no patches) (see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a href=""cli-reference.html#strict-vs-relaxed-mode"">Strict vs relaxed mode</"
       & "a>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Vendored code can also take part in the <strong>SPARK proof</strong>. A p"
       & "atch carrying <code>SPARK_Mode</code> / <code>Pre</code> / <code>Post</code>"
       & " / <code>Global</code> aspects is a <em>proof patch</em>. The <code>prove</c"
       & "ode> subcommand merges it into a patched tree copy. The copy uses <code>.ads"
       & "</code> spec contracts and <code>.adb</code> body patches that opt a SPARK-c"
       & "lean vendored body into the proof.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <a href=""../contributing/proving.html#proof-patches-proving-vendored-"
       & "dependencies"">Proving and writing proofs</a> for how to write them. See <a h"
